\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10800\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  Compares E.V. Skeptics To Landline Lovers; \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  Tanking In Swing State Polls Against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ; Just Say No: Oregon Recriminalizes Drugs After Policy Caused Chaos; $20 Minimum Wage Chaos! California Law Causing Layoffs, Confusion, Price Hikes; Ghosted By Gen Z: Young Workers Not Showing Up For Job Interview\b0\par\par\uc2 Jeanine Pirro, Jessica Tarlov, Jesse Watters, Dana Perino, Greg  Gutfeld \par \uc2 7,942 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 April 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Five\par \uc2 FOXFIV\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 ANDY TILLETT, NEW YORK POST NATIONAL EDITOR: McDonald's and \uc2 Burger King\uc2  and various fast food locations.\par \par \uc2 SANDRA SMITH, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Incredible. It was great to see you, great to chat with you, and good stuff from the New York post. Thanks for joining us.\par \par \uc2 Neil will be back tomorrow. And you can catch me tomorrow alongside John Roberts 1:00 p.m. Eastern Time on "AMERICA REPORTS". For now, here is THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Hello, everyone, I'm Judge Jeanine Pirro along with Jessica Tarlov, Jesse Watters, Dana Perino and Greg Gutfeld. It's 5:00 in New York City and this is THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is now openly mocking Americans who aren't buying into their electric car scam. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's fantasy of replacing your gas guzzler with an E.V. is short-circuiting. Sales are nowhere near what the administration promised and most people don't have the green to go green.\par \par \uc2 But America's hard hat-wearing transportation secretary is keeping the faith. \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  is dismissing anyone not on board with the E.V. revolution as some kind of tech Neanderthal.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PETE BUTTIGIEG, TRANSPORTATION SECRETARY: Let's be clear that the automotive sector is moving toward E.V.s, and we can't pretend otherwise. Sometimes when these debates happen, I feel like it's the early 2000s and I'm talking to some people who think that we can just have landline phones forever.\par \par \uc2 The reality is that the automotive sector is moving toward E.V.s and the U.S. can either fall behind China, or we can claim the lead. President Biden wants to make sure that those E.V.s are made in America.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Buttigieg going on to brag about his at home charger, which is a luxury that he is afforded, but not for the rest of us. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has spent $7 billion of your tax money and has produced only seven stations in two years.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BUTTIGIEG: There are more ways to move electricity than there are to move electric -- than there are to move liquid fuel. You know, that's why my house in Michigan, I control our hybrid plug in electric with electricity. Obviously, I can't do that with gas at my house.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Truckers are bashing Biden's E.V. push in their industry, saying, electric big rigs are a pipe dream. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LEWIE PUGH, INDEPENDENT DRIVERS ASSOCIATION EVP: There was a company in Joliet, Illinois, that was going to put a terminal in for 30 trucks. The city said, 'you can't do it, you're going to use more electricity than the entire city at Joliet, Illinois.\par \par \uc2 ALEX "THE TRUCKING GUY", TRUCKER AND TIKTOKER: Our newer trucks will have to have a longer than usual warranty. They're going to add that in into the pricing of the trucks, which, for smaller trucking companies, they're not going to be able to afford it. And so, they're just going to have to extend the life of their old trucks and come less efficient, and it ends up creating more pollution.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: All right, Jesse, you know, it seems the administration is in a big rush for this when the infrastructure is not only not ready for the charging stations. But it appears that our electric grid is balkanized and is as old as it is isn't going to be able to sustain these electric charges.\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: No, it's not. My dad sent me one of those funny old man videos from the internet. That's like, what's the difference between a liberal and a conservative and it starts out well, conservative doesn't like to eat meat. He's a vegan, that's fine. The liberal doesn't like to eat meat. He tries to ban meat everywhere. Say Liberal, doesn't like a talk show, Conservative just changed the channel, the liberal ban the talk show.\par \par \uc2 Republican doesn't have health care, maybe he's down on his luck. They see what they can do to improve their life. The liberal, give me stuff, free health care, welfare, make my life better. It's about personal responsibility. We live our own life. We make our own decisions, we're accountable.\par \par \uc2 And the liberals just want to get everybody in society involved in their business and I've had it. Just because something is new, Jessica, doesn't make it better. I know a man who only drinks liquids that had been around for a thousand years. Only drinks tea, wine and water.\par \par \uc2 Should he drink a Gatorade because it's new, because it has electrolytes, Jessica? Of course not. Something that is new, doesn't mean it's progress.\par \par \uc2 Things that have been around for thousands of years are actually pretty good. Look at the architecture. You see around these great buildings. Some of them look like they were just put up a couple of years ago, and they look like vomit.\par \par \uc2 How about fashion? Ever seen men's fashion these days? It's ridiculous. Go back to 1820 in Great Britain, everyone looked like a stud. Do you think it's better to read a book? Or do you think it's better to stare at the stupid screen all day? It's better to read a book.\par \par \uc2 Did you know this, Jessica? That an electric car is twice as heavy as a regular car? So, we're going to double the weight on all the parking garages, the roads and bridges. You think, last bridge that collapsed is going to be a onetime thing? Everything's going to collapse.\par \par \uc2 You're doubling -- you're doubling the size and the weight of everything that's on the road. What do you think's going to happen to the road? Mayor Pete couldn't even fix a pothole, there's going to be thousands of potholes all over the country. This is what we have to face.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Thank you, Jesse.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You're welcome.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Do you want to respond, Jessica?\par \par \uc2 JESSICA TARLOV, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: It was such a rich diatribe, so much in there. I would be fine if most men dressed like upper-class Brits from the 1820s. But there were a lot of people not looking so hot in 1820 as well, as fashion, but also the infrastructure. Well, we know the Biden administration cares about that.\par \par \uc2 What else did you have thrown in there? Oh, the person who only drinks wine, tea and would never touch a Gatorade.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: My point is that --\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I know what your point was.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Progress doesn't necessarily mean a new thing is better.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Well, no, sometimes there are things that are invented that are terrible. But there are other things that are amazing. And we should have a conversation about how you consume things. Because you say you're happy to give this up. So, you just sit there with your big book. But I don't think that that's really true.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Didn't say I'd give it up.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: But you said it was better.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Anywho, this is one of those issues where the administration does have a good answer that they could go towards, which is hybrids, and everyone agrees about that.\par \par \uc2 So, Mayor Pete is -- Secretary Pete, I'm sorry, Mayor Pete is just so much cuter. They know that the car companies because all the CEOs have come out and said we're not going to be able to make these targets. It is our aspirations to be able to cut down on emissions. But the infrastructure doesn't work for this. And we don't know the appetite and they're too expensive for people.\par \par \uc2 And most people are driving electric vehicles are driving Teslas and we know that Teslas are very expensive comparatively. So, the hybrid route seems like the right way forward. And I think that's what they should be emphasizing. And the CEOs of these companies would also be happy.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You know, what's interesting, Greg, is that the E.V.s are slowing down in terms of people's appetite to have them, even \uc2 Tesla\uc2  has suffered a slowdown to in terms of purchases. So, what is -- what is Buttigieg talking about when he says we don't want to fall behind China? Aren't we buying all the batteries from China to begin with?\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Yes, I just have to say, I just know Jesse too well now. You sat down, you're going, I can't believe we have to talk about this. And so, you just decided to completely derail the entire segment with 2.5 minutes of magical, nonsense.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Magical. Emphasis on the magical.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: It was magical. I think that there's a problem there, but Buttigieg should concentrate on the more urgent issues that we are facing in the world of transportation. We have bridges collapsing, ships crashing into bridges, trains derailing, planes losing doors, people sleeping at airports. This shows you when you listen to them that sooner or later luxury beliefs will drain you of the energy that's necessary to actually deal with substantial problems in the present day in reality.\par \par \uc2 You know, remember, why all these things are going wrong, this guy was preoccupied with how racist the roads were in the past. And there's something else in his comparison to landlines, no one advocated for bans for landlines like they're doing with gas cars. We didn't demonize people for having landlines. We didn't say you have blood on your hands, grandma, for still using your landline. And we didn't -- we didn't push our argument based on faulty science and faulty statistics that are all coming apart now. Landline and landliners weren't pressured, or vandalized