2 GUTFELD: This is -- yes, that is wrong and I'm a deeply ashamed to be an alumnus of Cal Berkeley 19 -- just 2005 I graduated.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Minimum wage jobs are not designed to make a living. You aren't supposed to live comfortably on a minimum-wage job. A minimum wage job was intended as the first rung of the employment ladder. You get started with some work experience, you get some money in your pocket to get -- put gas in the car and take Betsy Sue to the old drive-in and maybe get her some flowers and, you know, maybe have some money left over for a dime bag of candy.\par \par \uc2 But now, those are the people that are going to lose their jobs because you can't raise minimum wage without raising all the wages above it. An assistant manager who made $20.00 now is going to have to make $25.00 or $30.00 and so on. So, you either slice off the bottom of the ladder or you slice off the top of the ladder. Either way, you get a tiny little step ladder which Dana has.\par \par \uc2 So, if minimum wage was $7.00, that's $56.00 bucks a day. If it's $10.00, it's $80.00 bucks a day. For a high school kid, that's good money. For a retiree, it's good for cigars and beer. But for a dad with a family, it's absurd. So, it's not about the wage, it's the mismatching of worker to wage by so-called economists.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: So-called economists indeed. Judge, what do you think of all of this?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well, I think it's -- I think it's the unions that were able to get the passage of the bill. I think that ultimately it hurts everybody. It hurts the workers who are going to lose their jobs because they can't afford to keep that many at $20.00 an hour. It also hurts the consumers when you talked about the prices going up. And there's going to be lawsuits because nobody knows who's included. There's a lot of confusion here.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Jessica?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: The confusion part is real and I'm sure that that's a terrible place for the workers and the owners of these franchises to be in where they don't know what's going to happen tomorrow. I will say though, the minimum wage has been steadily increasing in California since 2015, so this jump is not a substantial -- it's not like they were earning $8.00 and suddenly they're earning $20.00. I think it was about $16.50.\par \par \uc2 But you have to ask yourself the question -- well, two questions. One to Greg's point, do we want a society of 25-year-olds and up that are working these jobs? What can we do -- be doing better to get them trained up to do something else or to become franchise owners? Those are always the best stories, right? Someone who worked at a McDonald's from 17 and ends up owning one.\par \par \uc2 But if you're looking at this for people who are earning it and need to support a family, it seems actually like a pretty good deal. The average increase in price is not the 12 percent from \uc2 Burger King\uc2  but around five percent, but people are getting sometimes up to a 20 percent wage bump which they need to be able to support their families. And I think that's where people who are advocating from this are coming from.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: But that won't help them, Jesse, if the business owner decides to leave.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes, Dana. Talk about common sense. Here's a Democrat. Ready? I'll pretend I'm a Democrat.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Got it.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Hey, let's build a bridge out of spaghetti. It'll be great. We'll save money on construction costs and then we'll just pay the workers $1,000 an hour. Well, does the bridge work? It doesn't matter. An economist says the bridge will be fine. If you just build it like this, you just slide everybody down. And at the end of the bridge, there's a bowl of soup.\par \par \uc2 Everybody says that's not going to work. And the Democrat is like, no, we're going to do it. We're going to make it work. And everyone is like, I'm -- I swear to God it's not going to work. And they start building this bridge out of spaghetti, and everybody gets tangled up. I'm sure it tastes great while you're driving over it.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: And you got fat though, right?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Spaghetti makes you fat?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Carbs.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Carbs don't make you fat.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: What?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: That's another hoax, Jessica. The fine people, dictator on day one, and carbs.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Oh, OK.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK, yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I love this show. Coming up, the latest taking trend at your workplace.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Gen Z now treating employers as if they were on a bad date. 93 percent of the young workers admit to not showing up for an interview and 87 percent couldn't even be bothered to grace the office with their presence on day one of the job. Greg?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: These are employment heroes. Can I tell you how many people that I've hired I wish had had the guts and poor thoughts not to have shown up? It would have saved me so much time and suffering. You think it's hard to hire? It's way harder to fire. And the hardest people to fire are the incompetence because they figure out how to game the system, and they're so bad you just avoid them.\par \par \uc2 Why do you think Kilmeade is on "FOX AND FRIENDS" for 24 years?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: That was a mean one. Dana, what you got?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I am wondering if Generation X really screwed up raising these kids because this is not -- there's just like -- they can't even order at restaurants. This is -- it's a -- it's a problem. I'm just -- I'm going to blame Generation X and watch my mentions go crazy.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Judge?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I don't -- I don't know whether or not I should say what I'm thinking so I'm not going to.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh, yes, definitely do it though.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Do it. Do it. Do it.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Hold her hands.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Are they stupid? I mean, I don't get it. They -- first of all, they can't get anything accomplished. You say to someone in the store, a young person, do you have this? Yes, it's over there. Where? I don't know. It's over there. Show me. And they're looking at their phone while they're talking to you. It's like they're doing you a favor. And then I feel like the bad guy because I want to give this place my money. I'm done with them.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Let me give you my money. I always think Jessica when you're going to an interview, they're not interviewing you, you're interviewing them. That's how I approach interviews. I'm interviewing -- is this place going to be a good place for me to work? What kind of people do they have here? What is this interviewer all about? Maybe I don't like this guy. Maybe I do. But you need that face-to-face to determine whether or not you're going to shake them down and never get fired because you're a DEI hire like Kilmeade.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh, my God.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: "ONE MORE THING" is up next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: It's time now for "ONE MORE THING," and they say I go because I didn't go yesterday, Greg. Sometimes you have to take matters into your own hand. Check out this preschooler who was determined to make a shot. The young boy traveled up and down and up and down the court without dribbling once for over a minute straight, ignoring his teammates' please to pass the ball.\par \par \uc2 He goes back and forth. He goes we're not going to do it for the whole minute. But I love this kid. Look at this. He's doing a dance now. You know, he never gives up the ball except there. Go ahead, Jesse.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: That's pretty funny. All right, the Fox News shop has slashed prices. Thank you, Bidenomics. We are here now, beautiful tote bag. You can take this to the beach with your family. You could take it to the airport. You could take it anywhere. You can put Dana in it. This thing is great, very fashionable. Go to shop.foxnews.com to browse.\par \par \uc2 And tonight, "JESSE WATTERS PRIMETIME," the Diddy \uc2 Maxine Waters\uc2  connection. No relation.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Love it. Greg.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: No relation.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Tonight, I have Matt Whitaker, Jamie Lissow, Kat Timpf, and Tyrus. That's tonight at 10:00 p.m. Watch it.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: That's it?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: That's it.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK. That's it for us, everybody. I hope you enjoyed the show. We have another six seconds. Do you want to say anything, Greg?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: That's it for us tonight. Have a good night.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FOXFIV0020240404ek4300001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Biden's Sordid History Of Habitual Lying\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Kellyanne Conway, Ari Fleischer, Charlie Hurt, Clay  Travis \par \uc2 8,147 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 April 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 And tonight as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  continues to deteriorate now right before your eyes one thing does remain constant the president is -- well, no other way to put it, he is a liar. He is not to be trusted ever. We will explain and we have highlights of his most recent and frankly most egregious lies about the border, about his son. Now, he's blaming the nationwide crime wave that he created, of course, on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Also, tonight, we got Biden, Obama, Clinton fundraising. Where was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ? He was visiting the wake of the slain \uc2 NYPD\uc2  officer. We'll have reaction straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 Also, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  will join us with more on Joe's transgender day of visibility proclamation which he denies. No, we actually have a copy of it.\par \par \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2  will be here to respond to a nasty, vicious, vile attack from the DNC.\par \par \uc2 And the Speaker of the House Mike Johnson has a message for the president who just called him uninformed. We'll see who is uninformed.\par \par \uc2 But, first, let's turn our attention to what is perhaps \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's most blatant lie of all. Now, yesterday, when millions of Americans were celebrating Easter, which is the holiest holiday in all of Christianity -- well, the White House, they were busy promoting another celebration -- frankly, one they kind of made up. On Easter Sunday, self-proclaimed, devout Catholic, your president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , posted that message right there, quote, today, on transgender day of visibility, I have a simple message to all trans Americans. I see you and you are made in the image of God and you are worthy of respect and of dignity.\par \par \uc2 Now this celebratory message followed an official Biden White House proclamation, quote, I, \uc2 Joseph R. Biden Jr.\uc2 , by the way, not the alias he used to use in emails, president of the United States of America, to hereby proclaim March 31st, 2024, as Transgender Day of Visibility.\par \par \uc2 At 1600 Pennsylvania Avenue, Easter now has been replaced or at least at the very least is now forced to share a day with a new holiday that the administration clearly prefers transgender day of visibility on the holiest Christian holiday.\par \par \uc2 Now, the Trump campaign called the move appalling, blasphemous. Other Americans, they were equally outraged. But when the president was harshly criticized for the move -- well, he turned to his favorite tactic of all, he just flat out lied. When asked about his trans holiday proclamation, Biden told the press pool, quote, I didn't do that. Maybe he just didn't remember.\par \par \uc2 In reality, Biden did do that in writing and then reminding everyone with a celebratory post on X and other social media platforms like the one right there on your screen.\par \par \uc2 Now, the White House did avoid any posting of anything that that day in its Spanish language accounts and what appears to be to some a blatant attempt to hide the day from traditional Catholic Hispanic voters where he's bleeding a lot of support.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the -- well, famous White House Easter egg roll, that had to wait until today, the day after Easter. Needless to say, any display of Christianity was all but banned from the Biden White House, even religious themed painted eggs, they were strictly prohibited.\par \par \uc2 You can't make this up, you really can't. This is simply hostility now towards religion. And during his Easter speech, Biden mentioned Jesus how many times? Zero. However, a very confused looking Joe did shuffle out onto the White House lawn for all the festivities but for a president who famously goes to bed early and wakes up late -- well, the early morning start time was quite difficult for Joe.\par \par \uc2 Hunter on the other hand looked pretty wide awake. His father, the big guy really could have borrowed some of that energy. Take a look. You decide.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Enjoy the day and I'm coming down to do that Easter egg roll just a minute. Thank you all so very, very much. Thanks, everybody.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, say, hello to our Easter bunnies. Come on up, bunnies. Get up here they can see you. Come on get in there. Pretty big bunny, huh?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. The slurring, mumbling, bumbling confusion continued during a very friendly interview, oh, with that hard-hitting weatherman \uc2 Al Roker\uc2  on his favorite network, NBC News, where only Democrats are allowed to appear. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 AL ROKER, NBC NEWS: What is so special about this egg roll?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Well, what's so special is just open this is the people's house, and you expect over 40,000 people be here the largest ever, and it just -- we just like open it up the place and let people see this is their place, and it always makes me feel good to look out there and see average Americans just walking around, looking at what's going on because they own it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, that's the best joke could do despite zero tough questions from the Democratic operatives on NBC.\par \par \uc2 Now, of course, the president isn't just a habitual liar, he is also utterly and completely incompetent. And as a result, Biden is losing support from both moderates and his radical pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  base, for example.\par \par \uc2 By the way, the terrorist sympathizers, they were out in full force on Saturday. Take a look there on your screen. They're interrupting the evening Easter mass at St. Patrick's cathedral in New York City, ultimately even rushing the altar.\par \par \uc2 Here's the worst part, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is desperate for their vote. Right on cue, he is rolling out his secret weapon, Vice President Harris, who is now attempting to woo far-left voters with, let's see, calls for ceasefire in Gaza and calls for elections to get rid of the prime minister and the promise of, oh, legalizing weed and drugs and visiting abortion clinics.\par \par \uc2 This White House has drifted far and away from even the days of \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 . Remember he once said about abortion, it should be legal and rare. But if Kamala's campaign is anything like her time as border czars, I don't think Republicans have much to worry about.\par \par \uc2 Now, another Biden strategy is name-calling. In an effort to beat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Biden is now trying to be more Trump-like, but his nicknames -- yeah, they're pretty lame. He's not a pro at this. For example, so-called broke Don made billions after Truth Social went public.\par \par \uc2 Another desperate Biden strategy for November, they're bringing back Obamacare? Really? Where premiums have skyrocketed since Obamacare, the cost of health care, that's way up, prescription drugs, they're more expensive. Taxes are even higher, and the promise, remember, you can keep your doctor, keep your plan and the average family is going to save $2,500 a year.\par \par \uc2 Well, that was a total lie, millions of Americans lost their doctors, millions lost their plans and on average, Americans are paying over 200 percent more with almost half the country now having only one Obamacare exchange option. Obamacare was just an expansion of Medicaid paid for by anyone that works for a living.\par \par \uc2 Now this all reeks of desperation. They're trying to shore up their base and there are no accomplishments from Biden's presidency to tout. Of course, not.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been a failure. Everybody knows it and if you don't think this is a tipping point election, an inflection point for our country and for the world, in 217 days, you are dead wrong.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, here with reaction to all of this, former presidential candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 How's that -- look, he lied about having conversations with his son and brother and others about foreign business deals. For three years, he said the border was closed and the border is secure. Now, he's saying that the economy is doing great, and now, they're blaming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for crime. Is there any -- does the buck stop there at 1600 Pennsylvania Avenue ever?\par \par \uc2 VIVEK RAMASWAMY\uc2 , FORMER 2024 GOP PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Well, look, the Affordable Care Act has made healthcare unaffordable. The list continues to go on, Sean.\par \par \uc2 But I think the most insulting thing President Biden did was on Easter, to name that transgender day of disability, that is a slap in the face to every American regardless of their faith. And it's a good example of what's going on in the country, Sean, it's not a tyranny of the majority that rules in the country today. It is a tyranny of the minority, of a fringe minority that's actually in the name of minority rights exercising a new form of cultural and political tyranny on the rest of the country.\par \par \uc2 That's what the Biden presidency represents. That's what the modern left has accomplished, using Biden as their puppet, their vehicle to accomplish it, and we got to see what's actually going on before we solve that problem, and I think hundreds of millions of Americans today are beginning to see through that veneer for what it is. That's how we're going to win this November.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, this is just breaking, according to "The Wall Street Journal", \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  secured $175 million bond to guarantee the civil fraud judgment during his appeal, saving him from having his assets and real estate seized. Any reaction to what I believe is a weaponized Department of Justice under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Your reaction?\par \par \uc2 Well, look, I'm -- that's obviously narrowly good news with that as a breaking report you're bringing right now. But it's an example of this weaponized system of justice. Imagine the same shoe fit the other foot what would the media's treatment be? We're not a country where a political party in power and a president weaponizes the justice system to go after his political opponents in the middle of an election, at least that's not what the United States of America is supposed to be. That is the stuff of banana republics.\par \par \uc2 And I am worried, Sean, we are skating on thin ice as a country right now. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the one they're going after today. Well, it can be any American tomorrow. And you know what? We have for 250 years in, protected the dream of our Founding Fathers, setting this country into motion. That's what's at stake right now in this election, is this is a 1776 moment.\par \par \uc2 This isn't one of those elections where it's about increasing or decreasing the tax rate by 1 percent or 2 percent here or there. This is about the basic rules of the road. Do we or don't we believe in free speech? Do we or don't we believe in free and fair elections without interference from a justice system prosecuting opponents in the middle of an election? That's what's at stake this year, and I think that just as our Founding Fathers did 250 years ago, this is a moment for us to remember the basic ideals that this country was founded on. And I think if we do, we can win this election in a decisive landslide that dare I say it unites this country and that's what I'm rooting for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to do and Republicans all the way down the ballot to do as well. That's what it's going to take to get this country back.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, I sat on this program in 2007, Vivek, I said that journalism in America is dead. I had no idea how right I really would be. We watched the incident last week with \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2 , they don't even want a -- you know, have you ever been a Republican or a Trump supporter. That seems to be their new litmus test.\par \par \uc2 Biden lies about the transgender day of visibility. He lies about the economy, told that lie, oh, the economy is great to \uc2 Al Roker\uc2 . He lies about crime being \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's fault. He told -- lied about the border saying it's closed and secure, lied about never to talking to his son brother or anybody about their foreign business deals. There's an awful lot of lying and that lying never seems to get called out.\par \par \uc2 And that to me is the greatest contribution he will have this campaign cycle that he had the last campaign cycle. They let this guy hide in his basement and he was able to pull it off because of COVID. Now, is anybody in the mainstream media, will they ever hold them accountable or is it always about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , democracy in peril, demagoguing and lying about abortion, Republicans are racist, sexist, homophobic, xenophobic, every phobic. I mean, dirty -- they want dirty air and water.\par \par \uc2 When does the truth ever come out of their lips? I don't think it's possible anymore.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Of course, they've abandoned all basis for trust of the American people. But this is what George Orwell warned of when he wrote his books. George Orwell intended it as a warning, these people have taken it as a how-to guide, just as George Orwell said war is peace, now diversity is conformity. Now, inclusion in the name of inclusion, they've created a new culture of exclusion, where certain points of view just aren't welcome.\par \par \uc2 But it's time for us as conservatives, Sean, to also level up, to rise up and say we're not just going to say this is who we're against, the Biden administration or the radical left. We have to see the problem for what it is, yes, but we also have to say this is what we stand for, this is what an alternative looks like.\par \par \uc2 And so if the left is