\par \uc2 Anyway, joining us now to respond, \uc2 RNC\uc2  co-chair \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2  is with us.\par \par \uc2 I mean, when people say stuff about me and it's funny, I laugh. I like it. You know, I'll see memes on X or whatever, I'm like, that's pretty creative. I tipped my hat, good job.\par \par \uc2 But this -- it's not funny, what was your reaction?\par \par \uc2 LARA TRUMP, REPUBLICAN NATIONAL COMMITTEE CO-CHAIR: Yeah. Well, Sean, I actually released a song last week that I wrote over the winter, prior to taking this position as co-chair of the \uc2 RNC\uc2 . And so, I guess they say imitation is the highest form of flattery, I must have a lot of fans over at the DNC.\par \par \uc2 What's amazing is that whenever they have a candidate who has the lowest approval rating of any incumbent in history and zero accomplishments to tout, this is where the DNC was putting their focus on, an A.I.-generated song to somehow mock me, which as you said wasn't even funny. Why did they go A.I.? Isn't Hollywood in the music industry, in with the DNC? They couldn't have gotten one of their people to record a song. It is really amazing to see this sort of thing happen.\par \par \uc2 And here's what I know, Sean, they are terrified. They have nothing to show for their candidate. If they were going to go with A.I., maybe they should have just done A.I. version of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . That would have been better than the real thing for them. But we are doing amazingly well at the \uc2 RNC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I will tell them they may want to sit down and get ready for our March fundraising numbers and they had three presidents it took to raised $25 million last week. All we need is one. I can report tonight that this coming weekend, we have pledged $33 million to be donated to the \uc2 RNC\uc2  and the Trump campaign from our first major fundraiser.\par \par \uc2 So if I were them, I'd stop messing around with the A.I. songs and start focusing on their failed candidate.\par \par