ning, Sean. I mean, that might be even more alarming. But I think this episode highlights what your two previous guests have already said. I think Vivek and Lara said it very well. This election is about showing the contrast between these two visions for America, and this proclamation on Easter Sunday is just a great example of that.\par \par \uc2 This radical leftist progressive vision for the country is not who we are as Americans, and I think most of the country agrees with us, Sean, and I think that's why we're going to have a very successful election in November.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Let's look at I'm not really sure why -- I -- maybe I understand why Kevin McCarthy resigned, but then you have Bill Johnson resigned, Brian Higgins resigned, \uc2 Mike Gallagher\uc2  is resigning, and your very slim margin -- the slimmest of any House speaker in history has gotten even smaller. And, look, I feel the same frustration that many other -- conservatives feel and that is that they want the Republican majority, you know, united on certain principles like, okay, securing the border and balancing the budget, those two things. But you can't get that consensus.\par \par \uc2 Now, it has now resulted in \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  threatening a motion to vacate. You apparently have been in conversations. What is the standing of that?\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: Yeah, Marjorie and I are going to talk again this week. She's frustrated and we all re, to your point. Every conservative is frustrated about our current position, we have the smallest majority in U.S. history. We have a one vote margin right now. So, it's very difficult to move. Big things up the field for our principles.\par \par \uc2 But here's how we're going to do it. This is a very simple formula. We will grow the majority in November. We will win back the Senate and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be returned to the White House if we do a couple of simple things.\par \par \uc2 We have to show what we're