s. As somebody who has been chased down in public places by armies of liberals, I really appreciated her comments then.\par \par \uc2 But listen, Sean, you're exactly right. They cannot run on Joe. They can't even let Joe speak for himself anymore. In fact, they ask him not to speak. They can't run Joe on not even being able to find his way out of a door or his way up a step.\par \par \uc2 So they have to run on this. They have to run on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is bad, he's threatening political violence and the media, they're the worst players in all of this because they lie and they lie with conviction. They lie so much they believe their own lies, but why wouldn't they?\par \par \uc2 You played the clips. They've lied about his comments in Charlottesville. They've lied about COVID. They've lied about January 6th. They lied about Russia, Russia, Russia.\par \par \uc2 Their lies never have any consequence. So why would they change their strategy now? Lying seems to be the only way they can get elected. So that's going to be the strategy.\par \par \uc2 Throw in as you often mentioned, Sean, climate change, abortion and that pretty much wraps up the entire Democrat strategy, and it's pretty pathetic.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They'll lie about abortion and demagogue that. They'll lie about the economy. Now, they're trying after three years of saying the border is closed and the border is secure, Charlie Hurt, oh, now, they're blaming Republicans for the situation at the border and by the way, now we even have known terrorists and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  supporters that we know got across that border.\par \par \uc2 So this is all they've got. What do the Republicans do? Let's talk about strategy. What is the best way to counter the never-ending lies and the desire to have the DOJ keep \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in a courtroom for the entire campaign the next 231 days with Joe's weaponized Department of Justice? What is the best way to handle that?\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE HURT, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Quite frankly, Sean, I think the best way to handle it is exactly by doing exactly what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is doing which is to go out there and give the ca -- his campaign speeches, talk about things that people care about, and then let the media freak out about it, let Democrats freak out about it, and a kind of interesting thing happened there.\par \par \uc2 You know, I think one of the reasons that everybody was so shocked all these people were shocked by Trump's speech in Ohio, talking about the auto industry is, it's so rare. You know, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  never goes out talking about anything that anybody cares about. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  goes to Ohio and talks to voters about stuff that voters actually care about, and he talks about it in vivid terms. And he uses a word like bloodbath, everybody freaks out in the media, Democrats freak out, they lie about it as you point out.\par \par \uc2 And they -- and but the funny thing about it is that with all of their hysteria, they managed to convey Trump's message for far broader, far wider than it would have been broadcast if they hadn't freaked out about it. So \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins this, wins this massively.\par \par \uc2 Everybody, every sane person knows what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was talking about when he called it a bloodbath and said and predicted a bloodbath they knew precisely what he's talking about, he was talking about the auto industry, he was talking about the economy under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and he was talking about stuff that people actually care about.\par \par \uc2 So I think, honestly, the solution for Republicans is to get by behind \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and let Trump do what he does best, which is dominate the conversation, dominate the -- you know, the topics that this election are going to be defined by. Nobody is better at it and, you know, on these issues, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  loses.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah. Charlie Hurt, Tomi Lahren, thank you both.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now with more reaction is Ohio Senator J.D. Vance is with us.\par \par \uc2 Sir, good to have you. Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 So, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the irony of all this, he chose a vice president that supported the rioting in the summer of 2020, tweeted out the bail fund, and then went on Colbert and said they're not going to stop, they shouldn't stop, I'm not going to stop, and that violence is going to continue. And ironically, also called out the one person in the Democratic primary that called him out for partnering with the former Klansman to stop the integration of public schools and busing, she said she was one that girl, she was that person that was punished because of what Joe was trying to do.\par \par \uc2 Pretty ironic on both fronts, wouldn't you say?\par \par \uc2 SEN. J.D. VANCE (R-OH): Yeah, I'd say so, Sean. The Democrats seem to not have great self-awareness on this stuff. They've been using violent rhetoric to describe their political opponents, not just for a couple of cycles but for decades. And if we just go back to what President Trump said, one of the craziest things I've seen today is that the Chinese -- a Chinese car executive, Sean, promised a bloodbath in the American auto industry literally echoing exactly what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said and now the media is freaking out because he described a reality with actual true language.\par \par \uc2 If we don't stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's war on American auto workers and American cars, you're going to have a complete decimation of the jobs and the livelihoods in the state of Ohio that rely on that auto industry. If you're in Michigan, if you're in Pennsylvania and your livelihood depends on the auto industry, what are you more worried about, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  telling the truth but using a word the media doesn't like or the fact that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is coming for your job and coming for your livelihood?\par \par \uc2 This is so good f