: Well, absolutely. And you have no choice because this is not sustainable. The cities are going bad. The cities, the country, the whole place is going bad.\par \par \uc2 You know, every state is really a border state. And we're talking to the governor before. And he has done really a great job, Governor Abbott.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Governor Abbott.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : He has --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Ted Cruz wanted to be here, but \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  kept them back in D.C.'s.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : He's here probably for a good reason, right?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Look, we have to deport a lot of people and they have to start immediately. People don't know that \uc2 Dwight Eisenhower\uc2 , he's is a pretty tough president. I never thought of it is that.\par \par \uc2 But 10 years ago, you start reading and start really seeing. And he was a big deporter. And he would deport tremendous numbers of people. And they'd bring them just to the other side of the border, they come back. And bring them again, they come back. Then he brought them 2,000 miles back. And they didn't come back.\par \par \uc2 We have no choice. And the way you do it is your local police. We have the greatest police. They don't get the respect that they have to get. They are treated so badly. They do something and they end up losing their pension, even if it's a good thing.\par \par \uc2 If they stop crime nowadays, they lose their pension, their family, their house. And we're going to give immunity to police. And we're going to let the police do the job that they have to do.\par \par \uc2 I think it's very important. They understand who these migrants are. They know them by their first name, their last name. They know where they come from. They know everything about.\par \par \uc2 It's going to be the local police are going to turn them over and we're going to have to move them back to their country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: When the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was the world's premier law enforcement agency, and I believe we will achieve that again, hopefully.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Hopefully.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They had some of the top \uc2 FBI\uc2  officials. They have said, what we are witnessing is an invasion of military age men. You ask the question, you try to understand people that think differently than you. For the life of me, I can't come up with any rationale or reason for this.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So there's two things that you think of. Number one, they maybe want the votes. I think that they're going to get these people registered and to vote.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'll give you citizenship. I hope you remember me at the polls.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : You know, all sorts of things. But I don't know. I'm doing very well with Hispanic, and you have a lot of Hispanic coming. But the fact is that, you know, two thing, either they are stupid, right, or they hate our country. Because it can only be basically one of those two things other than the voting element, which, I don't know, I am not so sure that they believe that so much. I think it's down the road and although they are trying to register people right now as we speak in which who have no idea what they're doing and --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Who may not know this in New York City for example, local elections.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Illegal immigrants can vote. We got to take a break. We're just getting started. We are at the border at Eagle Pass, and we're glad you're with us. We continue more with former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He will be with for the hour. Shelby Park in Eagle Pass, Texas, thank you of being with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Welcome back to "Hannity."\par \par \uc2 We are broadcasting live tonight from Shelby Park in Eagle Pass. We are in the state of Texas, the free state of Texas.\par \par \uc2 Still with us for an exclusive interview is former President \uc2 