hat much harder. What is your reaction to that?\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Well, first of all, it is true insanity. But also, it did not happen four years ago. Just four years ago under President Trump, we had the lowest illegal immigration in 45 years, because he put in a place policies that prohibited that illegal immigration.\par \par \uc2 And then \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  comes in and eliminates all of those policies. And now we have record-breaking numbers of people coming across the border. Moments ago, President Trump said that he thinks that the border now is the most dangerous in the world. Someone who agrees with him, who typically doesn't, is the United Nations. The United Nations declared the border between the United States and Mexico and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as the deadliest border crossing in the entire world.\par \par \uc2 Because of that, because of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , he's abandoned his responsibility. Texas has had to step up. One thing I did is because we are dealing with an invasion, because of the danger that Americans are in, because we're losing American lives every week because of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's open border policies.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, fentanyl, opioids, human trafficking, sex trafficking, right here.\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: And that's why I had to declare it officially under the Constitution and invasion. And then after that invasion is when we had the Texas National Guard, who's doing a tremendous job, the men and women of the National Guard, they erected razor wire border barriers across this working.\par \par \uc2 So you're -- what the cameras are showing right now is a place where there would be 3,000, 4,000, 5,000 people crossing a day.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And you stopped it?\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: We stopped it. They're now going to California and Arizona.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm sure they're very grateful.\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Well, so \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 's upset so that there's a saying that my fellow Texans will like and know. And the cartels dealing with Texas now and knowing they cannot get through Texas and have them go to California, they've learned what Texans have said from day one and that is don't mess with Texas.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It really is. I've asked you about the border. I do have a couple of other issues I've got to get to. OK, I think a very, very important decision by the Supreme Court, and that is they took on the issue of presidential immunity.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Right, right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I thought that was critical. Then you see what's happening to your friend down in Georgia, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 . And all of this, I would say the left and the weaponization or a law fair or the weaponization of our justice system, in my view, and I think the Governor would agree with me, they're trying to drown you in legal troubles. What is your response to that? Because what, are they going to start a trial the week of the Republican National Convention? Is that their plan?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, they're not allowed to under the DOJ rules, and they should have brought any of this stuff. And it's all nonsense, you know that. It's all nonsense. It's stuff that has been a joke, and every Democrat said they'll never do anything. And they did. They weaponized it. And they came after you and stuff for January 6th. Stuff that nobody thought was even possible to be brought up, and they've done it. And it's reverted really to their hazard.\par \par \uc2 Because you take a look, my poll numbers are now higher than -- in fact, the Governor just said in Texas, I have the highest poll numbers I've ever had.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Winning in every swing state.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah, everything.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You're beating \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Because the people understand it, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: New poll this week beating him by a significant margin.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah. The people understand it and I was very honored with the Supreme Court because -- and this isn't about me, this is about the presidency. They have to do the immunity thing because if you don't, a president will not be able to be a president.\par \par \uc2 If you're going to make a big decision as president and you're afraid that as soon as you get out, you're going to be indicted by the opposition party, by the Democrats, by the radical left lunatics, who will indict you and try and put you in prison because you're trying to do something good for the country. Even if it's severe, it's severe, it might be a great thing for the country.\par \par \uc2 They have to have presidential immunity. If you don't have immunity for a president -- and I'm not talking about only me. If you don't have immunity for a president, you're going to -- you will not be able to function properly. You will not be able to do the right thing for the country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And then they have the other case, and that is now three states have tried to kick you off the ballot, Colorado, Maine and Illinois as of last night.\par \par \uc2 I'd like to talk to you both about, I think, a fundamental issue. You have two-thirds of the American people now living paycheck to paycheck. Many of them have to put bare necessities on their credit cards or they're cashing in their pensions early with a big penalty.\par \par \uc2 So the issue of the economy is foremost in people's minds. It has been since 1991 that the American people are spending as a percentage of their income the most money that they have ever spent. People are suffering. How do you get the economy back on track and how fast can you do it?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So, I think -- and the governor is going to help, because there's nobody better at this. It's called energy.\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And we are going to, as I use this expression -- now everyone else is using it, so I hate to use it, but drill, baby, drill. We're going to drill, baby, drill.\par \par \uc2 We're going to bring energy so low, and everything's going to follow, because that's what happened. He screwed up the energy. Now he's going back to some of the things that I did, and he's letting energy get developed a little bit, but it's too late, because what they have done -- if you look at the cost of food, where it's four times higher than it should be.\par \par \uc2 So we're going to drill, and we're going to create a tremendous amount of energy. You look at the New England states, they're paying so much. It's incredible they could vote for a Democrat. But we're going to bring energy way down. Everything else is going to follow. We're going to get prices way down.\par \par \uc2 I made a pledge to New Hampshire and to some of the New England states, who are so bad, it's so high, that I will cut your energy bill in half, at least, within the first year. And we will be able to do it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Be energy-dominant, that maybe it could pay down some of the $34 trillion in debt that's been accumulated.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Sean, just three years ago, we were energy-independent, and we were soon going to be energy-dominant. We have more liquid gold. He has most of it. We have more liquid gold under our feet than any other -- than any other nation in the world, Saudi Arabia, Russia, anybody.\par \par \uc2 And we're going to be using it. Right now, we get our oil, a lot of it from Venezuela. We don't take it from where we should be taking it. So we're going to be drilling. We're going to be creating low energy. And that's going to bring everything down.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask.\par \par \uc2 I know you have given a little bit of a short list of people that you might be thinking about for vice president. Is Governor Abbott on that list?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, I will tell you what.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I know I'm not on the list.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I know.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And I told Sean before I have been hearing that more and more from friends of mine. After this show, I think I'm going to hear it a lot more too.\par \par \uc2 He's a spectacular man. I was honored when I got his endorsement like seven months ago, eight months ago.\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Right, long time.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And I likewise endorsed, though we didn't have a deal. It wasn't like, you endorse me, I will endorse you.\par \par \uc2 I just felt good about it. And he came out and he said, I'd like to endorse you. He did a good job. And I felt the same way about him. And he's done a great job. Yes, certainly, he would be somebody that I would very much consider.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So he's on the list?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Absolutely, he is.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Anyone else that maybe we haven't heard?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, you know, it's very funny. I was talking about Tim Scott.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You guys negotiate. Go ahead.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : He was not -- Tim -- Tim, for himself, he was fine. He did OK. I mean, he was OK as a candidate, but he didn't want to talk about himself.\par \par \uc2 He's a very good man. For me, he's unbelievable. He's a surrogate.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I see...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: He goes on these shows, and he's ripping everybody apart.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: He's very humble.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And I -- yes, I told him. I said: "Tim, you know what? You're much better for me than you are for yourself."\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: So, he's done a very good job.\par \par \uc2 We have a lot of them. We have a lot of -- we have a lot of great people in the party.\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: We do.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : This man has done a terrific job.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, now you know you're on the short list, Governor.\par \par \uc2 Great to see you. I appreciate your time, Mr. President.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: This is important, what you're doing down here, Governor.\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Great.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Thank you for your hard work.\par \par \uc2 It's sad to watch that you have to do the job that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the federal government are not doing, and how they fight you every step of the way. This has been your top issue.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And the fact that Biden showed up today is a national joke, only for a photo-op. Let's be honest.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's all this was.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : That's all it is.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Anyway, thank you both.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Mr. President, thank you.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 ABBOTT: Great to see you again.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Governor, good to see you. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, we will wrap things up. More HANNITY right after this break.\par \par \uc2 We're in Shelby Park, in Eagle Pass, in the free state of Texas -- straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. As we continue tonight, before we go, a quick programming note. And that is, on tomorrow night's program at 9:00 p.m. Eastern -- please set your DVR -- we will air my exclusive border tour with both President Trump and Governor Greg Abbott. You're not going to want to miss this. We'll air that in its entirety tomorrow night.\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, that's all the time we have left this evening. Please set your DVR so you never, ever, ever miss an episode of HANNITY.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, let not your heart be troubled. Greg is up next. And we'll see you back here tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020240301ek2t00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Trump Easily Defeats Haley In Michigan GOP Primary\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Bret Baier, Ari Fleischer, Newt Gingrich, Jonathan  Turley \par \uc2 8,111 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 February 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: All right. We start tonight with the FOX News alert. It is 9:00 p.m. on the East Coast, 6:00 p.m. on the West Coast, and all the polls in Michigan are finally closed. We will continue to monitor the results throughout the evening.\par \par \uc2 But former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has built up a massive lead of more than 30 points thus far over \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  in this Republican primary. And while \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  appears well on the way to winning the Democratic primary, well, and what is an alarming sign for team Biden, roughly 16 percent of voters in the result we have so far voted for the option of uncommitted. It's going to be interesting to watch tonight.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, Democrats, they have expressed their anger over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's stance on the war in Israel and most notably squad member, Michigan Congresswoman Tlaib. Now in their calls for Democrats to vote uncommitted, as they push for a ceasefire -- well, today, according to Congresswoman Tlaib, she -- well, did just that.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. RASHIDA TLAIB (D-MI): Everyone, it's Rashida. I was proud today to walk in and pull a Democratic ballot and vote uncommitted. We must protect our democracy. We must make sure that our government is about us, about the people. When 74 percent of Democrats in Michigan support a ceasefire, yet President Biden is not hearing us, this is the way we can use our democracy to say, listen, listen to Michigan, listen to the families right now that have been directly impacted, but also listen to the majority of Americans who are saying enough, no more wars, no more using our dollars to fund a genocide, no more.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. This is a FOX News alert, we can now project that \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  will easily beat \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  in the Michigan Republican primary and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has won the Democratic primary.\par \par \uc2 But we're watching the uncommitted numbers tonight and is receiving now over 15 percent and right now, prominent Democrats watching this they are sounding the alarm over this protest vote and what it could mean for Biden. Now, take a look at what respected Democratic strategist James Carville and what he had to say. Take a listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: There is this push to have people in the state fill in uncommitted to -- as a protest vote. It's very hard to measure when to be super concerned about it, when it's a red flag. In 2012, there were 20,000 people who wrote in uncommitted for Obama. What is the bar where you're going to think, oh, my gosh, this is a huge problem?\par \par \uc2 JAMES CARVILLE, DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST: Well, already, no matter what happens, I know it's a huge problem and the uncommitted will do fairly well.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, by the way, circle back circle back, it is back on TV. How interesting and -- well, anyway apparently this sentiment is now being felt by team Biden as well. According to a new report, the White House and his 2024 reelection campaign, they're, quote, freaking out that Biden is bleeding support from Arab American voters in Michigan. One of the groups that helped elect him in the first place.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now to break down these numbers, he is the host of "Special Report" right here on the FOX News Channel. Now, you notice it used to be the Hannity big board, then the Hemmer big board. Now tonight, we're calling it the Bret Baier big board. But he's at that board tonight.\par \par \uc2 Big numbers tonight, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS HOST: Yeah, hey, Sean, I'm just borrowing the board for just a night.\par \par \uc2 Michigan primary, it's interesting, as you mentioned, the former president winning. We'll take a look at the Republican side. You know, there's only 16 delegates tonight. There's 39 delegates at a state convention over the weekend. They had to split it up because of rules.\par \par \uc2 But as we dig in here to the numbers and there you see about 12 percent in, and 65 to 30, now a lot of these counties have not filled in but if you look down here in Detroit, you know, they haven't even filed yet. But next door, this is Washtenaw. This is where \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2  is, Ann Arbor. If \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  was going to have a big night, she had to have one right there, and you see the former president, that's 55 percent in. If you look over here at Grand Rapids, again, not a lot of numbers yet.\par \par \uc2 This state has been really interesting for Republicans if you think back to the last elections. 2016, this turned into Trump country, all of this upper Michigan part, and that's what makes it so interesting for the general election. He's going to win big, all the polls heading in had him up significantly, but really how union voters vote in the general election if we're going to have this head-to-head again, and how Arab American voters vote.\par \par \uc2 You mentioned the Democratic primary and the push back against the policy of the Biden administration, by Arab Americans specifically led by Congresswoman \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 . Now, it's at 16.2 percent. But you look at some of these counties coming in. And again, I pushed to Oakland County. It's at 14. If you go to again, Ann Arbor, look at this, 23.8. You're going to see some of these numbers and some of the Democratic experts on the ground think that the uncommitted vote could get up to about 100,000 votes.\par \par \uc2 Now depends on how many total Democrats vote, but that could be a significant signal to the former president. I want to take you back just really quickly to the calendar and what we have ahead. Obviously, we're coming to the end of February. We're right here in the Michigan primary.\par \par \uc2 But if you go over to March, the next big contest is obviously Tuesday, Super Tuesday, and you've got 15 contests, 11 of them are open primaries, Democrats and independents can vote in them, but a lot of delegates at stake.\par \par \uc2 And then if you go back, you could have a scenario whereby these big states start to add up delegates where the former president could start clinching the nomination. And that's what we're looking at, how long it takes, whether \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  stays in or not after Super Tuesday. But tonight, in the Michigan primary, the former president is rolling, and it's just a matter of how big the margin is.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Bret, I think you're in the right to call it the Bret Baier big board. Great analysis be --\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Just tonight, just tonight.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Just, but no -- we'll get you your own big board, you've been around long enough. I think you've earned it.\par \par \uc2 All right. Bret Baier of "Special Report", thank you, sir.\par \par \uc2 All right. Yesterday, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  embarked on a disastrous trip to New York City. He joined Seth Meyers on his late night show for an extremely unfunny appearance. This should have been a layup for Biden, sitting for a pre-tape show with a liberal host who struggle to -- who struggles to get close to a million viewers a night. In fact, as "The Hollywood Reporter" pointed out last month, he wasn't even averaging 800,000 viewers a night. How does he survive on TV?\par \par \uc2 But during his appearance, Biden tried to ease concerns over his age before later forgetting what year it was. You can't actually make this up. You decide. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SETH MEYERS, TV HOST: You are currently 81 years old.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Who the hell told you that?\par \par \uc2 MEYERS: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: That's classified.\par \par \uc2 MEYERS: That's classified. All jokes aside, according to recent polling, and this is a real concern for American voters, how do you address that concern going forward as you come up to the 2024 election?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Well, a couple things, number one, you got to take a look at the other guy, he's about as old as I'm.\par \par \uc2 It's about how old your ideas are. Look, I mean, this is a guy who wants to take us back. He wants to take us back in Roe v. Wade. He wants to take us back on a whole range of issues that were 50, 60 years, they've been solid American positions.\par \par \uc2 MEYERS: What do you -- would you want to do? What's your 2024 agenda? Because I feel like we live in such crazy times that that is one of the things I feel we hear less about.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Look the 2020 agenda is to finish the job.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. After filming the show, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  joins Seth Meyers for ice cream. Remember his favorite flavor is -- take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Mr. President, what did you order?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Chocolate chocolate chip.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Mr. President, what is your message to Republicans who are prepared to block the January 6 Commission?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Eat some chocolate chocolate chip.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Chocolate chocolate chip, wow.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, he broke some pretty major news while eating his little ice cream cone. Take a look at this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Can you give us a sense of when you think the ceasefire will start, sir?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Well, I hope by the beginning of the weekend -- I mean, the end of the weekend. At least -- my national security advisor tells me that we're close. We're close. It's not done yet. And my hope is by next Monday, we'll have a ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Okay, thank you.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Really, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , you're going to announce to the world that a ceasefire in Gaza may be around the corner. Now, according to the national security advisor, while eating an ice cream cone with a very unfunny late night host by the name of Seth Meyers, and while Joe tried and failed again to ease concerns over his age, more Democrats, they are now sounding the alarm, as former Obama aides are now expressing concerns over what they are saying is a frail and mumbly Biden.\par \par \uc2 And add to that by the way, his age, a very real issue Obama aides are sounding kind of like me, more and more every day. Thanks for watching.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, here with reaction, former senior Trump adviser \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , FOX News contributor \uc2 Ari Fleischer\uc2 . Good to see you both.\par \par \uc2 Ari, start with you. What do you make of the uncommitted number in Michigan? This would be a very important state for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to win if he wants to win the general election. Real Clear Politics average now has him up by five. Thoughts?\par \par \uc2 ARI FLEISCHER\uc2 , FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, it's not unusual to have candidates get a certain percentage of the uncommitted vote, it's happened previously in Democratic primaries. What's different now is it's \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and it's an expression, a meaningful real expression that much in the Democrat base is dissatisfied with him.\par \par \uc2 And so I would not look at this historically and say it's happened before. I say it's another indication that Biden is wounded and he's wounded himself.\par \par \uc2 And the question here though, Sean, and this is what Republicans have to be sober about is, is this a protest vote and will come home in October? And my advice to Republicans, I do think most of these people who are uncommitted now will come home in October. This is going to be a close election in November, and Republicans shouldn't assume because of all these frailties, which are legit real issues,, that's going to be a cakewalk. It will not be.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Either -- either come home or maybe stay home. \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 FLEISCHER: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN MILLER\uc2 , FORMER SENIOR ADVISOR TO PRESIDENT TRUMP: Well, I do think there's a very real concern on the part of the Biden campaign and the Democrat Party that voters are so uninspired and so worried about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , they will stay home and you add on top of that, of course, the problem with Arab voters in Michigan who are demanding that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  push a radical left ceasefire policy with the war in Gaza, which, of course, would be unacceptable to most American voters. And so, they're caught there between the radical base and mainstream public opinion.\par \par \uc2 But I do want to agree with Ari when I say, look, this is the party that dragged \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  over the finish line at a point in time when he couldn't even campaign, through aggressive, robust ballot harvesting efforts. The Republican Party needs to understand as they head into 2024, as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  calls it his 2020 campaign, they need to understand how mischievous, how determined, how relentless Democrats are going to be in filling up every single drop box all around the country with mail in ballots, and they must have a strategy to counter the Democrat's mail in ballot machine, which is truly a leviathan.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, let me -- Stephen, let me follow up on that because I would argue 2022, the reason the big, quote, wave didn't happen, I would argue in large part it had to do with abortion. You mentioned Pennsylvania, you had a top of the ticket Democrat, \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , nice guy, but he didn't even have exceptions for rape, incest or the mother's life. He lost by, what, 15, 16 points. Dr. Oz was able to get, you know, double digit ticket switching, in other words, they voted for a Democrat for governor but the Republican Oz in this case for the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Had Mastriano not had that position, I would argue that that race would have been a lot closer, and Oz would be in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  today. And I think this is a cautionary tale for every Republican. You see the reaction of the left in this country on the issue of the -- of IVF, in vitro fertilization, the Alabama court decision, and clearly, Republicans better message that. In New York district 3, almost every ad was about abortion, and that the ad was that Republicans are going to take away a woman's right to choose, the Republicans better message that better because that's not the case that is not what the Dobbs decision said.\par \par \uc2 MILLER: Well, Sean, I'll just say that the answer is yes and both. Absolutely, it hurt the Republican Party in the midterms to be portrayed as the party that doesn't even support exceptions for cases of rape, incest and the life of the mother. It is also true that Democrats have mastered the art form of hammering that message to a specific demographic of female voters aggressively, relentlessly, with hundreds of millions of dollars in spend, and then sending workers, union workers to their house, sending teachers unions to their house, sending canvassers to their house to collect that mail in ballot.\par \par \uc2 It's the combination of that hyper-focused messaging on specific issues, to specific subsets of voters with the ballot harvesting operation that made them so effective in 2022, and it's essential that Republicans understand the enormity of the machine they will be facing no matter how declined, senile, incompetent, embarrassing, humiliating and disgraceful \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is and remains each and every day.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, I agree with you, and I've been -- we're singing from the same hymnal here. I've warning Republicans, you better overcome your reluctance and resistance towards early voting, voting by mail, and I was really hopeful when I heard \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2  who is looks like she's going to be at the \uc2 RNC\uc2  say they will inst -- they will institute what is the largest legal ballot harvesting efforts we've ever seen. That is critical for Republicans if they want to win.\par \par \uc2 Ari, I want you to weigh on both the abortion, the IVF issue, and the issue of legal ballot harvesting.\par \par \uc2 FLEISCHER: Well, number one, you've got to play offense. If you're running in this cycle, if you're running in any cycle, but you need to play offense and put the Democrat on the defensive about the border, about inflation, about support for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . These are the biggest issues.\par \par \uc2 Now, you also have to play smart defense and the smart defense on abortion is just to take it on directly and make your case to the voters. Most voters are right in the middle on abortion. They oppose the Democrat efforts to allow abortion right up to the day of birth. They also are opposed to a national ban on abortion, and Republicans in my opinion need to be somewhere right in that zone where the American people are and make that clear. And that is when you're pro-life and you're for the three exceptions as you talk about, Sean.\par \par \uc2 But the mindset of every candidate is play offense and make every Democrat on the ballot own the Biden economy, the Biden border, the Biden inflation and all the messes that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has brought us. You win by playing offense.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, I totally agree. What I would push \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  on the issue of any restrictions on abortion, no matter how many times I went back at it, he refused to answer I think that was the answer.\par \par \uc2 All right. Stephen, Ari, thank you so much, both of you.\par \par \uc2 Here now with more reaction to tonight's breaking news, former speaker of the House, FOX News contributor Newt Gingrich.\par \par \uc2 All right. Let's -- let's look first at the Republican primary. One has to ask, especially after Saturday night and tonight why is \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  hanging around in this race. I think at some point, there will be a lot of resentment among Republicans that she is literally forcing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who will be the nominee into spending money he otherwise could be using in a general election campaign. Your reaction?\par \par \uc2 NEWT GINGRICH, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, first of all, I don't think she's going to force President Trump to spend anything because he's going to beat her in every single primary in the country. That's just going to happen.\par \par \uc2 Second, the longer she stays in, the more she will alienate Republicans. This theory that she's hanging around in case something happens to Trump so she can then be the choice, no MAGA Republican, no Trump delegate is ever going to pick \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 . They will pick any of a dozen or 50 Republicans who are acceptable, but they aren't going to pick her.\par \par \uc2 And you saw that in Nevada, where she lost by two to one by none of these candidates. I mean, when none of these candidates beat you by two to one, there's a -- there's a hint that maybe you're in the wrong game this year. I hope she'll drop out. I hope she'll become part of the effort to beat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , I do not think it's helpful to have her out there saying nasty things about the Republican nominee.\par \par \uc2 And as far as I'm concerned, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tonight is the Republican nominee. This is over and the issue is to focus on the general election, and why Trump would be a dramatically better president in 2025 than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'd like you to weigh in on the issue of Republicans reluctance to voting early, voting by mail, and Republican efforts heretofore have not been very strong when it comes to the issue of legal ballot harvesting. I would argue they better ma -- at least match, hopefully surpass Democratic Party efforts especially in swing states well we just saw this happen again in the special election in New York where the Democrats won the early vote and then we had a snowstorm on election day. So that suppressed the normal Republican election day turnout.\par \par \uc2 I'm very encouraged that \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2  is going to make a major part of her co-chairmanship building a case across the whole country for early voting and for getting those ballots in. I think it's very, very important and one of the places where frankly Republicans have been at least three election cycles behind where the Democrats are. If Lara can do her job and can get people around, she's very attractive, very intelligent and I think very articulate.\par \par \uc2 She goes across the country and convinces people, this is how you do it, we're going to be much stronger this fall.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And that very district you're talking about, my old district when I once lived in New York, the ads that were running, almost 80 percent of them dealt with the issue of abortion. Now, we have the Alabama decision on top of that. Certainly, I see the Democratic campaign is demagoguing Trump is evil, Trump is evil, democracy in peril, January 6th, demagoguing abortion, certainly now demagoguing IVF, and saying that Republicans are racist and sexist and want dirty air and water and want to kill grandma and grandpa.\par \par \uc2 Now, that's the narrative that they always come up with. How do Republicans counter that?\par \par \uc2 GINGRICH: Well, first of all, President Trump reacted exactly right, came out in favor of in vitro fertilization, as did Speaker Johnson and I think we can clear that issue out pretty quickly, almost all Republicans are going to be in favor of in vitro fertilization.\par \par \uc2 Second, if you look at the young lady who was killed in Georgia, at the University of Georgia by a Venezuelan illegal immigrant, you can make a pretty good argument that the party that does not protect women, the party that is not defend the innocent is the Democratic Party, and that in fact what they're doing with illegal immigration is a far greater danger to the average woman than anything Republicans are charged with.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, and by the way, reminder, I'll be with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on the border on Thursday. I'm sure it's a mere coincidence, Mr. Speaker, that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  after years of saying the borders closed and secure and now blames Republicans and saying I've done everything possible they won't help me, it's interesting he'll be there the same day.\par \par \uc2 He's welcome to join me and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Ted Cruz and Greg Abbott. We'd love to have him, but we'll see if that -- I wouldn't hold my breath. Speaker Gingrich, great to see you.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, coming up, A