he simple truth, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , his party is a party of division. Think about this, they have racial preferences, they have religious preferences, they have gender preferences.\par \par \uc2 What do we have in the GOP under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ? Well, we have a guy who is committed to making sure that whether you're Black or White, whether you're Hispanic or Asian, that our economy works for you. He's done it before, he'll do it again.\par \par \uc2 Think about the fact that the strongest most powerful force for good is an optimistic spirit with a strong backbone, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is our candidate, he will kick butt, take names and we will win in November, but we need to start talking about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , not \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , the race is over and it is time for us to secure our border.\par \par \uc2 I got to stop here. The number of Americans who've lost their lives because of this open border breaks my heart. It can be stopped, Sean. We need a president who believes in America enough to close that freaking border. It has to stop.\par \par \uc2 I'm tired of reading stories about 2 year olds in the D.C. area being murdered because illegal immigrants come in our country because \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is more concerned with finding future voters than protecting Americans today.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And now, and now, him showing up after years of lying and saying the border secure and closed, you're going to show up Thursday. I'll be down at the border with President Trump on Thursday and it is -- you know, beyond frankly, it is frankly repulsive politics. You know, it's an election year conversion if ever there was one.\par \par \uc2 Your name keeps getting me mentioned. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says that you campaign harder for him than you did for yourself and I think I know the reason why because I've known you for all these years. I was well aware you were getting engaged years before anybody else, and we've been friends for a long time.\par \par \uc2 And what's fascinating is --\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Long time.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- is that I think there's some truth because I know how humble you are as a person. So my question is, if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says, Tim Scott, I want you to run with me your answer?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Well, listen, I will do whatever it takes to make sure that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has no more years and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has four more years. I've said it several times before but, Sean, South Carolina loves you, by the way, you should do your show from South Carolina in my opinion.\par \par \uc2 Here's the truth, whatever it takes, we should get the job done. It doesn't matter whether I'm the VP or not. What I do care about however is making sure that the best is yet to come, and that takes four more years of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, certainly, the country is -- the economy, on borders, on energy, war in Europe, war in the Middle East -- these are scary times.\par \par \uc2 Senator, thank you. When we come back, we'll tell you about more my exclusive interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . This Thursday, we will be at the border except he actually means it. Joe, that's just a show, as we continue.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Before we go, reminder, to tune in this Thursday. We will be at Shelby Park in Eagle Pass, Texas, to interview former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at the border. Governor Greg Abbott, Senator Ted Cruz will also join us. That's this Thursday, 9:00 p.m. Eastern, right here on FOX News.\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, though, that is all the time we have left this evening. Please set your DVR so you never ever, ever, ever miss an episode of "Hannity". And as always thank you for watching and making the show possible.\par \par \uc2 Let not your heart be troubled. Greg Gutfeld is next to put a smile on your face. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020240228ek2r00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Biden Tries To Make Jokes With Governors\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Ainsley Earhardt, Kellyanne Conway, Ari Fleischer,  Charlie Hurt, Jimmy Failla \par \uc2 7,734 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 February 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to HANNITY. And we are broadcasting from the great state of South Carolina, home of the Gamecocks, by the way.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, tonight, I told you this would happen, that your president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , would get desperate and they'd go back to the Democratic playbook. And at 38 percent approval rating from Gallup and 86 percent of the people thinking he's too old to be president, well, he's that desperate.\par \par \uc2 So what does he do? He resorts to using the worn out race card tactics to attack Republicans. You're not going to believe the lies that he's spewing this time.\par \par \uc2 Now, South Carolina Senator Tim Scott, he will join us in a few minutes, as well as \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But first, tomorrow, former President Trump and former Governor \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , they will square off in the South Carolina Republican presidential primary. Now, after coming in third in the Iowa caucuses, losing by double digits in New Hampshire, losing to the option of none of these candidates in Nevada by more than 30 points, I would argue that everything is pretty much on the line for \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  in her home state.\par \par \uc2 Across the board, pundits are wondering, is this the last chance for former Governor \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and the presidential primary? She has promised to stay in the race regardless of the results, but here's a problem and it's very real. According to the Real Clear Politics polling average, she trails former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by more than 25 points. That's a big margin.\par \par \uc2 Now, I would argue as we get closer to Election Day, things always tighten up in the final days of a primary. But where will she win? What state will she win if she doesn't win her home state? And how would you know any double digit loss be in her home state?\par \par \uc2 And while she spent the last week desperately making the case to voters in what is a last ditch effort -- well, there's a lot of ground to make up in one single day. And meanwhile, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 's bus tour continues. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , he held a huge primary eve rally in Rock Hill, South Carolina, tonight.\par \par \uc2 Let's take a look at some of these highlights. Look at this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT & 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Tomorrow, you will cast one of the most important votes of your entire life. And honestly, we're not very worried about tomorrow. We want to aim toward a time called November 5th. That's what we need, November 5th.\par \par \uc2 You've got to beat crooked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  if it's going to be him. I don't know if he's going to make it to the starting gate. We're going to do great tomorrow. But it's really important you get out and vote because as we want to send a signal to the real, the real hard line people, the people that are destroying our country, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , we got to send them a signal that we're coming. We're going to send them a big.\par \par \uc2 So get out tomorrow. We're going to win this state, and then we're going to tell crooked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , you are fired. Get out of here. You're fired.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, earlier today, "FOX & Friends" co-host Ainsley Earhardt, well, she spoke with voters in Columbia, South Carolina, by the way, her hometown ahead of election day tomorrow. And here's what they had to say. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 AINSLEY EARHARDT, CO-HOST OF "FOX & FRIENDS": Tomorrow is the election. Are you going to go to the polls?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We are. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 EARHARDT: Who are you all voting for?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We're going to vote for Trump.\par \par \uc2 EARHARDT: Why is that?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We have a very large family. And you know, we just need things they were not like this few years ago when he was in office. So we just want to see if we can get lower gas prices and lower groceries and things like that.\par \par \uc2 EARHARDT: Voting tomorrow. Who are you voting for?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 EARHARDT: Okay, why is that?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Because I like where we were four years ago.\par \par \uc2 EARHARDT: Who are you voting for?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Well, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , but, I'm going to support whoever the Republican is that gets nominated in at the convention. And, so if President Trump gets the nomination, that's who I'm -- I will definitely support him.\par \par \uc2 EARHART: You've already voted. Do you mind if I ask who you voted for?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: We voted for Trump.\par \par \uc2 EARHARDT: Okay. Why?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I think we need some strength in this country. And having served in the military for over 26 years, I think we need to have that sort of mentality to be strong again.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I am going to the polls tomorrow and I am on the fence. You know, I really am. I mean, I know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did a fabulous job when he was president, and that just keeps hounding me. But sometimes I'd like a change, too. And, you know, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  did so much for our state. And I'm just so proud of how well she has become as a woman. So I think I'll know when I walk in there tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Trump, I'm voting for Trump.\par \par \uc2 EARHARDT: Okay. What do you like about Trump?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: He seems to get things done. He's concerned with the same things I'm concerned with, primarily the border. We -- I feel like we've already lost our country. I don't know that we'll ever get it back.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Here with more is the great podcast host, maybe soon to be vice chair of the \uc2 RNC\uc2 , I'm hearing these rumors all over the place. I heard you were put in charge of South Carolina, another rumor.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2  is back. Lara, great to have you.\par \par \uc2 LARA TRUMP, PODCAST HOST: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 And, Sean, I was actually in South Carolina all day on Wednesday. And let me just tell you something. The people of the state of South Carolina are ready to deliver a decisive victory tomorrow for \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, I think when we get into the expectation game that that always can be. You know, a little a little slippery for a lot of people.\par \par \uc2 However, we're looking at where we are, having been to Iowa, New Hampshire, Nevada, and now South Carolina for a lot of presidential candidates. South Carolina do or die. Any double digit loss tomorrow. What does that mean in your mind?\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: Well, a loss is a loss. And the truth is, you just kind of went through \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 's track record. She has come in last place, Sean, in every single race in this primary.\par \par \uc2 So you have Iowa, she came in last. New Hampshire, last. Wasn't even registered for the caucus in Nevada and lost the primary that didn't get her anything to none of these candidates. That is bad.\par \par \uc2 She is about to enter her home state of South Carolina. Even \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  if you remember back four years ago dropped out before her home state voted, because even as much as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  likes embarrassing herself as we see on a regular basis that was even a bridge too far for her. So I think if \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  loses tomorrow, as you just mentioned, I said it the other day, it is time to come on to team Trump.\par \par \uc2 We all need to be focused, Sean, on one thing. November 5th of this year, we need to be focus focused and ready to defeat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Democrats. And the reality is \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  -- what is it getting her to waste all of this donor money millions of dollars that could go to things like get out the vote efforts, legal ballot harvesting, voter registration, these are tactics and tools we are going to need to win on election day and I think it's very confusing to a lot of people why she is still in this race.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2 , thank you as always. We appreciate you being with us.\par \par \uc2 All right. Now, Biden's blunders continue to embarrass the White House while his aides tried to cover for him, as his approval rating now edges down even further. According to the latest Gallup poll, I mean, this is a disaster for a sitting president, approval rating is more than 20 points underwater. As I said, just 38 percent, well below the 50 percent threshold that incumbents typically need if they want to win re-election.\par \par \uc2 And his polling issues extend far beyond just his approval rating. Now, you might remember the recent ABC poll, it showed a staggering 86 percent of the American people think he is too old to serve another term. By the way, no kidding, it's so obvious.\par \par \uc2 Now, yesterday in California, Biden met with a widow of and daughter of the Russian opposition leader. Remember \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2 , following the news of his death, and he made these comments right after. Listen very closely.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: This morning, I had the honor meeting with \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2 's wife and daughter. But the one thing I made that was made clear to me is that Yolanda is going to -- she's going to continue to fight he had on the way. They're not letting up. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Joe, her name is Iulia, not Yolanda.\par \par \uc2 But that's not the only embarrassing thing Biden did this week. You might remember, the Biden cheat sheets now we've been showing you for years, the ones that tell who he is meeting with, sit down, stand up, say hello, shake hands -- well, they're back and the headlines again, apparently, Joe is now using those cheat sheets at fundraising events. I mean, it's concerning his donors, they're scared to death and frankly, rightfully so.\par \par \uc2 Fundraisers are not difficult events. You walk into a room, you thank everybody for contributing to your campaign. You talk about the things you want to do as president. Why do you need a cheat sheet for that? This is it. I have a haven't even looked at this piece of paper right here in front of me.\par \par \uc2 And now, meanwhile, earlier today, Biden met with governors at the White House and made more several bizarre attempts at humor. Take a look at this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Thank you. If I were smart, I'd leave right now.\par \par \uc2 Folks, thank you very much. Governor Cox, Governor Polis, all the governors for being here, I know you just heard -- did Jill already speak, my wife? Well, what the hell am I doing here? Jill enjoys traveling to states.\par \par \uc2 We're building a nation's first high-speed rail line in California, Nevada. And I want to thank Governor Newsom for his leadership in that. And by the way, I'm not sure how many people leave L.A. can do it in two hours to get there, whether -- they're going to come back or not. Las Vegas.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And in another really sad moment for Joe this week -- well, he tripped again but he was going up the baby steps to Air Force One, because he can no longer use the big boy steps after falling multiple times.\par \par \uc2 Now, the administration reportedly even bought him new sneakers as part of his aide's plan to prevent him from stumbling and falling so much. Well, doesn't actually seem to be working too well for them.\par \par \uc2 Now, Joe is weak, he's frail, he's a cognitive mess. We warned you about this in 2020, and now here we are four years later and it has gotten dramatically worse.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: My dad used to say Joey, a paycheck is about more than -- a job is about more than a paycheck.\par \par \uc2 I guess I should clear my mind here a little bit not say what I'm really thinking.\par \par \uc2 There's some movement there's been a response from the -- there's been a response from the opposition but -- yes, I'm sorry, from \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I think that -- as you know, initially, the president of Mexico, Sisi, did not want to open up the gate.\par \par \uc2 When I said when I -- we pushed all these programs, I said I'm going to be a president of everybody, whether you live in a red state or green state.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Here with reaction, FOX News contributors Kellyanne Conway and \uc2 Ari Fleischer\uc2  and Charlie Hurt.\par \par \uc2 You know, I actually in the beginning, Kellyanne, in 2020, I kind of made fun of it, and I talked about sippy cup Joe and he gets warm milky and the bedtime story and he falls asleep at 7:00 p.m.\par \par \uc2 This isn't funny. Putin's watching. Xi's watching. Kim Jong-un is watching. The Iranian mullahs watching, all evil actors on the world stage, and they're not just, you know, watching, they're also acting.\par \par \uc2 It has become a clear and present danger not only for our country but for the entire world. Your reaction?\par \par \uc2 KELLYANNE CONWAY, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: You got it, Sean. There's no question that when we project weakness at the highest echelon of our \uc2 United States government\uc2 , bad things happen. And all those strong men you mentioned see it. When \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was there, Putin wasn't annexing a sovereign nation, Crimea, like he did in 2014, when Biden was vice president, he wasn't invading a sovereign nation Ukraine, the way they did in 2022, when he was -- when Biden was in the White House, and so on and so forth.\par \par \uc2 Look, the following people and entities are emboldened because of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's weakness. The \uc2 Taliban\uc2 , Iran, \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 , \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , the -- I think any of the illegal border crosses are also watching and saying the borders poorest because the president is not on the job.\par \par \uc2 And the following are just weaker; taxpayers, bill payers, moms and pops, moms and dads, anyone who eats, anyone who drives a car. I mean, the disasters that have come from a man who simply cannot physically or mentally do the job.\par \par \uc2 And last point, I can't believe how many Democrats who otherwise can be reasonable people, wrong on the issues but reasonable people, they pretend that we don't know what we see. They wish away the 70 percent of Americans who say \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  can't do the job and shouldn't do the job. but they know one more thing, that a vote for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is a vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Folks, wake up out there, because she's next to line and then she could run for two terms on her own. Twelve or 13 more years of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  should be enough to scare anyone into voting for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: \uc2 Ari Fleischer\uc2 , let me ask you and maybe follow up on that but get your analysis of this. This is not funny. This is not a game. This is now I think it -- when you add it policies to, it's open borders. You know, we have war in Europe, we have war in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 These are serious consequential times and we need a strong leader. And \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is not it. How do you analyze the race?\par \par \uc2 ARI FLEISCHER\uc2 , FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: We don't only need a strong leader, we need a sharp leader.\par \par \uc2 And, Sean, the biggest mistake, he made you showed that painful series, it's painful to watch it, but the biggest mistake \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's memory made resulted in the death of Americans. And that's when he said that nobody in the military told him that he had option to leave a small force behind in Afghanistan, some 2,500 people. He said no one gave him that option, only to be contradicted later by the military who -- the General Milley, the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, who said indeed the president was briefed on leaving 2,500 behind.\par \par \uc2 He didn't remember his policy briefings, and then withdrew everybody from Afghanistan because he thought he had no options. This is why it's deadly. And the job of the presidency is the hardest job on the planet, even for a young man it grinds you down and wears you out. And we all have an old man doing a young man's job.\par \par \uc2 This is the problem of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . The flubs, the forgetting of names, it's bad, but it's not of that great a consequence. It's the memory loss.\par \par \uc2 This is the problem when you have a president who can't remember the briefings he's given.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That is a chilling and correct admonition warning to the country, it really is.\par \par \uc2 You know, Charlie, I'm -- I'm watching this unfold. We talk about it so often, and I don't know what's going to happen between now and November, but I don't he's not capable of another term. How the Democrats get rid of him, I don't know. Who would replace him, I can't tell you that either.\par \par \uc2 I would assume that Vice President Harris would be first up. Let's -- let's get your take on the overall issue.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE HURT, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, to be sure, Sean, he's not going to get any better considering, you know, all of the problems that he has right now mentally in terms of dealing with stuff. But, you know, also, the other thing is when you look back just three years ago, the difference between his cognitive state today versus three years ago he has degraded significantly, to the point that, you know, so many of the policies that he has embraced or ignored or whatever have -- have wreck unbelievable unthinkable havoc on the country, everything from the border to his foreign policy mistakes.\par \par \uc2 The other thing though I think that, you know, obviously Democrats are going to try to say that there's no difference between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and they talk about the uh nearness in age, even though the nearness -- you know, there is no comparison in terms of their mental abilities. You know, when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says something like he jumbles up his words and he says, you know, they Navalny me or something, like that everybody knows what he's saying. Nobody questions what it is that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is talking about.\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  does it, nobody has any earthly clue what it is that he's talking about and I don't even think he knows what it is that he's talking about. And when you have that lack of clarity in the world, you wind up empowering the worst people on the planet, whether it's -- whether it's \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  or the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  or the -- all of these people who are invading our country now to the tunes of hundreds of thousands, even millions of people, and we don't even know who they are who are invading our country. It's all because of that lack of clarity and that lack of strength that is being, that is being shown by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, we ask the question often in presidential election years, are you better off than you were four years ago? The answer is no on every front.\par \par \uc2 Can you think of a single successful policy of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ? The answer is no again, I can't and I'm trying to be objective here.\par \par \uc2 Anyway I want to thank all three. Thank you. We appreciate you being with us.\par \par \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  is next as we continue from the great state of South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (NEWSBREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. As we continue our coverage ahead of the South Carolina primary tomorrow, joining us now with reaction to all of this, South Carolina Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Senator, good to see you. How are you?\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 LINDSEY GRAHAM\uc2  (R-SC): Good.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Appreciate you being with us. I love your state. The people couldn't be nicer. I'm very grateful for the warm welcome I get every time I've been here.\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Yeah, good.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I want to ask you a couple of questions. I might start with a question that might surprise you.\par \par \uc2 So we have this \uc2 Alabama Supreme Court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay, this is on the issue of in vitro fertilization.\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: IVF, okay? I would argue to you that in 2022, that the reason the wave didn't come in large part was because of the overturning of Roe v. Wade and the demagoguing of abortion, and I believe if Republicans don't get their act together, they're going to lie and demagogue it anyway.\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: This is issue, and the abortion issue regardless of where you stand, if they don't get this right, they can't win. Am I wrong?\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: You're dead right. So as we speak, they're trying to demagogue this issue. \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  said yesterday, now they're coming after birth control.\par \par \uc2 So let's talk a little bit about the Alabama decision. President Trump put out a statement today saying I want fertility clinics open.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We'll put it up on the screen. We have that.\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Yeah. Just read it for yourself. You know, have to -- you know, just read it for yourself. He says, I want families to be able to have a child that are struggling, fertility clinics are just wonderful things for people struggling to have a children, have a child.\par \par \uc2 Now, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 's accusing us of being against birth control. I can tell you right now that every Republican I know, every Republican leader will support legal birth control approved by the -- you know, by medical authorities. The last thing we'll do is shut down a fertility clinic to have a child that you desperately want. And the last thing we'll ever do is try to outlaw birth control.\par \par \uc2 So when Hillary Clinton talks about that, that tells me they've run out of things to say about their own agenda. It's B.S., and it's not going to work.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, as I said -- as -- at the end of the last segment, are you better off than you were four years ago? Is there one policy that you can point to?\par \par \uc2 But this is a problem and we're going to get into Joe's comments about race and he played the race card in a --\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Yes, Strom Thurmond. I took his place.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, the guy that once said he didn't want to integrate public schools, partnered with a former Klansman and said he didn't want public schools to be racial jungles. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , your president, said that.\par \par \uc2 But this is important. Now, regardless, I happen to believe in the sanctity of life, but I understand politically and I bifurcate this --\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- that the country is not where I am, that the country is at first trimester or Dobbs 15 weeks. And when you brought that up, you were hit hard on it.\par \par \uc2 And I am telling you, if Republicans don't get these issues right and fight back on it, that could lead to a loss, an unnecessary loss.\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: So there's no better person to talk about this than President Trump. He first starts with the idea that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Democrats would allow abortion up to the moment of birth, while I'm dying for somebody to ask \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , do you have limits on abortion, anytime anywhere, what are they?\par \par \uc2 So President Trump is very mainstream on -- mainstream on this. Let the states decide, but at a point, 15, 16 weeks, when a child can feel pain, the French have a limit on abortion at 14 weeks, then we need to shut it down except for rape, incest, life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 But the new attack and this just really pisses me off, this is a great country, worthy of a great -- we're not trying to outlaw birth control. That's bull (EXPLETIVE DELETED).\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, it is and this is what's going to happen, because they can't run on their policies. They can't say this or that was successful.\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So they demagogue race. They'd lie about race. Republicans are racist. They'll t