ng. And you know, there was a little girl in California who was part of the second class to integrate her public schools and she was bused to school every day, and that little girl was me.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  playing the race card like this -- well, he's desperate but it's deplorable. It's disgusting, It's repulsive, but frankly when your numbers are as low as his is -- well, it's also fairly predictable. Joe's struggling and he is clearly now more desperate than ever.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now, South Carolina senator, our friend, Tim Scott, is back with us.\par \par \uc2 Senator, great to have you.\par \par \uc2 SEN. TIM SCOTT (R-SC): Thanks, Sean, very much. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 How disgusting and despicable are the comments of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . I just -- stunning --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I don't even know what to make of this. Let me ask you this and I really want you to give your full comment.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: This guy opposed the integration of schools and busing. He didn't want public schools to be racial jungles. Could you imagine the outcry of any Republican presidential candidate if they ever said something that repulsive?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: The things that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has said in the face of African- Americans, despicable. The actions he has taken as a member of the most elite governing body as a senator, incredible, disgusting.\par \par \uc2 Here's what we know about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and we know this about liberals and progressives, whenever they are on the losing end of a conversation, a competition or an election, they do one thing, they go to race and class. It's all they know, it's the party of division. It is the game of fear, and it is disgusting.\par \par \uc2 Sean, we know without any question, this is the president who allows our southern border to be wide open devastating the economic opportunities of people today living in poverty we know that this is a president who's driven inflation to the highest levels since \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2  devastating African-Americans, Hispanics, women and the majority population.\par \par \uc2 This is the president who has allowed our men and women in uniform to suffer through a commander-in-chief who seems to be asleep at the wheel, botched withdrawal from Afghanistan, war in Ukraine, conflict in the Middle East, and instability in the Indo Pacific while we have an open southern border with thousands of Chinese, thousands of people from the Middle East coming across our southern border.\par \par \uc2 He turns to race to get the attention off of his absolute failure as president and commander-in-chief of the greatest nation on God's Green Earth. That's why we need four more years of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah. We talked earlier, I mean, he's at 38 percent approval rating. You got 86 percent of the country saying this man is too old to be -- to be president four more years. I don't know how anybody overcomes those numbers.\par \par \uc2 Now, we're watching what's happening with President Trump and I call it lawfare or the weaponization of our justice system, and they're targeting one man, one family, one -- you know, one organization.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I guess they want to keep \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  if they can in court rather than out on the campaign trail. But so far, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been able to defy conventional political gravity and he survives this, but this will go on for the next, what, 256 days until Election Day. How do you think that plays out?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Listen, every time -- I'm seriously just leaving a rally -- just left a rally with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Thousands upon thousands of South Carolinians waiting outside to get in to hear the next president talk about the two-tiered justice system, how under President Biden, the Department of Justice and states attorney generals hunt Republicans, not just him, because if they'll do it to him, Sean, they'll do it to me and you know they'll do it to you.\par \par \uc2 Here's a man, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , willing to stand in the fire to keep America safe, to keep Americans safe from a two-tiered weaponized justice system. This is the man who can take the heat in the kitchen, and come out without a single shred of anything on him, no beads of sweat, no dust on his shoulders. He is ready for the fight. It's \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  he has to go down.\par \par \uc2 As he just said, let's fire \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Let's hire \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and get inflation down, crime down, let's refund the police, not defund the police. All that we're seeing in lawfare is an attempt to distract the American voter and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from the mission at hand.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. When we come back, thanks to Bidenomics, the tooth fairy -- well, they're leaving kids less money under their pillows. Wow. We'll explain that.\par \par \uc2 Also, it was a week that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  probably like to forget. Oh, the great Jimmy Failla, he's up next. You don't want to miss this, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Welcome back to HANNITY from South Carolina tonight.\par \par \uc2 Biden inflation is now even hurting the tooth fairy, I'm not making this up. New survey finding that the average amount of money left under the pillow by the tooth fairy is dropped $5.84 in 2023. Now, that's percent lower than the $6.23 that kids were getting on average in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, only one person that we could bring on this show to talk about it, the host of the hit show "FOX News Saturday Night", Jimmy Failla.\par \par \uc2 Sir, how are you.\par \par \uc2 JIMMY FAILLA, HOST OF "FOX NEWS SATURDAY NIGHT": Great to see you, my man.\par \par \uc2 You know the worst part of this story, Sean, is that not only is inflation drivin