e two words. Now, while Biden treats the White House like a glorified retirement home, the administration is totally devoid of any and all leadership.\par \par \uc2 Now, case in point, the saga of Defense Secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 . He is missing an action for days on end, and as it turns out, he was under general anesthesia for prostate surgery. Ultimately, he ended up with complications in the ICU, a serious complication. Now, no one, not even \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the White House knew that the secretary of defense was incapacitated and if the commander-in-chief doesn't know, that's not good.\par \par \uc2 Department of Defense\uc2 , they waited eight days after Lloyd Austin was hospitalized to actually release a detailed statement. This is beyond deeply concerning. It is strange. It is weird. It's not transparent as they said, especially at a time, take a look at that map, when our troops are getting attacked on a daily basis overseas.\par \par \uc2 Now we do wish \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , a very speedy and full recovery, but the secrecy, the breakdown in communication, that put our country at risk. The secretary of defense, he is critical to every national security response. Now, the general public, frankly, we don't need to know every detail about his personal private health care. I'm not that interested. I hope he's well.\par \par \uc2 But to keep the president, the commander-in-chief, his boss, in the dark for days and have no consequences, that is insane. And the big question tonight, how is it possible?\par \par \uc2 Well, watch our own Peter Doocy. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PETER DOOCY, FOX NEWS WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT: What kind of commander-in- chief is President Biden that at a time when American forces are under fire in the Middle East, he can go days without knowing that his defense secretary is in a hospital bed?\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY, NSC SPOKESMAN: Peter, there's a lot to your question. So I want you to bear be with me for just a second. The -- first of all, at no time was the ability for the United States military to defend our national security interest compromised.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, naturally no one's been held accountable. No one ever gets held accountable in the Biden White House. There's a crisis, especially one created by this administration. They ignore the problem, they lie repeatedly about the problem and then they stay the course, no matter what, which brings us to yet another important question from Peter Doocy. Let's take a look at this one.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Why should we believe anything that this administration tells us about anything ever again?\par \par \uc2 KIRBY: I think we all recognize and I think the Pentagon has been very, very honest with themselves about the challenge to credibility by what -- by what has transpired here and by what and by -- how -- how hard it was for them to be fully transparent with the American people.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: John Kirby's out answers. These are the same people -- the border is closed. The border is secure. You know, they know the administration's a train wreck. I wouldn't want that job because, you know, how do -- how do you continue to lie when you know what you're saying is just not true?\par \par \uc2 They have mismanaged our economy. They've caused inflation to soar. They mismanaged the Afghanistan withdrawal, leading to death and devastation. That could have been prevented. They mishandled \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , leading to war in Europe. They mishandled and mismanaged Iran, leading to war in the Middle East, funded by the billions of Iranian dollars in large part freed up by yours truly \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , your president rather.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, they also mismanaged the border and all of these crisis that we talk about continue to fester and every single one of them was preventable. The border has never been worse but they've been telling us it's secure, it's secure, it's closed, it's closed. No, it's not.\par \par \uc2 DHS Secretary \uc2 Alejandro Mayorkas\uc2  recently telling Border Patrol agents, 85 percent of all illegal immigrants apprehended at the southern border are merely released into the United States. By the way, I'll add, most of them completely unvetted. They're not sent back. They're not detained. There's no stay in Mexico policy in place because they got rid of that.\par \par \uc2 Instead, they are reportedly given taxpayer funded airplane tickets to anywhere in the U.S. I thought that was called human trafficking, I guess not. They're also given taxpayer-funded food, shelter, health care, education, millions, eight and a half million people in three-plus years.\par \par \uc2 And they're abusing our asylum process. They're breaking our laws, and now, they're living free on your dime, the taxpayer. And the administration now wants more money but not to secure the border but just to hand out to illegal immigrants.\par \par \uc2 Now, so when you're struggling to pay for your kids' education, when you're struggling for bare necessities, when you're struggling on your mortgage or rent payment or car payment, just remember where your hard earned tax dollars are going. You're literally paying for rooms for illegal immigrants in three and four-star hotels in cities like the middle of New York City is -- and by the way, is that an expense you're okay with?\par \par \uc2 Naturally, Biden's approval on the border is now reached an all-time low, nearly 70 percent of Americans, all of them unhappy with the flood of illegal immigrants. Even Democrats now are speaking out more and more because they are being impacted by Biden's horrible policies.\par \par \uc2 Now, Biden seemingly unaware, he's not making any policy changes. He's not even pretending to care about the border. He doesn't talk about the border. He only visited the border once barely for a few minutes last year. His borders czar has completely ignored the issue forever.\par \par \uc2 Does Biden even know that there's a problem there? Well, I know he's asleep at this time at night, it's 9:07 Eastern Time, 6:07 on the West Coast. He's been long asleep probably for three hours at this point. Or is this all intentional?\par \par \uc2 Let's see, a flood of people with dreams of -- let's see -- a Democratic Party amnesty one day, hmm. What would the Democrats want in exchange for assistance in helping people break our laws, not respect our borders, our sovereignty and maybe holding out, you know, the carrot of free citizenship, something of great value and great worth? Either way, it's a disaster. Everything is a disaster under Biden. Nothing seems to get better.\par \par \uc2 Do you really want four more years of this? Can we afford four more years of this?\par \par \uc2 And this is why \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will only talk about the threat to democracy. January 6, Trump, Trump, Trump, abortion, abortion, abortion, and of course, the usual Republicans are racist, sexist, and phobic of everything.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now, Texas Senator Ted Cruz.\par \par \uc2 Senator, how are you? By the way, I'm watching your race closely. That playbook is being played down in your state of Texas. Here you have been at the border again and again and again. You gave this program exclusive images early on when -- in the middle of COVID, when they wouldn't allow our cameras inside these facilities that had kids and cages overcrowded in the middle of a pandemic.\par \par \uc2 And if it wasn't for you, we wouldn't have had those photos. And yet, they're trying to bludgeon you and lie about your record in Texas already.\par \par \uc2 SEN. TED CRUZ (R-TX): Well, look, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and the Democrats have painted a bullseye on Texas. They're coming after me. Schumer has made clear I'm his number one target in the country. He's going to spend over a $100 million trying to beat me.\par \par \uc2 And so, I want to encourage your viewers. Go to tedcruz.org, tedcruz.org, tedcruz.org. I need your help. They're coming after me.\par \par \uc2 I got to say what is happening in Texas, what is happening on the border, it is a crisis at a level we have never seen before. As you noted, I spend a lot of time on the southern border. I go out on midnight patrol with the border patrol agents. I went into the Biden cages when they wouldn't allow FOX News and they wouldn't allow reporters in.\par \par \uc2 Their argument, by the way, when they wouldn't allow the reporters in, and the TV cameras in, they said the TV cameramen might have COVID, and so, as you know, I pulled out my phone and filmed the conditions, the deplorable conditions --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They tried to stop you, Senator.\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: Yes, they did.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They tried to stop you, a U.S. senator.\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They didn't want the truth to come out.\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: They did not want. You cannot see what's happening there and defend it. Last year, 853 migrants died crossing illegally into this country. You cannot see the children as I've seen many times who've been horribly abused physically and sexually by human traffickers. You can't see the women who've been violently sexually assaulted by human traffickers. You cannot defend it.\par \par \uc2 Biden's entire strategy is hope the media ignores it, and by the way, in an exercise of chutzpah, he stood up last week and said, well, the problem is the Republicans won't fund border security. What an utter lie.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Alejandro Mayorkas\uc2  are letting illegal immigrants into this country. They've created this problem. And I'll tell you, Sean, there's an amazing -- phenomenon -- whatever the Democrats in the leftwing accuse the other side of doing it is what they're doing.\par \