the way, they are targeting Senator Cruz big time. We'll be following that closely.\par \par \uc2 All right. Joining us now with more, Wyoming Senator \uc2 John Barrasso\uc2 , and, by the way, apparently ready to make an announcement.\par \par \uc2 Senator, I'm told you have told nobody about this coming announcement. We're glad you chose this show. Welcome back. It's great to have you. We love the people of Wyoming, except maybe we're a little mad at the Cheneys, but short of that, we like everyone else.\par \par \uc2 What do you -- what's on the agenda tonight?\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOHN BARRASSO\uc2  (R-WY): Well, people of Wyoming and, of course, all your viewers know that the country was much better off under President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  continues to fail America. You know, when President Trump was in office, we had the best economy in my lifetime, in most of our lives time. We had energy independence. Our enemies feared us and we had a secure border.\par \par \uc2 And now under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , we have high prices. We have a wide open border, like this -- what's happened at the border? The surrender at the border has allowed 8 million illegal immigrants into the country.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  goes and begs our enemies for fuel and energy. This is a disaster. We cannot afford another four years of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's failure. So if you want to get the country back on track, which is what I want to do, we need a strong Republican conservative House and Senate and we need \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  back in the White House.\par \par \uc2 And that's why tonight, I am endorsing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, we appreciate you picking our show to tell people. I will tell you this -- you know, it's interesting because I get asked a lot of question by people about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and why does he fight so much? Why does he fight so much?\par \par \uc2 And he has a good answer I think, and it's that, well, if he didn't fight, he wouldn't survive, number one. But his real fight is on the issues you're talking about. This is a guy that is going to fight for the things that work -- fight for a better economy, free and fair trade deals, secure borders, energy independence. There wasn't any one of those issues when he was president that was an easy lift.\par \par \uc2 What do you make of the never-ending, nonstop, unrelenting attacks and now the use of the legal system, now attempts to -- he's never been charged with insurrection, but they want to say -- take him off the ticket. They don't even want people to have a chance to vote for him. How's that going to play out?\par \par \uc2 BARRASSO: Very poorly for them, well for President Trump. They cannot continue to do this. It's not working for them. They know \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is a weak president.\par \par \uc2 But on the bigger question of are you better off now than you were four years ago, people overwhelmingly are worse off now than they were four years ago, which is why Americans are turning to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for president. He is the person -- \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has done massive damage to this country, to our border, to our economy, to our standing in the world. He is weak. He's not up to the job.\par \par \uc2 When I look at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and I was with him in Afghanistan, visiting the troops, Thanksgiving of 2019, this was a commander-in-chief who was loved and respected by the troops and he was feared by our enemies.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 BARRASSO: And you get \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , he's a pushover. They understand that.\par \par \uc2 So the Democrats, they wanted to impeach him day one when he became president. They've never gotten over the fact that he defeated \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , and he had me as the chair of his platform committee at the convention, like "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 " called it the most conservative Republican platform in a hundred years and I don't think they meant it as a compliment. The policies worked for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . They were afraid of him, he needs to be back in the White House and that's why I'm endorsing him tonight.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And I will tell you, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as president actually scares me now. I really -- you can see how compromised he is cognitively and, you know, you asked the question, are you better off than you were four years ago? I -- intellectually, honestly, I can't think of a single policy that he is -- he has been supporting that's working.\par \par \uc2 Senator, great to see you. We do love the people of Wyoming. Thank you so much for being with us. Come back soon. Happy New Year.\par \par \uc2 And coming up, two senators, they are now demanding accountability for what we have now learned about the \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2  scandal. And by the way, are their videotapes?\par \par \uc2 We'll check in with Senator \uc2 Marsha Blackburn\uc2 , \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , they're next, and much more tonight, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 Glad you're with us on "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. This is a FOX News alert: sad news to report tonight. Former First Lady Melania Trump's mother has passed away. Our deepest sympathies to her, her entire ire family. They're in our thoughts and our prayers, and we know, by the way, as we talk about these things, it's -- it's been -- a lot of people have speculated -- well, Melania Trump's not been out in public a lot. She's been taking care of her mom.\par \par \uc2 Also tonight, back to the news, final documents from the ongoing \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2  court files were released. They were made public today, and even more references to high-profile individuals including once again former President \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 . And one deposition transcript, Epstein's associate Ghislaine Maxwell confirming that she did, in fact, fly on Epstein's plane with Clinton. The former president did admit to flying on Epstein's -- Epstein's plane but says he never visited the infamous island.\par \par \uc2 Now, while the world got some answers this week, there is still a lot we don't know. Many are now calling for more details, including Tennessee Senator \uc2 Marsha Blackburn\uc2  who's now demanding that the \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2  subpoena the Epstein flight logs.\par \par \uc2 Senator Blackburn joins us now, along with Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  of South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 You know, there has been such a fight, Senator Blackburn, about this issue. It does make one wonder why people are fighting so hard, and I'm not sure I really believe the stories of certain people that tried to minimize their role when in fact we discovered through these documents uh that they were more deeply involved with Epstein than previously thought.\par \par \uc2 SEN. MARSHA BLACKBURN (R-TN): You're correct about that, Sean, and this is the reason to go in and subpoena the flight log, Ghislaine Maxwell's little black book. We want the video footage from the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . We also want the documents around the investigation and interrogations that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  has conducted.\par \par \uc2 It is imperative that we figure out, who was involved with \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2 . That is the only way we're going to break apart this $150 billion a year human trafficking sex trafficking ring and get justice for these women and girls that have suffered. They're victims, they're survivors of these sex trafficking rings.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Do you know anything about whether the reports of potential videotapes of famous people involved with these young women are actually real?\par \par \uc2 BLACKBURN: We are aware that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  has a video footage of the coming and going from the Epstein residences. That is footage that we would like to get.\par \par \uc2 As I've said many times, this is not about celebrity. This is about criminal activity, and we need to know who was associated and affiliated with \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2 , and beginning to get this information so law enforcement can break apart the sex trafficking rings.\par \par \uc2 This is what we're trying to do. I'm the top Republican on the human rights subcommittee. We have put a lot of focus on protecting women and girls and children, and breaking this atrocious industry apart.\par \par \uc2 And, Sean, it is an industry, as I said, $150 billion a year. We also want to know, was \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2  involved with the cartels? We know now that he was involved with Jean-Luc Brunel who was the sex trafficker in France.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 BLACKBURN: We've learned that from the documents. So every little piece of information helps us.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Lindsey, Senator Graham, let me go to you. You're -- I want you to weigh in on this topic. Also, my understanding is you just came back from a long trip. You've been in Israel. You've been in Saudi Arabia. You've met with world leaders, and any news you have on that front would be welcome.\par \par \uc2 A little disturbing to learn the Biden administration is now openly -- pretty much telling Israel they need to stop winning their war against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  which is beyond disturbing to me. They have every right to defend their country and their way of life.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 LINDSEY GRAHAM\uc2  (R-SC): Well, number one, I want to pass my condolences on to Melania losing a mother. She has been very attentive to her mother.\par \par \uc2 Secondly, I did get back from Israel and Saudi Arabia. The attack against Israel in October the 7th I think was motivated by Iran to stop the nightmare of the Arabs reconciling with the Israelis, a nightmare in Iran's world for the Arab conflict to end and Saudi Arabia recognized Israel.\par \par \uc2 So I'm cautiously optimistic the normalization efforts are still on track. We got a long way to go.\par \par \uc2 As to Marsha, I want to tip my hat to her. She's been tenacious. She's asking for the flight logs of who traveled with Epstein. I'd like to know that myself.\par \par \uc2 She's wanting to know why he got such a sweetheart deal in 2015. Remember, the Acosta (ph) guy that was the prosecutor but I think became labor secretary, he gave Epstein probation with numerous allegations of child rape. How did he get such a sweetheart deal?\par \par \uc2 There's so much we don't know. The well-connected in America cannot to get away with abusing young girls and child rape.\par \par \uc2 So I want Senator Durbin to know, you've accused Republicans on the committee of blocking the subpoena request of Senator Blackburn. That's B.S. Every Republican is with Senator Blackburn.\par \par \uc2 Senator Durbin, we want to subpoena everything she's asked for, the flight logs information about the sweetheart deal of 2015, and we on Judiciary Republicans want to get it out and get it out now, so American can judge for themselves.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you one follow-up question on the Middle East. I agree with both of you on the Epstein issue, and that is one of -- one of the Saudi leaders actually said today that they want a normalized relations with Israel, but they said as a condition that you would need a state of Palestine. Is that your understanding? Was that your discussion?\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: not going to really talk about the details, but I'll tell you this, there will be no deal that Israel doesn't agree to, destroying \uc2 Hamas\uc2  is non-negotiable, reconciling between Saudi Arabia and Israel makes the world safer. It's a nightmare for Iran, Palestinian state is something Israel will have to discuss.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah. All right. We'll continue to follow that story. Israel does have a job and that's to defend their homeland, and they were the ones under attack. They just want to fight the war and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  should stop pressuring them to stop. He should be encouraging them to actually win the war quickly -- as quickly as possible.\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Amen.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Thank you both.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, a shocking allegation about the Georgia prosecutor going after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . We'll explain as the president's attorney Alina Habba will join us, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Bombshell allegations of serious wrongdoing tonight by Fulton County District Attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , a codefendant in Trump's Georgia case is now accusing Willis of having an illicit romantic relationship with special prosecutor that she appointed or hired, depending on how you want to classify it. According to a court filing, Willis and the special prosecutor vacation together in Napa Valley, Florida, the Caribbean, even taken two cruises together.\par \par \uc2 The filing also alleges that the special prosecutor has been paid $650,000 for the work that he's done in the case so far, as an outside counsel, which is about five times more than \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  would make in a single year. Is she benefiting from the money she paid this guy?\par \par \uc2 Former President Trump addressed the allegations against Willis in Washington today, saying that the Georgia case is now totally compromised. Trump was in D.C. to attend arguments over his claim of presidential immunity in the D.C. January 6 case where attorneys argued Trump is a victim of a political prosecution by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Beforehand, Trump arrived - - before he arrived in court today, two unidentified so-called journalists waiting for him caught on a hot mic joking about whether -- well, he'd be coming in a convertible and assassinated like JFK.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, here with reaction to all of these developments, Trump's legal spokeswoman Alina Habba is with us.\par \par \uc2 Alina, your reaction to that?\par \par \uc2 ALINA HABBA, LEGAL SPOKESWOMAN FOR FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP: My reaction is probably like most human beings with any decency and soul, to joke about an assassination of a former president and leading candidate is deranged, it's sick and it should be handled appropriately. As it goes to \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , I just -- if those allegations are true, Sean, that is so disturbing on so many levels, number one, for the constituents of the state of Georgia that your taxpayer dollars are subsidizing her boyfriend who has now teamed up with her to persecute and prosecute Trump.\par \par \uc2 For the American people that when I thought we really couldn't get any lower, when I thought we really couldn't attack him anymore with literally no self-respect and dignity we have this. We have a woman who's now bringing in somebody who's her boyfriend paying him quadruple -- 10 times what she's making, whatever the number is, and then vacation on taxpayer dollars and then in their spare time talking about going after Trump.\par \par \uc2 You know, you shared the very devastating news, Sean about Melania's mom and I have had the pleasure of meeting her um and her husband, and I think we all have to remember as human beings, as Americans, Democrats, Republicans, this is a human being and we all have family. And when you lose a loved one, you are still a person.\par \par \uc2 And I think the American people forget that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a person with a family who is fighting the fight, but also has real life happening and I would just like to remind everybody to hug everyone and that you love and send my condolences to the Trump family tonight.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: A lot of people like to speculate, you know, about -- well, maybe she's not at this event or that event. My understanding is she'd been personally taking care of her mom for a long period of time now. Just she's been doing it quietly and she's a private person, and she'd have every right to do so.\par \par \uc2 But back to this issue, so --\par \par \uc2 HABBA: Right, that's right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So here you have, it sounds like that the D.A.'s office in Georgia, they're hiring outside counsel. They're paying him outside counsel fees, and as a result, that is funding a lifestyle that benefits in this case the district attorney that's going after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I would imagine that on some level that she's compromised. What does that mean for, you know, the, quote, RICO case, which I never quite understood?\par \par \uc2 HABBA: It's unbelievable. I've always said it, Sean. I know you've said it they'll accuse him of the things they are doing themselves, and that is the case right here. It's a perfect example. It says it all.\par \par \uc2 If this is true, if she really was using taxpayer dollars to funnel vacations and then go after Trump, completely disregarding ethics, completely prosecuting -- it's called selective prosecution, you are going after someone as a target and then teaming up with your friends, the only RICO I see is the RICO with the D.A.s and A.G.s that is happening.\par \par \uc2 The conspiracy is not a conspiracy at all. We have Soros-backed and other funders that we've seen that are backing these individuals and they are coordinating. They are profiting and they are becoming famous and politically, their agenda is all the same, get Trump. That is the only RICO case I see here. That is the only RICO case.\par \par \uc2 The facts are the truth. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has done nothing wrong, and they have intentionally done this and waiting to interfere with an election because they can't beat him in the polls.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What about the issue of the immunity case? Going before a three- judge panel, arguments were held earlier today, at times based on reports I read, it almost seemed to go off the rails, asking, well, what if the president instruct SEAL Team Six to kill innocent people, you know, would the president be acting in his capacity as the president of the United States? Would they have immunity?\par \par \uc2 That seemed to go off the rails. I understand two of the three judges, a three-judge panel were Biden appointed judges?\par \par \uc2 HABBA: That's -- that's correct. I've actually been in front of a judge in New York and been asked the same question on the \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2  case. I won that case on immunity. It's hypotheticals that do not currently exist because the real facts are so easy to win that we have to now argue the slippery slope argument of if he kills someone, we'll be -- will be held accountable?\par \par \uc2 He didn't kill anyone. He didn't cause an insurrection. He didn't get charged for it, but they're using hypotheticals to frighten America. This is a slam dunk case. He should have him absolute immunity and presidential immunity.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, it was Ted Cruz who said earlier in the show, democracy in jeopardy. That's \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's big campaign slogan, but they're the people that don't want \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to even be on the ticket, citing insurrection which he's never been charged with. Makes no sense.\par \par \uc2 Alina, thank you. Our sympathy to Melania and her family and the president tonight on the sad news that they have gotten.\par \par \uc2 Coming up next, bombshell testimony on the Hill from \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's art dealer today. Oh, I think we're all lied to again. What a shocker. We'll check in with James Comer, straight.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Major news out of Capitol Hill tonight, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's art dealer made a number of stunning revelations to lawmakers. Now, remember in 202, the White House claimed to have crafted an agreement under which Hunter would not know the identity of art buyers? Well, big shock, that was a lie, according to his art dealer. In fact, he testified that Hunter knew who bought about 70 percent of his art, paint by numbers, portraits of a crack addict, we call it affectionately, including Democratic donors.\par \par \uc2 The art dealer also testified that Hunter's so-called sugar brother, that's Hollywood attorney Kevin Morris, purchased most of Hunter's art for nearly $900,000. That's on top of the reported $4.9 million that he had, quote, lent, given, whatever, to Hunter last January.\par \par \uc2 And today's hearing comes as House Republicans have prepared a resolution that would hold Hunter in contempt for defying a subpoena, to testify as part of the ongoing inquiry.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, House Oversight Committee Chair James Comer is with us.\par \par \uc2 Let me ask you about this. Well, first of all, you know, the White House -- you know, they tell a lot of whoppers here. The laptop was Russian disinformation, but it wasn't. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  never met with any of Biden's business partners, Hunter's business partners, never got proceeds until he did. Now, we were told there was an agreement on the art sales. That turns out to be false, sir?\par \par \uc2 JAMES COMER (R-KY): Yeah, this is very concerning because \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said from the press box that the White House had, in fact, set up a policy in place that would ensure that there were no ethics violations between the buyers of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's artwork and \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 When we brought George Berges in, I honestly assumed, Sean, that they had done that. I figured it probably didn't have a lot of teeth, but I figured they probably had set some type of ethics rules and regulatory process in place.\par \par \uc2 But George Berges when we asked about it, he said he had never spoken with anyone from the White House and he didn't know anything about the ethics package.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Didn't -- didn't they claim they had an ethics agreement?\par \par \uc2 COMER: Yeah. Yes, they did. They said that but then George Berges didn't know anything about it, and if they had an ethics agreement, they would have had it with one person, George Berges. He said under oath today, he had never spoken with anyone from the White House about it, he didn't know anything about it.\par \par \uc2 That's another lie that's been told by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and or \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's administration about Joe's involvement with his family's shady business schemes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: John Solomon, justthenews.com, he had a report out last year. We covered it, a respected Hollywood talent this -- you know, this guy, this sugar guy, Kevin Morris, and another Democratic donor who befriended Hunter and became one of his lawyers, bought $900,000 in artwork on top of, what, the nearly $5 million he loaned Hunter or had a deal with Hunter. I -- I don't even know the nature of that that financial agreement.\par \par \uc2 Do you know the -- do you know the full nature of it?\par \par \uc2 COMER: No, we don't, but Kevin Morris is one of the next people we expect to bring in for a deposition. I think we've got that booked. We expect to see him hopefully in the next days, and that's a question we're going to ask him.\par \par \uc2 But if my math's right, Sean, this brings the total up to around $6 million that Kevin Morris has either loaned or given to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , and that's a disturbing amount of money for someone that never knew Hunter Biden prior to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's presidential election, someone that certainly is a -- is a major Democrat donor that for some reason has loaned or given the president of the United States' son $6 million, the president's son hasn't paid a penny of taxes on it, and there's no indication that he's ever made any type of principal, much less interest payment back to Kevin Morris.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you about this, \uc2 Stephen Bannon\uc2  and \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  were held in contempt and they're facing consequences as a result who is the person that's going to make that decision as your committee goes forward with attempt to Congress allegations that that those charges would have to be brought up by who and is this person conflicted at all?\par \par \uc2 COMER: Well, the person that's going to have to make the decision will be \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 . I think you're going to see both the House Oversight Committee and Judiciary Committees tomorrow will vote out of committee to hold \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  in contempt for defying two lawful subpoenas. That'll then go to the full floor. Next week, we'll pass that out of the full floor.\par \par \uc2 Then, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 's going to have a decision to make. Is there in fact going to be a two-tier system of justice, or is he going to continue to -- or is he going to try to start beginning to be consistent under the law? He went after Bannon and Navarro with the full force of the law once Congress -- when the Democrats controlled the House of Representative, held them in contempt of Congress for defying a subpoena. Now, he's going to have the same scenario with the president's son, so we're going to find out if he's going to be treated the same.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: James Comer, we're going to follow this every step of the way. The rest of the media's been ignoring it, we will not. Keep up the good work. Keep us up in the loop on everything that develops. Thank you, sir.\par \par \uc2 All right. When we come back, this is pretty gross -- my former state New York, viral rat video on the New York City subway system, is grossing out even the toughest people with, you know, the toughest stomachs. Wait until we show you the full tape, straight ahead. It's actually sad.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, let's take you below the streets of what appears to be New York City. There's viral video allegedly showing a pack of rats running out from under a blanket that apparently a homeless person is living under, in a -- look -- look at that, there's a person in there.\par \par \uc2 Now for many New Yorkers, just another day of their rat-infested city and the reason so many people like myself are now leaving, have left New York for good. I am done. I am a full-time resident of the state of Florida.\par \par \uc2 But don't forget, both Governor Hochul and former Governor Cuomo, they told Republicans to leave New York. They said, get out. You're not New Yorkers. You're not New Yorkers. Listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. \uc2 KATHY HOCHUL\uc2  (D), NEW YORK: And we're here to say that the era of Trump and Zeldin and Molinaro, just jump on a bus and head down to Florida where you belong, okay? Get out of town. Get out of town, because you don't re -- you don't represent our values. You are not New Yorkers.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW CUOMO\uc2 , FORMER NY GOVENOR: Their problem is not me and the Democrats. Their problem is themselves. Who are they? Are they these extreme conservatives who are right to life, a pro-assault weapon, anti-gay, is that who they are? Because if that's who they are, and if they are the extreme conservatives, they have no place in the state of New York. So because that's not who New Yorkers are.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And years later, Cuomo realized if liberals keep pushing the rich to tax the rich, they're going to leave. Look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CUOMO: SALT encourages high-income New Yorkers to move to other states, and what you have to remember is even if a small number of high income taxpayers leave, it has a dramatic effect on this tax base, tax the rich, tax the rich, tax the rich. We did. Now, God forbid, the rich leave.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They're leaving in droves.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, former Arkansas Governor \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Let's get your reaction. You know, get on a bus, get the hell out of here. You're not a New Yorker if you're pro-life, pro-Second Amendment. I don't know people that are anti-gay, but you know, obviously, they don't want conservatives, I'm gone. See you.\par \par \uc2 MIKE HUCKABEE\uc2 , FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: Yeah. You know, they got what they wanted. I don't know that they want what they got, because what they're ending up with is high net worth people have left the state which means fewer resources. They brag about being sanctuary cities, but I wonder about this poor guy who's sleeping under a blanket, covered by rats.\par \par \uc2 Sean, I watched that and I just remind myself, this is a human soul. He deserves better than that and he's not getting it in New York. I guess if he were an illegal, they'd put him in a hotel.\par \par \uc2 Now he's sleeping under a blanket, in the subway station, with a bunch of rats. This is a horrible human tragedy.\par \par \uc2 New York ought to be ashamed of itself for something like this. It's just disgusting.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I just -- I just think it's horrible. How can state -- a state like Florida with a higher population and half the tax income that they take in, how come they have so much better infrastructure and better schools than states like New York?\par \par \uc2 HUCKABEE: Well, a lot of it is because states like New York think that if you just tax a small group of people, and then you have no responsibility from others, and you take crime and you don't punish it, it's just a mess and they've destroyed the state. And particularly, not all the state but certainly New York City, it's gone and I think you were smart to get out of it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah. I mean, honestly, I know when I'm not wanted. So far, people of Florida been very welcoming.\par \par \uc2 Governor, good to see you.\par \par \uc2 That's all the time we have left this evening. Please set your DVR, so you never ever miss an episode. Thank you for making the show possible.\par \par \uc2 Let not your heart be troubled. Why? Greg Gutfeld is next. He'll put a smile on your face. Thanks for being with us. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020240110ek1900001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Fox News Democracy 2024: Iowa Town Hall With Nikki Haley\b0\par\par\uc2 Bret Baier, Martha MacCallum \par \uc2 9,621 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 January 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Special Report with Brett Baier\par \uc2 FNSPBB\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 QUESTION: What is your closing pitch for Iowa voters?\par \par \uc2 FORMER GOV. NIKKI HALEY (R-SC), PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: The country is in disarray. We see it with crime on our streets or a border that's irresponsible, reckless, and dangerous. We see it with our world on fire.\par \par \uc2 For the first time, 81 percent of Americans don't think their kids are going to live as good of a life as we had. We can't be OK with that.\par \par \uc2 We have one job as parents, and that's to do right by our kids. Every child deserves a good education, regardless of where they're born and raised. We feel it with our mortgage payments, with our insurance payments. Everything that we have to pay has all gone up.\par \par \uc2 I analyze the threats, and the stronger the threat, the higher the heel. I'm a problem-solver, but, more than that, I love America. No one's going to outwork me in this race. No one's going to outsmart me in this race. We do have a country to save, but I will promise you this. If you join with me in this movement, if you join with me in this fight, I promise you our best days are yet to come.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MARTHA MACCALLUM, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: Welcome to Des Moines, Iowa, everybody. Good evening from the Iowa Events Center.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, the first of three special town halls this week. We are now just days before the first-in-the-nation Iowa caucuses featuring Republicans who want to be president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 Great to have you all with us. I'm Martha MacCallum.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: And I'm Bret Baier. Welcome.\par \par \uc2 This evening's session is with former South Carolina Governor, former U.S. Ambassador to the United Nations Nikki Haley.\par \par \uc2 Governor, welcome.\par \par \uc2 First, we're going to talk about who is coming up next, and we will get some headlines. Talk in a minute.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes, like we said, it's a big week.\par \par \uc2 We have -- tomorrow night, we're going to talk to Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Wednesday night, we will have former President Trump with us.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: We have invited Iowa Republican voters from across the spectrum to attend tonight's event.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: We should note that none of the campaigns have input on who is in this room tonight, who was invited, or on the questions that we will ask.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: As mentioned, first, a look at some of the other "Special Report" headlines we are following tonight.\par \par \uc2 President Biden appearing at a rare campaign event today, he spoke to black voters at a church in Charleston, South Carolina, the president indirectly referring to the controversy over Governor Haley's failure to specify slavery as a cause for the Civil War, talked about that today.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: And the White House is dealing with a growing controversy over the absence of Defense Secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 . It says Austin's job is safe. The White House did say that today, and they are reviewing the rules and procedures regarding his failure to disclose that he is in the hospital and has been for days.\par \par \uc2 We still do not know why White House officials were not notified, were not aware of this until three days after Austin was admitted to the intensive care unit at Walter Reed Medical Center.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: And Homeland Security Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas admits today the current release rate of illegal immigrants apprehended crossing the border is above 85 percent. He told me the other day it was 70 percent. Above 85 percent.\par \par \uc2 It came during a private meeting with Border Patrol agents in Eagle Pass, Texas.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  back in the Middle East, as the war between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  rages on. He met today with Saudi Arabia's Crown Prince \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Also tonight, an Israeli airstrike has killed an elite \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  commander inside Southern Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Let me be clear, for those who don't seem to know. Slavery was the cause of the Civil War.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: There is no negotiation about that.\par \par \uc2 Now -- now we're living in an era of a second lost cause. Once again, there are some in this country trying, trying to turn a loss into a lie, a lie which, if allowed to live, will once again bring terrible damage to this country.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: President Biden in Charleston, South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Governor Haley, welcome.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Clearly, we want to start there.\par \par \uc2 The first part of that sound bite was pretty much aimed at you and your answer in that New Hampshire town hall about the cause of the Civil War. You have since explained that slavery was the cause.\par \par \uc2 But what's your reaction to the president going to the Mother Emanuel AME Church, a church in Charleston you often talk about, and he said -- to go after you and what he called MAGA Republicans led by a defeated president?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: I mean, first of all, Mother Emanuel Church is a sacred place. I mean, we had -- we lost nine amazing souls that night for just going to a Bible study. And I will tell everybody, those amazing people, all 12 of them, when someone else showed up that didn't look like them or act like them or sound like them, they didn't call the cops. They didn't throw him out. Instead, they pulled up a chair and prayed with him for an hour.\par \par \uc2 And when they bowed their heads in that last prayer, he began to shoot. These were people like Ethel Lance, who had just lost her daughter two years prior to breast cancer. But she would go around Mother Emanuel Church singing "One day at a time, sweet Jesus, that's all I ask of you, give me the strength to do every day what I have to do."\par \par \uc2 Tywanza Sanders, our youngest victim, had just graduated college. And on that night he stood in front of his 87-year-old great aunt Susie and looked at the killer and said, you don't have to do this, we mean no harm to you.\par \par \uc2 Or it was someone like Cynthia Hurd, whose life motto was simply to be kinder than necessary. That's who these people were. For Biden to show up there and give a political speech is offensive in itself.\par \par \uc2 But the second thing I'll say is, I don't need someone who palled around with segregationists in the '70s and has said racist comments all the way through his career lecturing me or anyone in South Carolina about what it means to have racism, slavery, or anything related to the Civil War.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So with regard to this other story that we mentioned in the headlines, Governor, this mysterious situation around the secretary of defense, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , who, for several days, the White House didn't appear to know that he was in intensive care. We just learned moments ago that they are saying they don't know when he is going to be released from the hospital, which makes this mystery a little bit deeper.\par \par \uc2 Do you believe -- the former president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , said today he thinks that Austin should be fired over this. Do you agree?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: I think Biden should be fired. This is unbelievable that we have a situation like this. When I had a crisis in South Carolina, if we were dealing with anything and I had to deal with my adjutant general, I was on the phone with him every day twice a day. We have war in Europe. We have a war in the Middle East. North Korea tested an intercontinental ballistic missile capable of hitting the United States. China is on the march.\par \par \uc2 First, I have a problem with the fact that Biden is not talking to his secretary of defense every single day anyway. Secondly, is there not enough connection that he didn't even know he was put in the hospital in intensive care at that? And then to go and say, oh, but his deputy secretary knew what was going on but she is vacationing in Puerto Rico? There are so many things wrong with this.\par \par \uc2 But the biggest one that bothers me, when I was at the \uc2 U.N.\uc2 , we knew the intel. We knew the health of everybody in every country. They know what's happening to Secretary Austin. What bothers me is while our adversaries may know, our own president doesn't know. And these things continue to happen and it's why I say the one thing that keeps me up at night is what happens between now and Election Day. Because Biden is making America very vulnerable and putting us at risk.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So on that issue of national security, we're going to hear from our first questioner tonight. Jennifer (ph) is a stay-at-home mom from West Des Moines. She has indicated that she's currently been looking at all the candidates. She is leaning toward \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  and caucusing for him, but she is here tonight with a question for you, Governor Haley.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer (ph), take it away.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Hi, Jennifer (ph).\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED: Hi there, good evening. I am concerned about your national security policies. Please explain to us how you will put the United States first and, additionally, I'm wondering how you can continue to send money to Ukraine where they're really not accounting for how they're spending all of our billions of dollars.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: That's a great question. And, you know, for anybody that questions why we should care about Ukraine, that's a legitimate question for you to ask. The problem is no one is giving you the answer. And I blame Biden for all of that. He should always tell Americans why we're doing what we're doing.\par \par \uc2 The reason we care about Ukraine, and I'll be the first one to say, I don't think we should give any country, friend or foe, cash, because you can't follow it and you can't hold it accountable. I don't think we need to put troops on the ground in Ukraine and Ukraine doesn't want them because they want to be able to win it themselves.\par \par \uc2 But what I saw at the United Nations, terrorists, thugs, and dictators always tell us what they're going to do. They're amazingly transparent. \uc2 Hamas\uc2  said they were going to go into Israel. They did. China said they were going to take Hong Kong. It happened. Russia said they were going to invade Ukraine. We watched it. China said Taiwan is next. We'd better believe it.\par \par \uc2 Russia said once they take Ukraine, Poland and the Baltics are next. Those are \uc2 NATO\uc2  countries. That puts America at war. This is about preventing war. It's always been about preventing war.\par \par \uc2 My husband is a combat veteran. He's deployed now. The last thing I want him or any of his military brothers and sisters to do is to go to war. But to avoid going to war, you have to prevent it. And just to support Ukraine, it only costs 3.5% of our defense budget. That's it. The Europeans have paid more, and they should. It's in their neighborhood.\par \par \uc2 But this is about preventing war. And we have to make sure that we do everything we can to keep Americans safe and to keep our national security safe.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: But as a percentage of GDP, we're the largest supporter of the war in Ukraine. And what we're seeing in terms of polling on this is that it's declined 9 points over the course of the last year, in your party, of people who say that we should continue to, that they favor continuing funding the Ukraine military. Are you concerned that since Trump and DeSantis, and Ramaswamy are on the other side of this, that they are more concerned about security at home than abroad that you might be on the wrong side of this issue in your party?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: No, because polling isn't what guides me. That shows that Biden should be communicating more why this happens. If people knew this prevented war, they would absolutely want to do this. I mean, what we know now is there's a reason the Taiwanese want the West and US to help the Ukrainians, because they know if Ukraine wins, China won't invade Taiwan. We need to remember that.\par \par \uc2 Before Russia invaded Ukraine, China and Russia held hands and named themselves unlimited partners. We need to know what that means. A win for Russia is a win for China. This is about preventing war. I will never do things based on a poll. What I will do is over communicate to every American so they know why things matter., why are we doing what we're doing.\par \par \uc2 And the fact that we don't go out there and just help countries for the sake of it, we do it when we know it keeps Americans safe and we do it when we know it protects -- it prevents war. I think that DeSantis is wrong for calling this a territorial dispute. I think that Trump has copped out because he used to get it right and now he's turning around and he's getting it wrong, wanting to be an isolationist.\par \par \uc2 We need to remember that America always needs friends. We needed a lot of friends on September 12th. But you got to be a friend to get a friend.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right. Governor, Jenny is -- thank you, an artist from Urbandale. Where are you, Jenny? This says, Jenny, that you're still undecided who you'll caucus for just six days to go. Is that right?\par \par \uc2 JENNY, REPUBLICAN VOTER: Yes, that's right.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: OK. You're leaning towards somebody.\par \par \uc2 JENNY: No.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Really undecided?\par \par \uc2 JENNY: Really undecided.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: OK. So what's your question for Governor Haley?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Hi, Jenny.\par \par \uc2 JENNY: Hi. Thanks for taking my question.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Sure.\par \par \uc2 JENNY: I watch the news a lot every day, and I watch how many people are pouring over the border. And I keep wondering, how are we, as the United States, supposed to provide housing, medical care, food, education for all of these people? And then if we deport them, how do we pay for that as well?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: We're not supposed to. And your question is exactly what I think every American is worried about. And it's not just the southern border, it's the northern border too. You look at the fact that we have had 8 million illegal immigrants come to that border. Biden sent back only 142,000 last year. That's it. We've had more fentanyl cross the border that would kill every single American. Number one cause of death for adults 18 to 45, fentanyl.\par \par \uc2 And don't think for a second China doesn't know what they're doing when they send it over. If we want to deal with this, we have to deal with it once and for all. No more excuses. And that means more than just building a wall. We need to do more than that.\par \par \uc2 When I was governor, I passed one of the toughest illegal immigration laws in the country. Obama sued me over it. We need to carry that nationwide. We'll do a national e-verify program where businesses have to prove that the people they hire are in this country legally. We'll put 25,000 border patrol and ICE agents on the ground and let them do their job. They're not letting them do their job right now. We will defund sanctuary cities once and for all, so that there are no safe havens for any illegal immigrants.\par \par \uc2 We will go back to the Remain of Mexico policy so they never step foot on US soil to start with. And instead of catch and release, we'll go to catch and deport. And for all of those that have come over, as cruel as it sounds, you got to send them back.\par \par \uc2 We have to send them back because if we don't send them back, it is an incentive for others to come. And Biden gave half a million Venezuelans temporary protective status. That's half a million Social Security numbers, that's half a million driver's licenses. I saw at the \uc2 UN\uc2  what that does. They pick up the phone and they call their family members and tell them to come on.\par \par \uc2 Not only that, they're cutting the line of those people who were trying to do it the right way. We are a country of laws.\par \par \uc2 The second we stop being a country of laws, we give up everything this country was founded on.\par \par \uc2 We need to secure the border. We need to build the wall. We need to deport anybody that doesn't come here the right way, and we need to start thinking of, again, national security.\par \par \uc2 America right now is acting like it's September 10th. We better remember what September 12th felt like because it only takes one person.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Governor, former President Trump's campaign is out with an ad today that says that you are too weak and too liberal to deal with the immigration issue on the border. It says that you refuse to call illegal immigrants criminals and was opposed to Trump's border wall.\par \par \uc2 What's your response to that?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: My response is, why did Obama sue me for passing one of the toughest illegal immigration laws in the country?\par \par \uc2 Look, just because President Trump says something doesn't make it true. Every -- first of all, I appreciate all the --\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 I appreciate all the attention President Trump is giving me. It is quite sweet and thoughtful of him. But he's lying about it.\par \par \uc2 And I'll tell you the reason he's lying about it is because he's taking snippets of things I said. I said you shouldn't just do the border wall. You have to do more than that. That's what I said.\par \par \uc2 From the second I was governor of South Carolina, we fought against illegal immigration. We fought against the Syrian refugees. We fought against Guantanamo Bay prisoners coming. We fought every single second because we cannot have people who have not come here the right way.\par \par \uc2 My parents came here the right way. We are blessed to take care of my parents. They are 78 and 90. And whenever I have dinner with my mom, she still says, are those people still crossing the border?\par \par \uc2 They are offended by what's happening. And my mom would always say if they don't follow the laws to come to this country, they won't follow the laws when they get to this country.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, you're also getting heat for not being conservative enough or a true conservative from DeSantis. He has a new ad out saying that \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  was your inspiration. And he plays a number of videos where you say, yes, you know, we differed on certain issues, but she inspired me to get into politics. I saw her speak at The Leadership Institute. I walked out the door and I made my decision to get into politics.\par \par \uc2 You're shaking your head.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: No. Because I mean, look, DeSantis is desperate. He's lying because he's losing.\par \par \uc2 But let's go -- the problem is if you have to lie to win, you don't deserve to win.\par \par \uc2 I never said \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  was an inspiration. What I said when I was talking to a group of women, who were looking at running for office, I said the same thing about her that I said about \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2 . And that is when I was looking to run, everybody told me why I couldn't do it.\par \par \uc2 They said you're too young. They said you have small children. Oh, you should start at the school board level.\par \par \uc2 And I went to a women's leadership forum at \uc2 Furman University\uc2  and one of the speakers happened to be \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 . And I have never agreed with a single thing \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  has ever said and I said that, too. But Ron forgot to put that in the ad.\par \par \uc2 But what I'll tell you is, she ended it by saying, for every reason they tell you not to run, that's exactly the reason you should. And I left there and said that's it. I'm running for office. I had never been politically active. I had never been involved in politics.\par \par \uc2 So, they can twist and turn this all they want, but it's because they see what we see, we're surging in the polls -- not just in Iowa, not just in New Hampshire, not just in South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 But I'll say that's the problem with politicians. Rather than talking about what they can do, they just want to talk up and make things up that I -- that they are saying that I said.\par \par \uc2 I'm happy to dispute it every day of the week. But at the end of the day, I'd rather be talking about inflation and our economy and education, and how we have to go back to the basics and get our kids reading again. About a border that's out of control. About the fact that we need law and order back in this country and that we need a strong America that we can be proud of again. And that's what I'm going to stay focused on.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Governor, we have a lot more questions on those very topics. When we come back, we will talk about a lot of those topics with Governor Haley coming up. And, also, deal with the frontrunner in this race, former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I'm sick of the division in the country on both sides. I think both parties have failed the country. But I'm hoping that Nikki Haley can be that fresh voice to bring our party and the country together.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Welcome back to our town hall with Republican presidential candidate, Former South Carolina Governor Nikki Haley.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, we are going to go straight to our next questioner. Dan is a small business owner. He voted for Trump in 2020, but he says he is considering Haley this time around and he's open to all of the candidates.\par \par \uc2 So, Governor, here's your opportunity to convince Dan. Dan, what's your question tonight?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Hi, Dan.\par \par \uc2 DAN: Hi, Governor Haley. My question is, inflation is soaring and multiple states are implementing higher minimum wages, which will only exacerbate cost of goods and job growth even more. What can you realistically do as president to combat this or is there no going back?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: There's going back. They just may not like the going back and what that looks like. I mean, first of all, you look, and as much as I would love to say Biden did this to us, our Republicans did this to us too.\par \par \uc2 I mean, you look back at that $2.2 trillion COVID stimulus bill that they passed with no accountability. We now have 80 million Americans on Medicaid, 42 million Americans on food stamps. That's a third of our country. And did Republicans try and make it right? No. They opened up earmarks and pet projects for the first time in 10 years, pushing through 7,000 of them last December.\par \par \uc2 Want to know how they spent your money? Thirty million dollars on an honors college in Vermont, $10 million to tear down a hotel in Alaska, $7.5 million on a courthouse in Colorado, and the list goes on. In the 2024 appropriations budget, Republicans put in $7.4 billion worth of pet projects and earmarks. Democrats put in $2.8 billion.\par \par \uc2 So now you tell me who the big spenders are, all while one in six American families can't pay their utility bill, 60 percent of Americans are living paycheck to paycheck, 50 percent of American families can't afford diapers? Social Security will go bankrupt in 10 years. Medicare will go bankrupt in eight.\par \par \uc2 So what we have to do is realize there are no saints in Washington that got us into this. Stimuluses never work. Debt never works. Everybody talks about how great the economy was under Trump, but at what cost? He put us $8 trillion in debt in just four years. Our kids will never forgive us for that. That's not how you improve an economy.\par \par \uc2 What we will do is, we will stop the spending, we will stop the borrowing, we will eliminate the earmarks, and I will veto any spending bill that doesn't take us back to pre-COVID levels. We will go and take as many federal programs as we can and send them down to the state level. That will reduce the size of the federal government, but it will empower people on the ground.\par \par \uc2 And then we will focus on the middle class. Right now, the middle class, we're watching the rich get richer and the poor get poorer. We're going to go and eliminate the gas and diesel tax in this country. And then we're going to make sure we cut taxes on the middle class and simplify those brackets.\par \par \uc2 And, finally, we're going to make the small business tax cuts permanent. They made them temporary. They made the corporate tax cuts permanent. I grew up in a small business. Small businesses are the heartbeat of our economy. But we can't just say it. We have to prove it.\par \par \uc2 So when we start to focus on the spending that's happening -- and I will do it in every one of our agencies is make sure we take them back to what their core mission is, get all these old programs down, get all this federal regulation down, get all this extra bureaucracy down. That's how we will start to get our financial situation back on track.\par \par \uc2 And that's why I think we need an accountant in the White House.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Well, Michelle (ph)...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: ... is of the same mind-set as far as her job. She's a financial adviser. She's from West Des Moines.\par \par \uc2 It says here that you're undecided.\par \par \uc2 Michelle, is that true?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes, I'm going to make my final decision after tomorrow night's town hall.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: OK, you have a question for the governor.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Hi, Michelle.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Hi.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Nice to see you again.\par \par \uc2 And you have already led into some of this, but most Americans are counting on Social Security benefits during their retirement years. But, as you highlighted, current projections show that Social Security, as we know it today, is no longer sustainable.\par \par \uc2 What changes, should you become president, would you make so Americans can be confident in the future that Social Security -- Social Security will be there for them?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: First acknowledge what I just said, that it's going to go bankrupt in 10 years. Medicare will go bankrupt in eight.\par \par \uc2 Every one of my opponents, every single one has said they're not going to touch Social Security and Medicare. Do you know what that means? That means they're actually going to go and become president and serve four or eight years and leave it bankrupt. That's irresponsible.\par \par \uc2 What I will tell you is, we have got an issue. We need to fix it. And the way we fix it is, no one has to worry that you're going to lose what you paid in or what you gave. America should always keep her promises and we have to live by that.\par \par \uc2 But what we will do is make changes to those like my kids in their 20s, those coming into the system. We will change their retirement age to reflect life expectancy. We will change -- rather than doing cost-of-living increases, we will do increases based on inflation.\par \par \uc2 We will limit the benefits on the wealthy, and we will expand Medicare Advantage plans that seniors love that create competition. Once we do that, we will know exactly what we're dealing with. We're not going to put our head in the sand. If anything, we're going to get in front of the issue and fix it, so that you never have to worry about not having it.\par \par \uc2 But, also, let's fix it so that our kids can have it too. Right now, they know they're not going to have it. Let's make the changes to be responsible. That's how you deal with it. You don't just do what's politically popular by saying, I'm not going to touch any of those things. That's irresponsible.\par \par \uc2 We do have to do it. But we don't have to hurt people to do it. We just have to get in front of people to get it done.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: So, Governor, Governor DeSantis is hitting you for claiming the retirement age is -- quote -- "way, way too low."\par \par \uc2 He said -- quote -- "I don't know why she's saying that."\par \par \uc2 So, are you saying that? Where do you stand?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: I have never once said that. I have...\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Well, wait. Wait, wait, wait.\par \par \uc2 In \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  interview, you said: "Anyone who says they will leave America bankrupt, Social Security will go bankrupt. Medicare will. So, we don't touch anyone's retirement. But go to people like my kids in their 20s and tell them the rules haven't changed. Change the retirement age to reflect life expectancy.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Yes, for those in their 20s. But I have never said retirement age is way too low for everyone else. I mean, he's totally misrepresenting the facts. That's what he has done. Ron continues to lie because he's losing. But the reality is, that is what I have always said, is America should keep her promises, every time.\par \par \uc2 But rather than saying you're not going to touch it, like Ron says, we have to touch it. But we have to also be honest and over-communicate with those in their 20s that this is what we're going to do. But if we do this, we'll make sure you have something to go forward with.\par \par \uc2 And it's also letting seniors and those in their 40s and 50s know, don't worry, we're not looking to touch yours. We're looking to actually save it so that you have something when your time comes.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: OK. Take a listen to this, the former president.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT, 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Nikki would sell you out just like she sold me out. I mean, I'll never run against him, he was a great president, why would I run? Ladies and gentlemen, I've decided to run.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: What do you say to the former president about he says you betrayed him, that you sold him out, because you promised him you would never run against him?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: I will tell you when I said that I would never run against him, we hadn't had the debacle in Afghanistan. We hadn't had inflation go through the roof. And we didn't lose the midterms by ridiculous numbers. And I campaigned for a lot of candidates, House and Senate, and governors races on those. And we were devastated when we lost the midterms.\par \par \uc2 But I will also tell you this. What he won't tell you is when I decided to run, I called him. And I called him for two reasons. One, because it was the right thing to do. He had given me the job. And, two, because I wanted him to know I was in it to win it. And I told him then we needed a new generational leader. I told him then we needed to leave the negativity and the baggage behind. And I stand by that.\par \par \uc2 Look, I think President Trump was the right president at the right time. I agree with a lot of his policies. But rightly or wrongly, chaos follows him. And you all know I'm right. Chaos follows him.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HALEY: And we -- we can't be a country in disarray and the world on fire and go through four more years of chaos. We won't survive it. You don't fix Democrat chaos with Republican chaos.\par \par \uc2 And not only that, we can't go through another nail-biter of an election. We can't. And if you look at the head-to-head polls, Trump, on a good day, might be up over Biden by 2 points. Wall Street Journal had him up by 4. I'm in every one of those same polls, I defeat Biden by 17 points, 17 points. Do you know what that means?\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HALEY: That's -- that's more than the presidency. That's governorships. That's House. That's Senate. That's all the way down to school board.\par \par \uc2 But more than that, you go in with a double-digit win over Biden in D.C., that's a mandate to get our out-of-control spending back on track. That's a mandate to make sure our kids are reading and get our education back to the basics. That's a mandate to secure our borders with no more excuses. And that's a mandate to bring law and order back to our country.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: But, Governor, if -- if I may, so but -- but that's if you get to the general election. Right down you're 30 points down from -- from former President Trump. And some people -- you've got a lot of momentum, a lot of very big donors have come to your side because they think that you're the one who could take him down. And some of them criticize you for not going after him hard enough. They say you talk about chaos following him but that you are too -- too careful about your approach. What do you say?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: What I've always said and what is still true, pro-Trumpers don't think I love Trump enough, anti-Trumpers don't think I hate him enough. And I don't hate him. I told you I think he was the right president at the right time. But any policy that comes up, I'm going to tell you exactly where I stand on that policy.\par \par \uc2 But politics isn't personal for me. And that's actually been what's wrong with politics for so long is they make it about personalities. The reason I'm doing this, I don't want my kids to live like this. We have got to stop with this hatred back and forth. We've got to stop with these divisions.\par \par \uc2 I don't have resentment for President Trump...\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Let me just press you on this.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: ... but I don't think he should be the next president going forward. And I'm happy to tell you all the reasons why I think that is.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: We obviously just got through the anniversary of January 6th. Do you agree with Democrats and people like Lynne Cheney -- or \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , rather, who say former President Trump is a threat to democracy?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Oh, what I think is I think the American people can decide this. And so what I have said is, he said January 6th was a beautiful day. I think January 6th was a terrible day. I hope we never see that happen again. And so that's the focus we should have.\par \par \uc2 I believe the American people and I trust the American people. And all these people who are trying to tell, whether it's Iowans or Granite Staters or South Carolinians, what they're going to do before they have even done it, everybody is tired of that.\par \par \uc2 Talk to the people of Iowa. They are still making up their mind right now. So for you all to say that Trump is 30 points up, I would say wait until caucus day, because that's the only day that's truly going to show where Americans are.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right. Governor, we have many more questions from our audience here when we come back, how Governor Haley would navigate the challenging issue of abortion on the national stage.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Also, does being a role model really matter to voters, when we come back.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We think the President should be someone who we look up to, and who we admire, and who we would want our children to act like. And so that's one of the things that we've talked about this morning that we would like to have that as a leader of our country. And so then that indicates who we might support or not support.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 MACCALUM: Welcome back to Iowa, everybody, in our town hall tonight with Republican presidential candidate Nikki Haley.\par \par \uc2 We're going to talk now a little bit about family values and issues, including abortion and we have our first question.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: From Sue in Des Moines.\par \par \uc2 Sue, you have made up your mind or haven't made up your mind?\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE MEMBER: I'm --\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Getting there?\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE MEMBER: -- getting there.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: You're getting there. So, maybe you're leaning towards the governor here?\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE MEMBER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: OK. Let's -- what's your question for the governor.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Hi, Sue.\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE MEMBER: Hi, Governor.\par \par \uc2 As a college-educated mom of seven, I am concerned about my young adult and teenage children coming of age in a society that no longer values life and the institution of the family or trusts in higher education.\par \par \uc2 Describe your vision for America's family, one mom to another?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Oh, love that question and you're a super mom at that.\par \par \uc2 You know, I'll tell you, for me, I've always said that -- and you'll relate to this -- if I'm a good mom and a good wife, I'll be a good governor. If I'm a good mom and a good wife, I'll be a good ambassador. If I'm a good mom and a good wife, I'll be a good president.\par \par \uc2 When my kids were little, even when I was governor, I would still be home five days a week to have dinner with them because I thought the family dinner mattered. Sundays were our days. We always were together on Sunday. And Friday nights were Haley family fun nights.\par \par \uc2 And I think right now, what we need to do is -- one, it's okay to have God in your life and say that. I mean, I think I walk by faith, not by sight. And I think we should never be afraid to say that.\par \par \uc2 You know I always go back to the day bef -- the Saturday before the Mother Emanuel shooting that was so devastating. I called for a state day of prayer. And I was vilified for it.\par \par \uc2 And I thought it was so important because at that time there was a lot of toxicity from the Obama administration and division that we were feeling what was happening. And I thought that it was important. Now I think it was divine.\par \par \uc2 The fact that we had that day of prayer before one of the worst shootings that our country had ever seen, I think God saved us. You know, there was a reason on the heels of Ferguson that we didn't have riots, we had vigils. There's a reason that we didn't have protests we had prayer, because we had that in our hearts and on our minds.\par \par \uc2 And I think that we have to always do that, especially now going forward. You look at our kids, they have more anxiety, stress, and depression than we've seen ever. We need to be there for them, and we need to make sure that they know that there are places that they can go that will show them that your faith can get you through this, or guidance can get you through this.\par \par \uc2 And so, that's what we want to do is make sure that it's always about faith, family, and country. That's what it used to be. Our parents would raise us to be strong individuals. We would go to school, and we would learn what we need to be successful. We would go church and we would find our faith and our conscience.\par \par \uc2 That's what we have to take our country back again.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 MACCALUM: But you had not support -- you said you wouldn't support, I believe, correct me if I'm wrong, a six-week federal ban if it were to go into place. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has said that, you know, you are too moderate on this issue.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: That's not what I said. What I said is be honest with the American people. The only way a federal ban will pass is if you have a majority of the House, 60 Senate votes and a signature of a president.\par \par \uc2 We haven't had 60 senators in over 100 years. We may have 45 pro-life senators. So, instead of demonizing this issue, the fellows just don't know how to talk about it.\par \par \uc2 Instead of demonizing this issue --\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HALEY: You have to humanize this issue and understand that everybody has a story. Our overall goal should be how do we save as many babies as possible and support as many moms as possible. That way you take away all the divisions. Democrats have used fear in women when it comes to this issue. Republicans have used judgment.\par \par \uc2 This is too personal of an issue to use fear or judgment. We need to talk about it in a way that's saving babies and supporting moms. And whatever 60 senators bring to me at whatever level, we will support because the only way we're going to do it is if we find consensus on the federal level.\par \par \uc2 And I think we will find consensus on banning late term abortions. I think we'll find consensus on expanding adoption and good quality adoptions. I think we'll find consensus that doctors and nurses who don't believe in abortion shouldn't have to perform them.\par \par \uc2 I think we'll find consensus on the fact that contraception should be accessible. And I think we'll find consensus that no state law should say to a woman that gets an abortion that she's going to jail or getting the death penalty. That's where we will find consensus.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right. Terry (ph) -- Terry is a retired farmer from Dallas County. He -- have you made your decision?\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE MEMBER: I've narrowed it down to the candidates that we have seen here in Iowa that speak from the heart rather than a teleprompter written by somebody else.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: OK.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: And who are those candidates?\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Yes, who's that?\par \par \uc2 TERRY: Who are the candidates?\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes. Who are you narrowed down to?\par \par \uc2 TERRY: One is standing on stage right now, smiling, speaking from the heart.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Well, what's your question for the governor?\par \par \uc2 TERRY: And I've heard DeSantis, I've liked him, I've liked Vivek. But I'm a proud grandpa. I know you're a proud mom. Let's talk about education.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TERRY: So, tell me what differs you from the others that gets us back to -- from the other candidates in the Republican Party, that gets us back to reading, writing, and arithmetic rather than guns and fentanyl?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: What worries me about education is, right now in America, only 31 percent of 8th graders in our country are proficient in reading. Only 27 percent of 8th graders are proficient in math. If we don't do something and do something quickly, we're going to be in a world of hurt 10 years from now.\par \par \uc2 And remember when I told you we wanted to take those federal programs and send them down to the state level? That includes education. We need to make sure we go back to the basics. We've got to make sure that our kids are learning reading, writing, history, science, math, arts, and that's it. We don't need to get these federal programs.\par \par \uc2 And what happened is when they started to get it too big with federal, we've seen it from Common Core, we saw it with No Child Left Behind, they became bigger things that got away from the basics of education.\par \par \uc2 When you send this down to the states, the resources that the states have, they can decide where they need to go. So, for example, I want to put vocational classes back in our high schools. We need to teach our kids how to be a part of the economy before they get out of school. Vocational classes in Iowa would be very different than vocational classes in South Carolina. Let the states decide that.\par \par \uc2 When you go and you look at these other things that the -- that D.C. has decided are good for our states, that's the problem. What I want to make sure of is that when we move those programs down, we make it more state centric.\par \par \uc2 Secondly, we should have complete transparency in the classroom. No parent should ever wonder what their child is learning in the classroom. Every syllabus should be online for every parent to see. And every parent should choose where their child goes to school and what mode of education they have. Because a parent knows best.\par \par \uc2 And finally, I will say, we have to grow strong girls in this country. And strong girls become strong women. Strong women become strong leaders. And none of that happens if we have biological boys playing in girls' sports. We've got to cut that out.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Thank you, Governor.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Let's bring in Steph Harold (ph), who is retired from West Des Moines. Hi, Steph. Let's get a microphone over to you. There we go.\par \par \uc2 STEPH HAROLD (PH): Hello, Ambassador.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Hi, Steph.\par \par \uc2 STEPH HAROLD (PH): And please thank your husband for his service.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 STEPH HAROLD (PH): I am very excited that you are wanting to bring up and tackle term limits. Exactly how do you propose to do this, since I can't imagine that most in Congress would want to shorten their stay.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: It's very true. You know, not only do I want to see term limits, I want to see mental competency tests for anyone over the age of 75. And I'm not being disrespectful when I say that. We all know people over 75 that would run circles around us. Senator Grassley is a perfect example of that. But then we know \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And right now, Congress has become the most privileged nursing home in the country. These are people making decisions on our national security. These are people making decisions on the future of our economy. We need to know they're at the top of their game.\par \par \uc2 And yes, I'm a strong advocate for term limits. The way we would deal with that, no Congress isn't going to vote on it. So, we're going to build them up to it. I will have a Haley term limits pledge that everyone needs to sign when they decide to run for office, incumbent or otherwise. And we will find out where they are on term limits. And then, I'm going to give that information to the American people so that you know to ask that elected official about it and you know where they stand.\par \par \uc2 And then, when we get enough term limit pledges into Congress, that's when we will go and vote on it to make sure that we get term limits back in D.C. We will do it from the outside in, rather than the inside out.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right. Governor, thank you. Well, we're going to take a quick break right here. And when we come back, we will talk about the future of America. A lot to talk about.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: A lot to talk about. We'll be right back with more.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Welcome back to an exciting, snowy night here in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 We are in the town hall with Republican presidential candidate Nikki Haley. Welcome back, everybody.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Governor, there's a number of states that are looking to take former President Trump off the ballot. The Supreme Court is going to try to hear this, possibly decide it.\par \par \uc2 What do you think about that? Should he be taken off the ballot? How do you think the Supreme Court will be receiving that?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: No, he shouldn't be taken off the ballot, and the Supreme Court needs to rule quickly, before other states start to do this.\par \par \uc2 This is one of those don't open a door if you don't want to see what happens. This is a door we don't need to open. I will defeat President Trump fair and square. I don't need anybody throwing him off the ballot to do it.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HALEY: But this started back with COVID. The idea that you have people telling people what to do, how to think, what to -- how to live, all of that. That's wrong. If they can do this to him, they'll do it to someone else. We can't have others saying, I don't think he should be on the ballot. I think Americans can decide on their own whether they want him to be on the ballot or not.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Let's go to David (ph), who is retired and from sales management. He is from Des Moines. And you are deciding, I believe, between Trump and Haley, is that right?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED: Right. I think I'm going to out myself here right at the beginning by saying I voted for Trump in 2016 and 2020.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Me too.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED: Thank you for the opportunity. Governor Haley, I've heard you say many, many times you agreed with a lot of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's policies. You actually like some of them. It was all of the rest of the stuff that goes along with him that was the issue. Can you name two or three of his policies that you would consider bringing back and re-implementing should you be elected president?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Well, I think what we saw with President Trump, and -- and I think - - when I say he was the right president at the right time, he was good at breaking things, right? But now we need somebody to fix them. Because that was the problem. Yes, he -- he said that...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HALEY: You know, you look at the fact that he said that he was going to go deal with the border, but he never quite got there. We need to fix it now and make sure that we stop the flow. You know, when you look at what happened with education, he called things out, but we actually need to take it back to the basics and get all of the strings off of education so that we're focusing on our kids. When you look at what's happening, you know, with law enforcement, let's bring law and order back to our country.\par \par \uc2 But I think what he did do was he had a strength when it came to how to deal with countries abroad. That was important. The problem is, again, he didn't follow-through with China. He allowed us to get these Chinese police stations. He let there be a Chinese spy base to go off our shores in Cuba. He didn't do anything about the fentanyl flow.\par \par \uc2 So it's like he broke it but he never finished it. He never fixed it. Now is the time we have to fix things. And that's why we need a new generational leader that's not going to focus on the past, which is what he and Biden both are doing. We need someone who's going to focus on the solutions of the future so that we can start getting things back on track.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, David (ph), what do you think about that answer? Does it -- does it, you know, persuade you either way or on the fence still?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED: He certainly broke things.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED: And I -- and I would say there is still a need for things to be broken. For example, today the president of Mexico was giving a list of demands to the -- to Biden about what we needed to do to get him to play ball with us. It didn't go that way with Trump. It was just the opposite.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: No. And you know what we would do on that? We would go to the president of Mexico and say, OK, if that's how you are going to be, then, no, you're not getting the 250 million in aid that you're getting right now.\par \par \uc2 The problem -- the reason Mexico is doing that, everybody smells blood in the water. Everybody smells weakness. And what I will tell you, at the \uc2 U.N.\uc2  I did one thing. I put a book together and I put all 193 countries. The second column was a percentage of times they voted with the U.S. and against the U.S. And the third column was how much foreign aid we gave them. I gave it to President Trump. And I said, quit trying to buy friends. Quit paying off enemies. We have to start being strategic.\par \par \uc2 Last year they gave Iraq money. They gave Belarus, who is holding hands with Russia, money. They gave Cuba, who we named a state sponsor of terrorism, money. They gave Zimbabwe, the most anti-American African country there is. We gave China money. How weak do we look? When I am president we will no longer give money to countries that hate America.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Governor Haley, thank you very much. This has been very instructive. Some great questions from Iowa voters. Did the governor sway some of you?\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Some of you? OK. We will see. We have a couple of town halls to come. We will be following you as you head towards next Monday and the caucuses. Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for watching our town hall with Republican presidential candidate Nikki Haley.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes, it's been great having everyone here. And for those of you who are undecided, if you want to come back, we have two more nights that we are in town here. We'll be here almost all week. So you're welcome to come back and join us for \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  tomorrow night and for former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Wednesday night.\par \par \uc2 It's exciting that people are making these decisions as we get to -- close to this. So we look forward to both of those this week.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: And this is the beginning of the process. Iowa is number one. And I was out and about talking to voters today that are going to caucus. And I said, are you worried about the snow? Are you worried about the cold? And they said, suck it up. It's Iowa.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: We're going to manage to get there no matter what. So we'll be there, too, bouncing around the state until next Monday.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: We sure will. We're doing shows from here all week. And we look forward to you joining us for those as the voters of America begin to speak. Because we talk a lot about the polls, as Governor Haley said, but now people will have their voices heard. And we will see what they have to say from Iowa.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for joining us, everybody.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Thank you, Des Moines.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FNSPBB0020240109ek1800001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court To Hear Trump Colorado Appeal; Biden Excoriates Trump Over Capitol Riot And Rhetoric; Biden White House Touts December Jobs Report; Trump Holds Iowa Rallies In Effort To Cement Lead; ISIS Claims Responsibility While Iran Blames United States; United States Silent On Responsibility For Gaza Rehabilitation; Oscar Pistorius Released On Parole After Serving Part Of His Sentence For Murdering Reeva Steenkamp; Representatives \uc2 Mike Bost\uc2  (R-IL) And \uc2 Mark Takano\uc2  (R-CA) Interviewed On Bipartisan Efforts To Provide Help To U.S. Veterans Contemplating Suicide; President Biden Launches Reelection Campaign By Characterizing Former President Trump As Threat To U.S. Democracy; Record Number Of Migrants Cross U.S. Southern Border In December Of 2023\b0\par\par\uc2 Gillian Turner, Shannon Bream, Jacqui Heinrich, Mark Meredith,  Jennifer Griffin, Alex Hogan, Greg Palkot, Casey Stegall, Bret Baier \par \uc2 7,987 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 January 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Special Report with Brett Baier\par \uc2 FNSPBB\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: So, they can't prosecute. Right?\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Oh, driver with car.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes, California.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And then, they voted afterwards.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes. Yes, that's right.\par \par \uc2 That's it for us. Have a great night. I want to thank everyone for being with us. We have four more seconds. Anything you want to say, Jesse?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I love you, America.\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Oh.\par \par \uc2 GILLIAN TURNER, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: Good evening and welcome to Washington. I'm Gillian Turner, in for Bret Baier.\par \par \uc2 "BREAKING TONIGHT", the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  is keeping former President Trump's name on the Colorado ballot for now. This, after the state's Supreme Court ruled him ineligible.\par \par \uc2 Now, the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  will review that decision removing his eligibility in a politically charged constitutional fight that's got major implications for the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Fox News chief legal correspondent and anchor of "FOX NEWS SUNDAY" Shannon Bream joins me now. Good evening, Shannon.\par \par \uc2 SHANNON BREAM, FOX NEWS CHANNEL ANCHOR: All right. So, Gillian, good to see you tonight.\par \par \uc2 For the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 , we consider this moving at lightning speed. Arguments will be held on this case, February 8th. Based on what just happened, the justice is formally getting involved. Colorado will include President Trump's name on the primary ballot, because the secretary of state had made clear that today is the deadline for her to certify the names for the ballot.\par \par \uc2 And she would do so unless the Supreme Court upheld the Colorado Supreme Court's ruling or declined to take the case. They are taking the case. So, that means President Trump's name stays on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 So, why did the High Court get involved? Well, likely because there are numerous other states considering the same issues under the 14th Amendment with Maine's Secretary of State already indicating, by the way, citing the Colorado decision that she thinks Maine should keep him off the ballot there as well.\par \par \uc2 In urging the court to take up the case this week, the Trump legal team argued that allowing the Colorado decision to stand with disenfranchise millions of voters, adding, that "If allowed to stand, it would mark the first time in the history of the United States that the judiciary has prevented voters from casting ballots for the leading major-party presidential candidate."\par \par \uc2 Now, the group opposing President Trump's name being on the Colorado ballot also argued to the Supreme Court, saying this, that the state made the right decision, "Based on the facts found by the trial court, Trump's intentionally mobilizing, and citing, and encouraging an armed mob to attack the United States Capitol on January 6th, satisfies the legal definition of engaging in insurrection."\par \par \uc2 We'd expect a decision from the Supreme Court within weeks, maybe even days. Once again, the Supreme Court hears those arguments February 8th, Gillian.\par \par \uc2 TURNER: Shannon, also, understand the court made an important decision on abortion today.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: They did. They are getting involved in a couple of cases out of Idaho. It comes down to this. Can hospitals there be forced by the Biden administration to perform abortions in emergency situations, even if the state has a near total ban on abortions, with an exception to save the life of the mother?\par \par \uc2 Arguments on that case will be held in April. In the meantime, the Idaho law will be totally in effect until then.\par \par \uc2 TURNER: All right. busy night for the court on a Friday. Shannon, thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 TURNER: Well, President Biden has thrown down the gauntlet against former President Trump, using his first campaign speech of the year earlier today to offer a dire warning about a possible second Trump term.\par \par \uc2 Biden accused the former president of sacrificing U.S. democracy in the interest of his own political power. Striking a decisively different tone than his 2020 message centering on unity.\par \par \uc2 The political address comes on the heels of the anniversary of the January 6th Capitol riot.\par \par \uc2 White House correspondent Jacqui Heinrich has that story tonight from the North Lawn. Hi, Jacqui.\par \par \uc2 JACQUI HEINRICH, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: Good evening, Gillian. President Biden is making the case that America's answer to January 6th, 2020 won't come until November 2024, the first election since.\par \par \uc2 His message is Trump's past attempts to hold on to power have democracy hanging by a thread.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's campaign is about him. Not America, not you.\par \par \uc2 HEINRICH (voice over): The opening salvo to President Biden's 2024 campaign was not about conjuring voter excitement over a second term agenda, but calling up fear about what could happen if he doesn't win.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: He's willing to sacrifice our democracy, put himself in power.\par \par \uc2 HEINRICH (voice over): Biden detailed Trump's effort to overturn his 2020 laws in the courts. And then, his failure to call off the violent mob of supporters who tried to stop Congress from certifying the election.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Was among the worst dereliction of duty by a president in American history.\par \par \uc2 HEINRICH (voice over): Biden appealed to voters of all parties to reject Trump as a threat to democracy, assailing Trump for loading those riders as patriots and likening him to Hitler.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Echoing the same exact language used in Nazi Germany. He went onto say, he'd be a dictator on day one.\par \par \uc2 HEINRICH (voice over): The \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  says, "While families can't pay their bills, children are dying from fentanyl overdoses, terror suspects are crossing the open southern border. Biden wants to further divide Americans with polarize