ur years and being prosecuted and persecuted.\par \par \uc2 What they're doing to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is unprecedented. You've covered it. We know that. We don't want that for any president, any president, let alone we don't want to set that precedent two different things.\par \par \uc2 So what I argue is not for President Trump, it's for all presidents, it's for the executive branch. We have to have them be able to govern this country in a way without being fear of somebody saying you defamed me, you put me in jail for the wrong reason. You were an insurrectionist when you were ask -- actually just asking for election integrity, actually asking for us to take a close examination to preserve American Constitution and democracy. That's what President Trump has done.\par \par \uc2 And presidential immunity is very important. It's never been questioned because nobody's ever been prosecuted like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but I'm excited for the Supreme Court to look at that as well. I think they're going to have to. I think that it's a very clean cut. Again, I think that it's important.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Do you think -- and I mentioned this early, how President Trump seems to defy all, you know, conventional political gravity. And in other words, with every pile on, every new charge, it seems to help him in the polls. What do you attribute that to?\par \par \uc2 HABBA: Derangeness, I hate to use his word, but it is.\par \par \uc2 Look, we've got a rogue prosecutor, Jack Smith. You mentioned it before I came on. Jack Smith is just ignoring a stay motion. He's filing motions despite the fact that they said there is a stay. That is a complete disrespect to the order of law, and the rule of law, and that is why his poll numbers go up.\par \par \uc2 The American people are not stupid. They're afraid and they're going to put their votes behind Trump because of it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, it's going to be interesting to watch the timeline line now unfold as the Supreme Court did not step in to expedite that case. We'll see how that works its way through the courts.\par \par \uc2 Alina, we'll be getting updates from you probably throughout the year. Thanks for being with us. Happy New Year.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, zero experience Hunter, guess what, he's on to his next endeavor this, time he's off to Hollywood. We'll explain. We get reaction from Pam Bondi, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. No experience \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and the guy described as his sugar brother Kevin Morris, they apparently are onto the next scheme. The Hollywood lawyer is now reportedly backing a documentary about the first son and has quietly had cameras following Hunter for years. Now, according to "The L.A. Times", the film will show Hunter painting, spending time with his family, living life as a sober adult amid his legal battles, which will be a slightly different film than the content found on Hunter's laptop.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, former Florida Attorney General Pam Bondi.\par \par \uc2 We could just get permission and run that. I think it would probably do a lot better at the box office, just my guess though. What do you make of this arrangement?\par \par \uc2 PAM BONDI (R), FORMER FLORIDA ATTORNEY GENERAL: Well, you know, he needs to tread very carefully. Sean, because everything he says can be used against him. It sounds like this is just another pathetic attempt by the left, by the liberals to help minimize charges, very serious charges against \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and everything \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  does has a lot of money attached to it.\par \par \uc2 So, now, we know Hunter Picasso Biden wants to be a movie star in Hollywood and he'd probably win an Oscar for it because he's going to have to tell a lot of fibs to get out of everything that he's done. It's really shocking that they're actually filming him, because none of this is privileged.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay. So, Joe, we know you know, bragged about taking official action, demanding the firing of a prosecutor, so his son that admitted in his own work he had no experience in energy, gas, oil, Ukraine could be paid millions at a time when he was admittedly addicted to drugs.\par \par \uc2 Now, Democrats in the House are trying to compare the fact that, well, some people from foreign countries, 20 foreign countries stayed at Trump's hotel in Washington, D.C., as if that is the equivalent. Well, number one, there's actually a service that was provided, a hotel room. Number two, I tend to doubt that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  got a daily list of who is staying in the \uc2 Trump Hotels\uc2 , but that's the argument now, oh they're trying to muddy the waters and say, see, oh, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was colluding with China and all these other countries, I can hear it now.\par \par \uc2 What's your response to that?\par \par \uc2 BONDI: Yeah, yeah, I can hear it now, too. Not even close though, Sean. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is one of the most accomplished entrepreneurs in our country, in our history of our country, and \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is a drug addict. Yeah, legitimate businesses from all over the world and countries, stayed at the Trump properties because they are spectacular. \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  was a drug addict, he couldn't even speak any other language, yet he's getting paid multi-millions of dollars. The Biden family received multi-million dollar payments from our enemies, from many countries who are considered our enemies, not even close.\par \par \uc2 But, again, Sean, that's how the left manipulates everything, and they will continue to manipulate it. But I know the American people are seeing through it and I think they're sick and tired of it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, I think they're tired of it. Do you think that muddies the waters? Because the media that showed no interest in Hunter, no experience, Joe taking action that benefited his son, all of a sudden, they're interested, oh, a hotel room was rented to a Chinese national. Will they be successful in muddying the waters? We have about seconds.\par \par \uc2 BONDI: Absolutely not, Sean. They will not be successful. Again, the American people are seeing through it. What \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  did was he was not qualified and took millions of dollars from foreign countries.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Pam Bondi, thank you. Happy New Year.\par \par \uc2 All right. Unfortunately, that's all the time we have left this evening. As always, thank you for being with us, and making the show possible. Please set your DVR so you never, ever, ever miss an episode of HANNITY.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, let not your heart be troubled -- by the way, broadcasting from the free state of Florida, our new broadcast home. Let not your heart be troubled, Greg Gutfeld is next. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020240105ek1400001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  Is A Failed President\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Mike Pompeo, Sara Carter \par \uc2 8,014 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 January 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to "Hannity" and happy New Year and happy election year 2024.\par \par \uc2 Now, the exodus out of big states like New Jersey, California, Illinois, New York, it continues. In fact, tonight, we are now broadcasting from my new home, the great free state of Florida.\par \par \uc2 Like so many Americans, I left New York for good, and am now in the state with, let's see, warmer weather, law and order, better education, more freedom, better quality of life and guess what? No state income tax.\par \par \uc2 Now, here is my prediction, this mass migration out of deep blue states like the ones I just me mentioned, that will continue unless and until the change -- they change their governing philosophies that are overtaxing people, over-regulating people. They're underperforming in schools and safety and issues of public importance, and that's why it's happening.\par \par \uc2 But no matter what state you call home, I will say this, 2024 is going to be a critical year not only for our country but for the world. As anyone who has lived in New York will tell you -- yeah, elections have consequences and in just 11 short months and they will fly by, you the American people, you will determine the future of our country and frankly the trajectory of the world.\par \par \uc2 Now, no one can predict the outcome, but I can tell you what the next year will look like. And by the way, anyone that does predict the outcome, they don't know what they're talking about. It's too unpredictable, probably the most unpredictable presidential election year in our lifetimes.\par \par \uc2 Now, Democrats, the media mob, they will work in unison, that I can predict with certainty. They will be on a never-ending, non-stop smear campaign, regardless of the Republican candidate. They will obsessively focus on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , January 6th, January 6th, and, of course, abortion.\par \par \uc2 They don't want to talk about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's accomplishments. Why? Because there really aren't any. They won't defend Biden's radical agenda because it has resulted in one national disaster after another, and you, the American people, you can see it. They don't want to talk about Bidenomics because, what, two-thirds of our fellow countrymen are living paycheck to paycheck, and the American people are getting wrecked by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's economy, of inflation, high interest rates.\par \par \uc2 They don't want to talk about Biden's performance on the world stage. Why? Because the president has been bullied over and over and over again by our top geopolitical foes as Joe has abdicated America's role on the world stage.\par \par \uc2 The world is paying a consequence. We see China openly planning an invasion or what they call reunification, it's an invasion of our ally Taiwan, while harassing our military in the Pacific, both in international airways and international waterways, spying on our nuclear sites right here in the continental United States with a slow moving spy balloon that it turns out they knew all about on top of all the intellectual property theft, all of their unfair trade practices.\par \par \uc2 We now see war in Europe as Russia invaded Ukraine, and war continues there and it seems like there's no end in sight.\par \par \uc2 Biden has utterly failed to deter what is one of the bloodiest conflicts in recent history, and of course, we have Iran, the number one state sponsor of terror. They are enriching uranium at the fastest pace ever, all while directing proxy wars and other proxies to attack Americans and our allies all over the region. Now we have war in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 On U.S. troops, there have been 118 specific attacks, including five in the New Year. Even the Houthi rebels, a radical group formed from Yemen, by the way, funded by the Iranians, they're using fishing boats and rifles to wreak havoc on important shipping channels in the Red Sea, all while \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  does little to nothing to respond.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, our southern border, it is worse than ever. We have a lot more on that coming up tonight.\par \par \uc2 And, of course, crime is completely totally spiraling out of several -- out of control of many major American cities and even some small towns.\par \par \uc2 And to put that special cherry on top, yeah, tax collection is now at an all-time high and with the extra two plus trillion dollars Biden added to the debt last year -- well, we started this fiscal year in October with the national debt now more than $34 trillion. That is a record and I don't know how we pay that back.\par \par \uc2 So make no mistake, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is your president, has been and continues to be an abject failure, both at home and abroad. Don't expect to see much of Joe by the way in the lead-up to November. In fact, he will campaign probably less than any other candidate in modern history.\par \par \uc2 If \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or any Republican is the candidate, I even doubt he'll show up for one debate. He will lurk in the shadows, he will hide in the basement, he will hide on the beach in Delaware while the media mob does all the heavy lifting for him. Now, it's not even clear that Joe can do the lifting at all at this point.\par \par \uc2 Even the most basic conversations are now really difficult for your commander-in chief, and here's just the latest and greatest. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Mr. President, before we start here about the New Year, I'm curious what sort of holiday foods have you been enjoying over the last few days. \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Well, I've been eating everything is put in front of me. I've eaten pasta which I love. Eating a lot of chicken, chicken parmesan, I've been eating all Italian foods basically.\par \par \uc2 JILL BIDEN, FIRST LADY: And ice cream.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT BIDEN: And ice cream, chocolate chip ice cream.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Mr. President, what's New Years resolution, sir?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: To come back next year.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Anything else?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: That's the biggest one right now.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's cognitive ability is not good. Anyone with eyes to see, you can see it. Every week it gets worse and it's getting worse by the day. Now keep in mind, Biden is also dealing with very real and serious corruption and bribery allegations, along with a very real impeachment inquiry. And his image as a loving father and grandfather -- well, that has forever been shattered and tarnished by frankly his disgusting treatment of his own four-year-old granddaughter in Arkansas. In other words, there are almost endless reasons to dislike \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  both politically and personally.\par \par \uc2 And now, according to Gallup, Biden's year-end approval rating is now lower than any other first-term president in modern history going into a, quote, reelection year. He's even losing support among very key demographics a big part of what is the Democratic coalition, that which, quote, propelled him to victory in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Look at this new "USA Today"/Suffolk University poll. Only 63 percent of African-American voters support \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Why is that significant? Well, that's down from 87 percent that he was receiving in 2020, and it only gets worse from there. Biden now trails Trump among Hispanic voters by five points after easily winning a majority in 2020.\par \par \uc2 And get this, Biden is down four points with another key constituency among the Democratic base and that is voters under 35, a usually very reliable Democratic voting bloc. If these numbers hold, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  if there's if he's their candidate for reelection he will lose today in a landslide. But a lot can happen between now and November, let's be very clear.\par \par \uc2 So let me start this year with a warning to conservatives and to Republicans. If you want any chance of winning in November, you need to do a couple of fundamental basic things. One, any conservative any Republican any voter that has any reluctance or any resistance to voting by mail and voting early, you have to get over that. You just can't start out these races on election night down by hundreds of thousands of votes and depend on people voting day of to make it up.\par \par \uc2 Also, many states that allow legal ballot harvesting, key word legal, and Republicans, they need to start matching the very, very well-organized Democratic Party efforts. That would be critical. GOP organizers in every state need to do it, especially the swing states, they've got to adopt, what is a robust operation that is -- basically puts them on a level playing field, and working within the system, not the one you want, it's not the system I want.\par \par \uc2 I want day of voting Election Day to be a natural -- a national holiday and I want paper ballots, that's not going to happen, and I want voter ID and I want partisan observers watching the voting all day and the vote counting all night. In a perfect world, that would be what happens, but it's not the reality. That is not our current reality. Republicans, you have to deal with the system, the hand you dealt, not the one you wish you had.\par \par \uc2 My last piece of advice is on the controversial issue of abortion -- not my moral point of view but I'm looking at it politically. Now, first, leave abortion to the states. That's what Roe v. Wade did, and that I believe is more constitutional. If Republicans -- if you want to push restrictive bans on abortion, like, for example, \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  running for governor in Pennsylvania, no restrictions, rape, incest, mother's life, he lost by a margin of like 16 points, that had not been seen in Pennsylvania history since the 1940s against a non-incumbent opponent. You'll pay a heavy political price.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, you'll have no ability to even stop late term abortions that many Democrats support. You can get the high ground on the issue. Look at Ohio, that is a state that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won twice by a very comfortable margin. Voters overwhelmingly approved a measure to make abortion a constitutional right in that red state. That ought to tell you a lot about the issue of abortion.\par \par \uc2 GOP candidates, you need to be smart about this because in 11 months, you have a prime opportunity to regain power in D.C. and get our country back on track before it's too late.\par \par \uc2 Anyway here now with more, South Dakota Governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  is with us.\par \par \uc2 Governor, great to have you back. Happy new year.\par \par \uc2 GOV. KRISTI NOEM (R), SOUTH DAKOTA: Oh, happy New Year, Sean. You're in Florida, in a beautiful state, but the news is still bad. We still have \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as our president and the country is in trouble.\par \par \uc2 So I'm in Iowa this week talking to folks and having those conversations about those critical issues that you were just discussing.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, let's talk about -- let's talk about what I'm saying about reluctance and resistance to voting early, voting by mail. That's not the system I want. I don't think it is the system that has the most integrity, that would give us the most confidence and results. However, it's the system we're living with. It'll be the system in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Do you agree with me that conservatives and Republicans need to get over reluctance and resistance towards early voting and voting by mail?\par \par \uc2 NOEM: Absolutely. If it's your state law, then you need to use the law to make sure that you can be victorious and get the right man in the White House that can fix the problems in this country.\par \par \uc2 Listen, we've seen, Sean what secretary of states will do. Look at what happened in these two states in our country where these secretary of states, the chief election officers, broke the Constitution to remove \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  off the ballot and another one spoke out in support of her.\par \par \uc2 So the Democrats will do anything to win. They don't care about the Constitution. They don't care about law and order. They don't care about our election laws. We do -- we have integrity. We're going to use this system to our highest performance level and run it with excellence so that we can win.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me talk about the issue of abortion and I'm not asking you about your own personal view. I happen to be pro-life, believe in the sanctity of life. I donate to a group preborn.com, because I believe in their mission. They use the science of ultrasound to convince expecting moms, they give them free ultrasounds, to choose life.\par \par \uc2 But on the political side, where do you stand politically? Because I believe politically, probably, the country, poll after poll that I read, is probably a first trimester, 15 weeks was -- which was the Dobbs decision. Nobody that even says they're pro-choice likes or supports late term abortion which many Democrats do.\par \par \uc2 What is your position there?\par \par \uc2 NOEM: You know what bothers me so much, Sean, is that people aren't even having these conversations. They're not even talking about it and avoiding it, which causes the public not to trust them.\par \par \uc2 So I think that at the federal level, that that certainly is where the public is landing, absolutely. And the issue is that us as leaders, we don't get to be dictators. We follow the public and the public opinion. I get to have personal views and I advocate for policies. But at the end of the day, the voters decide and they decide what the laws are.\par \par \uc2 And so, that's one of the things that we as conservatives mess up so often is we don't have the conversations. We talk like crazy people and then we never get the chance to actually govern, and we need to be a little smarter and wiser in how we have these conversations and let people know that we -- we care about these families, we care about mothers, we care about their health, that in South Dakota, we've started a website that is all about how we can come alongside and support women in these situations that are unplanned.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah. Any other advice you would offer, unprompted by me?\par \par \uc2 NOEM: Well, I think that that Americans need to start sitting down and having conversations, and that -- you know, conservatives can't shy away from these issues. So, you know, that's what I think that they're having lots of different debates. Roe v. Wade changed everything in this country, put the conversation at the state level.\par \par \uc2 My state law looks very different than what is in place in Florida or Illinois or any other state. If there's a decision that's made at the congressional level, the public will be weighing in on this election cycle and that that is what with the leaders will follow.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, all right. Governor Noem, great to see you.\par \par \uc2 By the way, you have a great jobs program. You've now got thousands of people that you're incentivizing to go to South Dakota. That's a tribute to you. Even -- even people that become apprent -- get an apprenticeship or making 80 grand a year by moving to your state. That's a great program.\par \par \uc2 Thank you, Governor. Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 NOEM: It's fantastic.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. According to a new poll, many Americans seem stunned by the president's lack of action overseas, as American troops are targeted now almost daily. Now, recently, the \uc2 U.S. Navy\uc2 , they did sink three little baby Houthi rebel speedboats in the Red Sea after coming under attack. But so far, the commander-in-chief has done little to counter this aggression.\par \par \uc2 Now, Iran, they're sending a warship to the region. And meanwhile, just a few weeks after their meeting in California -- well, China's dictator once again threatened what he calls reunification of Taiwan. We would call that an invasion.\par \par \uc2 The Biden White House doesn't seem to care. We have war in Europe. That continues with no end in sight. Now, we're in the Middle East and all my sources tell me \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is saying one thing publicly about Israel and very different things privately.\par \par \uc2 Here with analysis, FOX News contributor, former Secretary of State \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 You know, Mr. Secretary, I look at the world situation, I don't care if it's Europe, Ukraine, Russia, I look at this new axis of evil -- China, Russia, Iran -- as probably the biggest threat since the Cold War and I think they're more embolden than ever just based on their actions. What are you seeing?\par \par \uc2 MIKE POMPEO\uc2 , FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Sean, first of all, happy New Year. I think your analysis is exactly right. What we saw happen on October 7th, what we saw happen in Afghanistan where 13 Americans killed, the Chinese spy balloon -- these things are all connected by dictators, authoritarian regimes that do not fear the United States of America, that President Biden has allowed such an accelerated rate of decay of our deter that we had built up in the four years that President Trump and I were serving has really done the American people disservice, and it is dangerous. It's dangerous not only for the Israelis and for folks in the Middle East, but it's dangerous for folks here in the United States of America as well.\par \par \uc2 A wide open southern border and a North Korean leader, a Chinese leader, a Russian leader who don't think that the United States will stand up and defend its most sacred values is a place that is a very dangerous country here at home as well.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So when President Xi just recently spoke in the last week or so about reunification with Taiwan, that to me, he said it before, but this time it feels more real, feels more real to me because if in fact that is his geopolitical ambition or it's going to happen while Biden's president. That means he got -- he has at least -- they have in their mind about a year to get it done.\par \par \uc2 I predict that's probably going to happen. I hope I'm wrong but I think I'm going to be proven right.\par \par \uc2 POMPEO: Sean, I hope you're wrong too, and it's not a independent variable. We have the capacity to deter Xi Jinping,, to demonstrate our resolve to show that we -- just as we'll provide all the ammunition, weapons, missiles that the Israelis need to defend their homeland, just as we should be providing what the Ukrainians have asked for to defend their homeland from the invasion by \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , we need to make clear that we're not going to allow Xin Jinping to steal our property here at home.\par \par \uc2 We're not going to allow him to run spy rings, spy balloons against the United States on our own soil, and we're not going to let him take over an independent and free Taiwan by force in the Pacific. It'll be a very, very dangerous thing for all of us, whether that's the Hawaiian Islands, Alaska, Guam, all of these places.\par \par \uc2 When you pick up the map and see what he's doing in Taiwan, make no mistake about it, Xi Jinping's intentions aren't limited to what he calls the reunification. You properly described as the takeover of Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What do you make of the advancement of the Iranian nuclear program and they're sending a warship to basically, seemingly help out the hoodie rebels, and they've been using those rebels to fight a proxy war against Saudi Arabia, and they're even -- the Houthi rebels are firing missiles into Israel also, so that's another front in the Israeli conflict.\par \par \uc2 You know, is that not a bold move by the Iranians to send that warship there?\par \par \uc2 POMPEO: Sean, remember, the history of this administration in the Obama administration with Iran, they have -- they have emboldened the Iranian regime they've provided them $6 billion in exchange for six American hostages, there are now more Americans held by the Iranians after that than there were before, we released that $6 billion.\par \par \uc2 Now, this is all Iranian-driven. The Israelis have at least a three front, maybe as many as a five front war underway today, it's not something that's in the future -- or might happen if there's an escalation, if we don't impose real costs on the Iranian regime, we're coming up on the 4th Anniversary of when we took out Soleimani. It's on January 3rd.\par \par \uc2 If we don't impose real costs on the Iranian regime, if we just keep taking out dinghies and firing at empty warehouses in Syria, the Iranians will feel emboldened, empowered and they will not only continue to attack Israel, but they'll attack Middle Eastern countries, and I fear that they will do things here in the homeland as well.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Do you ever think you'd see this much antisemitism in the halls of Congress, on college universities? You know, just in the past week at the site of the World Trade Center where 9/11/01, we lost, you know, two -- that day we lost 2,977 Americans and they were actually shouting "Allahu Akhar". Australia, you had protesters shouting "gas the Jews", you see antisemitism rampant all across Europe.\par \par \uc2 It's beyond disturbing to me. How do you analyze it?\par \par \uc2 POMPEO: Yeah, no, I never -- I never thought I'd see this volume and this depth of activity. And then I never thought I'd see our central institutions, whether that's the United Nations or our universities so fail to understand this is black and white, this is good versus evil to allow this antisemitism to run rampant and then not to do anything about it is morally, morally indecent.\par \par \uc2 And I never thought I'd see that, Sean. I regret it. I hope that America can get find its way back. I'm confident that we will, but it's going to take real American leadership, not just from presidents of the United States but from each of us all across the country, making clear this is just unacceptable.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah. We do need people like you, we do need adults like you back in charge. I hope you're not busy in about a year or so. I think -- I think there's a big job waiting for you somewhere.\par \par \uc2 Secretary Pompeo, happy New Year, sir.\par \par \uc2 POMPEO: Thanks.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Coming up, Harvard president Claudine Gay has now finally stepped down. Congresswoman \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 , she reacts, she kind of made it happen.\par \par \uc2 Plus, where does Trump stand with the left's attempts to throw him off the ballot? We'll check in with Senator Ted Cruz, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. So after spending weeks embroiled in scandals, Harvard President Claudine Gay finally announced her resignation earlier today amid a growing number of plagiarism allegations, nearly one month after what was a disastrous testimony on antisemitism on Capitol Hill, what's going on on Harvard's campus, on Harvard's campus. She made the announcement in a pretty bitter letter that she shared with students and colleagues.\par \par \uc2 No shock to me, but it should be shocking. She refused to apologize for all the disasters leading up to a resignation. No apology for her vile testimony before Congress on antisemitism or the allegations of rampant plagiarism throughout her academic career. Instead she just resorted to the left's favorite talking point, get used to it. You will hear it all year long. She played the race card.\par \par \uc2 Now, Congresswoman \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 , who pressed Claudine Gay during her testimony celebrated the news, calling this resignation long overdue.\par \par \uc2 And Congresswoman Stefanik joins us now with more.\par \par \uc2 You really do -- you exposed something that -- it was a moment that you don't see often in Congress. Three college presidents -- three of the most prestigious universities that gave the most appalling answer when you were asking a simple question about, you know, antisemitism. I'm surprised it took the charge of plagiarism to make this happen. What's your take?\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 ELISE STEFANIK\uc2  (R-NY): My take, Sean, is there is a reason that the testimony of the presidents of Harvard, Penn and MIT made history as the most viewed testimony ever, with over billion views, and that's because their testimony was morally bankrupt and pathetic.\par \par \uc2 My question was very simple. It was a moral question. Does calling for the genocide of Jews can ruin your school's code of conduct? Does go against your school's code of conduct? And every single one said it depended upon the context.\par \par \uc2 We know it does not depend on the context. It should be condemned. It is not that difficult to say that, yet, all three failed abysmally and the world saw it.\par \par \uc2 It is unacceptable that it took Harvard a month to demand the resignation of Claudine Gay. Penn made the right decision immediately, but this is after it was forced in front of the world to see. And I believe these university presidents sit a top these institutions that have rotted out and have institutionalized antisemitism, particularly after \uc2 Hamas\uc2 's terrorist attack against Israel in early October. We've seen Jewish students assaulted, physically harassed and facing just vile attacks every single day.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, let me ask you this. If -- if it didn't violate the code of contact -- code of conduct, and it depends on context, would they apply that standard -- would they have answered the question the same way if it was clearly something said that was racist, misogynist, xenophobic, transphobic -- would they give -- would they have given you the same answer? I suspect the answer is no, they wouldn't say -- well, it depends on the context.\par \par \uc2 STEFANIK: They would not have -- they would not have, Sean, and that's why it was so pathetic, and it was so clear for everyone who saw that, how wrong that testimony was.\par \par \uc2 And I will tell you, what you can't see in the video that has now been viewed over billion times is there were Jewish students from each of those universities who were at that congressional hearing. And as I was listening to their responses to my question the university presidents, Jewish students you could see them shaking just of the abysmal lack of moral leadership. And then on top of this, you've seen just the shredding of academic integrity in Harvard's case, where it was very clear with this intense scrutiny that Claudine Gay was a plagiarist president, that she had plagiarized nearly 50 excerpts in her work, which is a very limited body of academic work when compared to other Harvard university presidents.\par \par \uc2 And I say this, as a Harvard graduate, I graduated from there, from undergrad with honors. And I will tell you, students -- if you plagiarized, you're expelled.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Congresswoman, take a bow. I think that was one of the best -- best moments that I've ever witnessed in terms of a congressman or woman out there, you know, being able to literally stump college university presidents on what was a layup question, and they deserve to get fired -- two down, one to go in my opinion. Thank you for being with us. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Now, tonight, former President Trump announced he is appealing Maine's Democratic secretary of state's unilateral decision to ban him from the ballot. Now, while the Colorado Republican Party has appealed Trump's ballot disqualification in their state, here with reaction, Texas Senator Ted Cruz.\par \par \uc2 Senator, first, you're -- you're a Harvard grad. I don't know how you feel about Claudine Gay, that's a separate issue.\par \par \uc2 Let -- let me ask you this. I always believed in the presumption of innocence, that you were innocent until proven guilty. Correct me if I'm wrong, I don't even know if you're going to use the 14th Amendment to keep Trump off the ballot. Has he ever even been accused of insurrection, even in any of the cases that have been brought against him? Because I don't rem -- recall seeing that.\par \par \uc2 SEN. TED CRUZ (R-TX): In no case in a court of law, he is, of course, accused of insurrection every day by Democrats on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and by media pundits. But insurrection is actually a formal crime defined in the United States code. And even Jack Smith, the wild-eyed partisan who is like Javert going after John Valjean in Les Mis, he wants to get Trump no matter what. Even Smith did not bring a charge of insurrection because the evidence doesn't remotely support it.\par \par \uc2 As you know, I do a podcast three days a week, "Verdict with Ted Cruz". Yesterday's podcast is entirely on the Colorado decision and the Maine's decisions. They are utterly insupportable. They are utterly lawless.\par \par \uc2 And my prediction is the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  will take the Colorado case, they will reverse it and, Sean, I think there's a real chance the Supreme Court will reverse it unanimously.\par \par \uc2 And it really does reveal the lie on the left, what the favorite phrase, the favorite slogan of Democrats today is we're saving democracy and, you know, nothing saves democracy like trying to stop the voters from voting for your opponents. I think the these cases show what utter hypocrites today's Democrats are.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It seems to me whether the Supreme Court wants to or not that they're going to have to get involved in a number of issues involving this election. I know they did not go along with Jack Smith's arguments in terms of expediting the ruling that should go to the appellate court in terms of presidential immunity. They're going to have to weigh in on something like this.\par \par \uc2 I can see a number of cases where they're not going to really have a choice. Do you see the same?\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: I -- perhaps, I think the one that they inevitably will take is the Colorado case, because that really goes to the heart of -- can you have judges preventing the voters from voting for one of the major two parties nominees, assuming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the nominee. And by the way, Colorado, they were trying to take him off the primary ballot.\par \par \uc2 I don't think the Supreme Court, I think they're going to reverse that quite easily. I think that decision is utterly lawless. The Maine decision is even more laughable and more and more we see in courts, we see at the Department of Justice, we see among elected Democrats, we see in the corporate media, they are motivated just by this overwhelming hatred of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and they're corrupted.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, I'll point out, this is also intertwined -- you were mentioning just a minute ago, Claudine Gay's resigning from Harvard. I think that was inevitable. It was the right decision, but a lot more needs to happen.\par \par \uc2 You look at Claudine Gay, she was a symptom of how our elite academic institutions have been thoroughly corrupted by cultural Marxism and you look at the testimony of the presidents of Penn, Harvard and MIT, as you mentioned, two down, one to go, president of Penn resigned, the president of Harvard resigns, the president of MIT needs to resign because our universities are so embracing cultural Marxism, they divide everyone into victims and oppressors and anything is justified on behalf of the victims against the oppressors.\par \par \uc2 It's why they can't stand up to antisemitism, but it's also why they hate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , because they view him as an oppressor and that's why they justify anything to go after him.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, let me ask you this -- I'm not so sure that had the plagiarism issue not followed up to the horrific comment -- to the horrific answer that \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2  was able to get out of these three presidents, I'm not sure she'd be gone today, and where I think the issue of her appalling comment on antisemitism, what should be -- should have been enough to get any college president fired.\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: Yeah. Well, the double standard on plagiarism was really galling, as Elise mentioned a minute ago. If you're a student at Harvard and you're guilty of plagiarism, you'll be expelled and that's one instance. With Claudine Gay, she had nearly 50 instances, "The New York Post" is reporting now that she's expected to still continue receiving her roughly million- dollar-a-year salary even though she has some instances of credible allegations of plagiary.\par \par \uc2 And nowhere in a resignation letter is a word of apology, nowhere in a resignation letter is a word of acknowledging what she did wrong, nowhere in \uc2 Harvard Corporation\uc2  statement is any acknowledgment of the willingness of the university to tolerate antisemitism. You know, I have a number of very close friends who have kids in college and who are Jewish who tell me their children are frightened for their safety, because the universities when given a choice between pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  protesters and their Jewish students, the university administrators side with the pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  protesters even if it endangers the safety of their Jewish students.\par \par \uc2 It is utterly indefensible and Harvard needs to do a lot more. Claudine Gay needed to step down, but they're not apologizing for any of it, and much of this was driven I think by donors who in Harvard's case rescinded roughly a billion dollars of pledged contributions, it makes you wonder where the donors to MIT is and why MIT is willing to hold out when Penn and Harvard finally did the right thing.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, let's see what happens over time. Senator, great to see you. Happy New Year to you, sir. Glad to have you as always.\par \par \uc2 Up next, shocking new record in Biden's border crisis, not a record you should be proud of. We've got the data.\par \par \uc2 Sara Carter speaking with Chicago residents about their growing crisis, thanks to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Also, Steven Miller will join us as we continue, live, "Hannity" from Florida.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's border crisis, that continues now to set more records. Get this -- border patrol now found over 300,000 illegal immigrants trying to cross in December alone. That is a new monthly record. Since Biden took office, the total number of encounters is 6.7 million illegal immigrants, with an additional 1.7 million known as, quote, gotaways. Those are the gotaways that we know about. That's a total of 8.3 million people.\par \par \uc2 He's not controlling our borders. He's not enforcing our laws. He's not respecting our sovereignty. Most of these people are unvetted, rewarded for the lawbreaking with free travel, health care, education for their kids.\par \par \uc2 This crisis is a major, major national security threat, I'd say a clear and present danger, as well. You know, we have hundreds of illegals coming from Iran, Syria, thousands from Egypt, Afghanistan. We have tens of thousands from Russia and China, all coming across our southern border.\par \par \uc2 Now California announcing as of the new year passing a law they've not only become a sanctuary state but they become a haven for illegal immigrants, 700,000 now in the state are eligible for free, well, California taxpayer- funded healthcare. That's a cost of at least $3 billion every year.\par \par \uc2 By the way, happy New Year, California. You're insanely high taxes, they just got higher.\par \par \uc2 But this is crushing, you know, what we have now is an influx of so-called asylum seekers. They're all told what to say, destroying communities around the country, putting an unfair financial burden on people, taking jobs from the American people. Anyway, the city of Chicago is one such place.\par \par \uc2 Our very own Sara Carter, she went there today, speaking with local residents that have watched their beloved neighborhood park turned into a crime scene. Take a look at this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CHICAGO RESIDENT: Then you come out here, they pee on my truck. They smoke weed across the street. I haven't actually seen a guy deliver the weed to them.\par \par \uc2 CHICAGO RESIDENT: They're smoking weed. They're drinking, littering. It's - - they play loud music until 11:00, 11:30 at night. I have to call the police to get them to stop.\par \par \uc2 CHICAGO RESIDENT: My wife like literally used to walk across the street to that park, not no more, because you go over there, you'll find condom on the floor. You'll see them smoking on there. I mean, it's basically you -- the neighborhood we used to know and love was no longer here.\par \par \uc2 CHICAGO RESIDENT: And I will simply say that field house should be for the kids. It could be turned into a youth center. It could be somewhere -- a safe place where kids can go, instead of the complete opposite.\par \par \uc2 CHICAGO RESIDENT: I mean, I don't know if, you know, you come over here seeking asylum and you're -- you don't have a job but you're smoking weed, you're drinking, whistling at all the women that go by, cat calling them because that's what they were doing when they had the horns that they were honking at, you know, people going by. It doesn't seem to me that they're very respectful.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Joining us now with more, Sara Carter, along with former senior adviser to President Trump, \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2  is with us.\par \par \uc2 Sara, let me start with you.\par \par \uc2 The park issue is important. We have facilities now being taken away from communities. That's happening all over New York. That's happening as you reported in Chicago. That's a big deal.\par \par \uc2 The cost of educating the children of illegal immigrants, that's putting a burden on our educational system, we have a burden on our health care system because our hospitals won't turn people away, but that's not my biggest concern. If you're coming from Afghanistan, Egypt, Iran, Syria, China and Russia, why do I suspect among those that maybe want a better life for their families, there are groups of people that have other ideas, nefarious intentions for our country?\par \par \uc2 SARA CARTER, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, you're absolutely right, Sean. One of the biggest issues that we're facing right now is that national security crisis. It's the weaponization of migration and this is what I've been talking with when I speak to U.S. intelligence officials, Western intelligence officials in Central America, in South America and across the globe that are saying, look, this pipeline is being used by nefarious actors, and also by our adversaries like China and Iran.\par \par \uc2 Look at what Iran did. Iran supplied \uc2 Hamas\uc2  with the money and with the training necessary to target Israel. Now, we see that Iran is also actively involved in Central American, South America, and that pipeline coming into the United States is being -- is being utilized by everyone and to put matters into perspective so that people can understand this, when people come into the United States, it is impossible to vet them if they are from countries like Syria, like Afghanistan, like China.\par \par \uc2 Why? Because those governments do not cooperate with us. And when you look at a city like Chicago, you're a microcosm of what we're seeing across the United States, it's the people of Chicago that are going to be paying the price. Look, the residents told me, we don't even know who these people are.\par \par \uc2 Okay, they're smoking pot, they're committing crimes. There was a Venezuelan migrant in front of the shelter right there near Gage Park that on December 23rd lost his life when he was targeted, when he was targeted and they are still looking for the killer. So these are the situations that Americans are facing right now, and it's a situation that our intelligence agencies are looking into more and more.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Stephen, a huge burden financially. But, you know, this is a clear and present danger to our country. Do you agree with me? I would say it's 100 percent certainty that among these people coming from countries, our top geopolitical foes that they're probably bringing in terror cells to plot, plan, scheme an October 7th, a 9/11 or whatever, maybe something worse, against the American people.\par \par \uc2 Why would we -- why would we put ourselves in that type of ri -- why would we burden ourselves with that type of risk?\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN MILLER\uc2 , FORMER TRUMP SENIOR ADVISER: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is waging war against America's national security. Every foreign enemy and adversary in the world knows and understands that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has a policy of open resettlement on the border. Turn yourself in, get resettled and if you are worried about that, you can be one of the millions as you mentioned of gotaways.\par \par \uc2 So either way, you're getting into the country, either because you're going to be released or you're going to just slip right on through along with millions of others. Anyone who wants to hurt America knows this, understands it, and can freely exploit it, and not just terrorist, Sean, but spies. How many foreign spies that maybe we could have stopped at an airport, that maybe we could have stopped through normal