y not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 NEIL CAVUTO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Nasty e-mail and said, Neil, now we got to do it. It's time for who's naughty and nice. With our look at e-mails that we've gotten lately, someone's a bit extreme, I feel vulnerable, but my staff said to separate the naughty stuff from the nice stuff. I'm still looking for the nice stuff. But that's tomorrow. "THE FIVE" is now.\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Welcome, everybody. I'm Jesse Watters along with Emily Compagno, Harold Ford Jr., Dana Perino, and Greg Gutfeld. It's 5:00 in New York City and this is THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Is Trump an insurrectionist, sir?\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Well, I think it's self-evident. You saw it all. Now, whether the 14th Amendment applies or not, the court makes that decision. But he's certainly supporting an insurrection. No question about it. None. Zero. And he seems to be doubling down on (INAUDIBLE)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Destroying democracy is totally fine if Democrats do it. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  giving his blessing to the bombshell ruling that kicked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  off the ballot in Colorado. You can blame these four Democrat-picked Colorado Supreme Court justices for the landmark decision.\par \par \uc2 They pushed a novel legal theory that sounds like it was written by MSNBC's primetime. Deciding that the former President's actions on January 6 make him ineligible to even run for president again. And are using the 14th Amendment, a relic from the Civil War era to stop insurrectionists from holding office.\par \par \uc2 I think we need a little fact-check on that last one. Trump has