le are in debt, and people know they're in debt and they're borrowing to get by. You got to grow their incomes.\par \par \uc2 I remember us growing incomes a few years ago, Sean, but it wasn't under Bidenomics.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's true. Socialism, any form, any name, any manifestation, always ends the same way. Broken promises, more poverty and a loss of freedom every time.\par \par \uc2 All right. Thank you, Brian Brenberg. Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 All right. Straight ahead tonight, liberal hypocrisy on full display at the \uc2 U.N.\uc2 's climate change conference in Dubai. Yeah, and \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  just declared coal plants shouldn't be permitted anywhere in the world. I'm sure China, India, I'm sure they're going to be willing participants in his lunacy. Straight ahead, we'll check in with \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Tensions are really high at the climate alarmist conference, this time in Dubai. Now, the president and host of the summit is now under fire for remarks that he made two weeks earlier. Apparently, he doesn't actually believe that science supports a phase out of oil or gas. Wow. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN AUDIO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SULTAN AHMED AL-JABER, COP28 PRESIDENT: I accepted to come to this -- to this meeting to have a sober and a mature conversation. We do not -- I'm not in any way signing up to any discussion that is alarmist. There is no science out there or no scenario out there that says that the phase out of fossil fuel is what's going to achieve 1.5.\par \par \uc2 (END AUDIO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Meanwhile, well, \uc2 John Kerry\uc2 , he jetted all the way to Dubai to say just this. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOHN KERRY\uc2 , BIDEN CLIMATE CZAR: There shouldn't be any more coal-fired power plants permitted anywhere in the world. And the reality is that we're not doing it. So, you know, the measure here is really sounding the alarm bell. I find myself getting more and more militant.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You've been militant for a while, John.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, car's fearmongering and attempting to further destroy the economy, it is the lifeblood of the world's economy. China, they're moving forward with numerous coal power projects. They don't have a care in the world.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, former Arkansas Governor \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 You know my favorite part of this, Governor, and only you could probably, you know, put the right words to this, is as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  brought us back into the climate accords that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  got us out of China, China and India are classified as developing countries. That means we pay the freight for getting rid of what is the lifeline, the engine of business around the world, the lifeline of the world's economy.\par \par \uc2 Why would we be so stupid and that guy seems to get at the head of the conference?\par \par \uc2 MIKE HUCKABEE\uc2 , FORMER ARKANSAS GOVERNOR: I don't know if you know this, Sean, but \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  is actually the chairman of the college bowl playoff committee and he was the reason that made the dumb decision to take Florida State out. That's just how smart this guy is.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, they went undefeated, too, yeah.\par \par \uc2 HUCKABEE: Totally undefeated. I mean, they got robbed and the U.S. is getting robbed if \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  gets his way, because we get 20 percent of our electricity from coal. By the way the world gets at almost 38 percent. So you take coal completely out of it just abruptly because \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  wants us to, and suddenly, you're not going to have enough electricity to power those electric cars that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wants us to go out and buy.\par \par \uc2 But I do want to tell you, at least \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  windsurfed over to Dubai. I'm sure he didn't take a jet because that would have sucked up a lot of fossil fuel.\par \par \uc2 But my question for all these guys -- why don't they just have a Zoom meeting like the rest of us end up having to do? I mean it would be so much more efficient and they wouldn't be blowing gas all over the Earth.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, it's funny you say that because all the private jets that are flying in there. And I don't care -- thank God for jet engines. We can go from here to there to everywhere, and all these people flying in on their private jets, and yet the head of this entire conference says there's no science behind the demand to phase out fossil fuel and \uc2 John Kerry\uc2 's the one saying, well, I'm the militant on the issue. Well, there's more than militant. I mean, it's just stupid.\par \par \uc2 HUCKABEE: Well, a gaffe is basically defined as when a politician accidentally tells the truth, and I think that's what happened. This guy told the truth and then everybody got mad at him because he said, don't you know, we're not supposed to do that. We're supposed to lie. We're supposed to tell everybody that they have to quit using fossil fuels, but let's not tell China or India or for -- let's don't tell Iran that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah. As if, they'd listen to \uc2 John Kerry\uc2 , the militant. That's not happening. He's been flying in private jets his entire adult life.\par \par \uc2 Governor Huckabee, good to see you, sir. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, that is all the time we have left this evening.\par \par \uc2 Don't forget, tomorrow night, Davenport, Iowa, exclusive town hall with former President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 . Just go to hannity.com if you want to join us. Tickets are free.\par \par \uc2 And live audience shows in New York City, Wednesday and Thursday. Again, tickets are free, Hannity.com. We'd love to see you there. Hope you catch a football.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, set your DVR so you never miss an episode.\par \par \uc2 Let not your heart be trouble, Greg Gutfeld is next.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020231205ejc400001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 DeSantis Versus Newsom: The Great Red Versus Blue State Debate; Florida Governor And Republican Presidential Candidate \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  And California Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  Debate Issues Of Antisemitism And U.S. Policy Towards China; Commentators Review Debate Performances Of Governors \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  And \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 .\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Kayleigh McEnany, Harold Ford Jr., Ari Fleischer,  Chip Roy, Mark Penn \par \uc2 10,062 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 November 2023\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: "This Book Is Gay," a book containing instructions on the ins and outs of gay sexuality.\par \par \uc2 Let me finish. Let's talk about it. A book that contains graphic descriptions about how to masturbate for males and females. My question to you, Governor Newsom, those books, do you believe that's appropriate for school districts to teach kids? Yes or no?\par \par \uc2 GOV. GAVIN NEWSOM (D-CA): Come on. Those aren't -- that's not part of the curriculum. They're not teaching. It's not --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Those are the -- that were -- those are books that were --\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Hold on. Hold on. The bottom line is, you aren't a book banning binge your state, 1,406 books, 3,362 in this country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You didn't answer about -- what about those books?\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: That's not -- we don't provide for K through third grade education that kind of curriculum. It's just made up. These guys make it up. It is part of this cultural purge.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Should it be --\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: It's just made --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What grade would be acceptable?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- what I find --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What grade?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: But, what I find offensive, Sean and Ron, what I find offensive is the very significant number of these books happened to be LGBTQ books, a significant number of these books happen to be --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Do you think it's appropriate in store?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- on African Americans.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Do you think it's -- governor, governor.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: And I honestly find --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Do you think it's appropriate in store?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I told you, we don't teach that. We don't teach that. We have sex education in middle schools, in high schools, where it's appropriate. This is a ginned-up, made-up issue to divide this country. You talk about dividing this country. This is part of the culture war, the weaponization of grievance.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: This is part using education -- we're focusing on Maths, Science. We're focusing on reimagining in our schools just to --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We're going to get to education next.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- criminalizing teachers, and criminalizing the --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: They check out the wrong book.\par \par \uc2 GOV. RON DESANTIS (R-FL): So, California, they've done -- they've used the schools to impose a liberal agenda, social justice. They have this ethnic studies where they're dividing people. That's what they're doing. Let me just say something about parents' rights, because he says California respects parents' rights. This is rich. He has been telling a lot of whoppers tonight. This may be the biggest. In California, if you're a parent in Iowa or New Hampshire, South Carolina, your minor child can go to California without your knowledge or without your consent and get hormone therapy, puberty blockers and a sex change operation --\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: -- all without you knowing or consenting. How in the heck is that --\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: You know what?\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: -- you are honoring parents' rights, when you're bringing people from out of state to go around their parents' backs and getting life altering surgeries? That is radical. That is a freeze (ph) kid.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Ron --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: That is an assault on parent's rights.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: You know what? Ron, this is --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: It's not for you to decide.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: You know what?\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: It's for the parents to decide. And the parents do not want their kids going for these other thing.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: You know what? These kids just want to survive. I find this honestly.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me let me stay on a follow-up. Let's turn to the issue of education.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Where is the decency and humanity --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: The decency of taking, ripping somebody --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Gentleman, gentlemen --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- nobody can hear you.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: That is wrong.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Let us turn, gentlemen, if I may, to the issue of education. Here is public school spending per K through 12 students, according to the education data initiative from the U.S. Census Bureau and National Center for Education. Florida spends nearly $12,000 per student while California spends over $16,000. Florida is ranked number one by \uc2 U.S. News & World Report\uc2 . In terms of state education rankings, California ranks 20th. Governor Newsom, what is your explanation? You spend more money and they have better results in Florida. Why?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I just told you what I'm doing in public education. We created a brand new grade pre-k for all. We're doing after school and summer school for all. We're reimagining the school day, not just the school year. We just provided 3.4 million of our students upwards of $2 billion for child savings accounts, and the opportunity to start businesses when they graduate. We have one of the best records under COVID, during COVID.\par \par \uc2 And again, you didn't answer to the fact you had more learning loss. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  had more learning loss during COVID. Fourth grade reading, fourth grade math, eighth grade reading, eighth grade math, we outperformed you in every -- it's a fact during COVID in every one of those categories. I'm -- I can't wait to get all the political facts tonight, because Ron, you keep denying some basic fundamental facts on health, wealth and education. We outperformed you during COVID.\par \par \uc2 You talk about things to apologize. You should apologize for your COVID record. You are with Fauci. You aligned with vaccines. You aligned with CDC guidelines until you didn't in tens of thousands of people --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Actually --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's turn our focus to education.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Well, when we opened the schools, we bucked all of those people, June of 2020. He kept the schools closed for a long time. And that had devastating impacts. And why? What \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  does in California is kowtow to the teachers union. Whatever they tell him to do, he does. He will never buck the teachers union. That's why the kids were locked out of school for so long. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in the pocket of the teachers union, and so is \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . That's why they thought --\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: By the way, it is not \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: -- full opening when he came in there, when they had that in there.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: It's \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , Ron. It's \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , Madam President to you in \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Stop insulting.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Biden came into office and he brought in the teacher union to be able to do all these different things to try to keep the schools closed. So, the Democratic Party, the far left in this country, they are owned lock, stock, and barrel by the teachers union.\par \par \uc2 I bet the teachers union in Florida to get the schools open -- first in the country, during COVID. Also to do universal school choice. Every parent in Florida has a right to send their kid to the school of their choice.\par \par \uc2 We're winning these fights. California is bending the knee to the union because they controlled the politicians.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Let's move on. A topic that will seemingly play a very large role in the future elections and it's the issue of abortion.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I have a question for both of you. I'll ask you to please respect the individual's right to answer uninterrupted.\par \par \uc2 And that is, Governor DeSantis -- I think it's actually your turn, Governor Newsom, if you don't mind.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: All good.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Most medical professionals believe a baby is