e clear on this. If a woman and her doctor for any reason --\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Not for any reason.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, no, no, I'm asking --\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: It's extremely rare.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Should there be --\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: This is a -- I know where you guys are going, Sean. You're even implacable (ph) with this whole issue and I understand it.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm asking -- I watch your -- I watch your --\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: This is where you guys have to go --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm asking. Should -- should there be --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- to cover for the extreme anti-abortion agenda of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  that's hurt your party.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- would you support a ban on abortion in seventh, eighth, and ninth month through (ph) --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I just answered your question.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- if -- if the doors if the mother's life is not in jeopardy?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: It is extreme, extreme exception. People aren't going on and having abortion unless devastating has happened.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Should it be illegal then? If it is rare, should it be illegal?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: It should be up to the mother and her doctor and her conscience. And it almost --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So, the answer is no restriction?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I've already answered it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No restriction?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: And I'd just reinforce it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: To cover, again -- hold on, for the most extreme abortion ban in the country. I have a simple question, though, this is important.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, no, no, I'm asking the question.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Will you -- \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , will you or will you not sign --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: My turn? It's my turn? Okay.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- a six-week ban in the unlikely case you're president of the United States?\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Will you support a national ban?\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Governor DeSantis, let's talk about your state.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- on that fundamental question.\par \par \uc2 You had -- you had 15 weeks, you had a 15-week rule in California. You reduced it to six.\par \par \uc2 My question is this, what was your thinking behind it? Was it for religious reasons? Was it for scientific reasons? What was the reason for you from going from 15 weeks to six weeks?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, I believe in a culture of life. I think we're better off when everybody counts, when everybody has an opportunity to do well, and that bill attaches when there is a detectable heartbeat for the child.\par \par \uc2 And some states have done that. Some states have done others. Some states have done later. And obviously, they have a right to do that.\par \par \uc2 But I think about one of our Floridians, a lady named Penny Hopper. She actually survived a late-term abortion back in the day and they left her on the -- on the table there, to basically wither away.\par \par \uc2 Her grandmother came, saved her, brought her -- brought her to a hospital, brought her -- saved her, and she ended up living a -- living a good life. So she counts and she matters.\par \par \uc2 And I think that what the position that we have from the modern left, including in California, is that they will take your tax dollars and they will fund abortion all the way to the moment of birth.\par \par \uc2 He's wrong when he says the latter terms are all because of this. Eighty- eight percent past 15 weeks are, in fact, elective from the Florida data. He doesn't keep data there. But that is really extreme, to take your tax dollars and to do this all the way up to the moment of birth. He didn't answer your question about any type of protections at all for a baby that has a beating heart, that can feel pain, that is viable.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Let me-hold on.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Respectfully, this is an important conversation. Will you or will you not support a national-\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: You didn't answer. Sean. Why didn't you answer his question?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Will you or will you not support a national ban if it lands on your desk? You couldn't answer that in any other context.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay, gentlemen, we're moving on to the next issue.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: No, Sean, not the next issue.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: You never gave a week.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: The American people should know this. I'll answer it for \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . He can't answer it. He will sign that extreme six-week national ban.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Okay, let me move on. I'm calling this the lightning round. It would be great. It would be great if you guys cooperated. I'm not a potted plant here. And I want to ask you, we all know that federal policy does have a huge impact on states. We know that. I'm going to ask you three simple questions, and I just want one-word answers, okay, from three of you.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: We will do our best.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We're coming up on a break. And the issue is, right now, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is president. So, I would like both of you to give a grade to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  overall as president. Governor Newsom, I'll give-\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: A. An A.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: An A.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Governor Newsom -\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I think it's been a masterclass.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Failed.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: A failure. Okay. Now, number two, are his policies helping or hurting your individual states? Is it helping the state of Florida?\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: The inflation is hurting our state big time.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Grade?\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Fail. He failed. He's failed