ing more there. But \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  wants to do, what he is doing in California, what Biden wants to do nationally, is government dictated green energy policies. They want to kneecap fossil fuels and reliable energy. We have already seen what has happening in California. They have rolling blackouts.\par \par \uc2 He actually implemented a mandate to buy electric vehicles. So pretty soon in California, you are not going to be able to buy a normal car. Only electric vehicles and they celebrated that it is like a great thing. A couple days later, there was a notice from the state government telling all EV owners, do not plug in your EV because they don't have enough grid capacity. So he is walking his people into a big-time disaster.\par \par \uc2 What Biden wants to do is he wants to take the California model, he wants to impose that nationally. He wants to take away your ability to purchase the car that you want. He wants to kneecap reliable energy and he wants to bring these rolling blackouts all across the United States of America. It does not work. It is going to cause huge problems. We have more energy here. We can be the dominant energy producer in the world.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Apparently not in Florida. You opposed fracking.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: And that's what we are going to do. Florida is not a big energy state. We have the Marcellus Shale. We have the west Texas. We have all of that. So let's do that. No forcing electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We got to take a break.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Save America automobile.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: When we come back, we will continue the great state -- red state/blue state debate, more with Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , more with Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  as we continue. Thank you for being with us from Alpharetta, Georgia.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Welcome back to -- welcome back to HANNITY. "The Great Red State- Blue State Debate."\par \par \uc2 We continue with Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to the Department of Housing and Urban Development, these are the numbers for the homeless population in each of your states. It is a big problem around the country. In the state of California, it is 172,000. In Florida, it is 26,000.\par \par \uc2 Now, the per capita numbers are pretty much the same. For California, it is 44 per 10,000 people, while Florida has 12 per 10,000 people.\par \par \uc2 So, Governor DeSantis, I ask you, why the disparity? What are the policies you are implementing that is different from that of California?\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: California is adopting leftist policies. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  was governor -- or Mayor of San Francisco. He put out a 10-year plan like 20 years ago. He was going to end homelessness. Then, a few years later, he had another plan. And now, he says he is going to do, and it's only gotten worse. In the last 10 years in California, the homeless has gone up 45 percent. It's gone down in Florida 45 percent. But, it's caused a huge problem with quality of life in California. The people that flee always bring up this. They've really empowered lawlessness and drug use.\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , at one point, tried to say that California was the freedom, saying I just kind of laugh like you're locking people down. You're doing all this. But then, I thought about it. California does have freedoms that some people don't -- the other states don't. You have the freedom to defecate in public in California. You have the freedom to pitch a tent on Sunset Boulevard. You have the freedom to create a homeless encampment under a freeway and even light it on fire. You have the freedom to have an open air drug market and use drugs. You have the freedom if you're an illegal alien to get all these taxpayer benefits.\par \par \uc2 So, those are freedoms. They're not the freedoms our founding fathers envisioned, but they have contributed to the destruction of the quality of life in California, and the results speak for themselves. People are leaving the state because they have failed at addressing the homeless population.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Well, I love the rant on freedom. I mean, here is a guy who is criminalizing teachers, criminalizing doctors, criminalizing librarians, and criminalizing women that seek their reproductive care. You're making it harder to vote. You're banning books. I mean, spare me this notion of freedom. Ask the folks at \uc2 Disney\uc2  about freedom and free enterprise. Ask the folks at the Special Olympics that you threatened to fine with $27 million.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Because they were discriminating against the athletes. You wanted those athletes to be out of there because of the Down syndrome.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Who goes after Special Olympians? When it comes to the issue, Ron, of homelessness --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: That is wrong.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- when it comes to the --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: That's being a liberal bully. That's being a bully.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Really? Attacking --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: They're Down syndrome. They want to discriminate against them.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- Special Olympians, $27 million fine --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: They were discriminating against -- because they were discriminating against the athletes. They wanted to marginalize the athletes, and you wanted the athletes marginalized.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- to the Special Olympians, I find that disgraceful. On the issue of marginalize --all right.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: That was wrong what you did. These are kids with Down syndrome.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: By the way --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: They just wanted to compete and --\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- I grew up working eight adoption special kids.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: -- you wanted them not at the Special Olympics.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I've been working with specials kids all my life.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: You're a liberal bully. You wanted them to be --\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: How dare you? How dare you, Ron?\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: -- you wanted them to be ostracized.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: You threatened to fine the Special Olympians --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: You can talk to Isabella from Florida.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- with $27 million of fine.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: She got to participate because we stood up for her.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: This is the way you treat? Yeah. I could -- by the way -- now, hold on. Let me say.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's your turn.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I can handle that. I can handle it. I'm used to that. But, you know what?\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: You wanted her not to compete.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Your attacks on the trans community, your attacked on the gay and lesbian community.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: You attacked her not to compete. That's wrong.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: You attacked vulnerable communities. You attacked women.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: She should have been able to compete. And we stood up with them, and we made sure that then could compete.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Again, Ron, relax. I can handle it. I'm used to bullying. You're nothing but a bully.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: You're a bully.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I understand that. Intimidating and humiliating people, that is your calling part.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Why did you want the Special Olympians if they weren't able to compete?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: And by the way, how well is it going for you?\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Why did you want them not to be able to compete?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: How well is this campaign --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Why do you want them not to be able to compete?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: How well is this campaign going? He is not going to let me talk. So, I will talk to the American people.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: I don't underst