sco, and you see how almost the whole thing is covered because that is what has happened in one of the previous greatest cities this country has ever had. Human feces is now a fact of life, except when a Communist dictator comes to town. Then they cleaned up the streets. They lined the streets with Chinese flags. They didn't put American flags there. They cleaned everything up. So, they're willing to do it for a Communist dictator, but they're not willing to do it for their own.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I want to get in with our limited time we have left. I want to get the two very important issues we have not hit. After the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  terror attacks on October 7, we have seen what is nothing short of a disturbing outbreak of --\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- virulent, hatred, antisemitism around the world, in the halls of our Congress, on American streets, on college campuses, last month outside in Sydney Opera House in Australia. We've seen it all over Europe. But, in Australia, anti-Israeli protesters literally in this day and age chanting "gas the Jews, F the Jews". In American cities, we have protesters calling for global Islamic war and demanding that Israel be wiped off the map, or in the words of Congresswoman Tlaib, from the river to the sea.\par \par \uc2 Israel, meanwhile, is vowing to eradicate the terrorist group \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . But, according to a report in \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  this week, U.S. officials have warned Israel that they need more -- to fight more surgically in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Governor Newsom, 30 seconds for you. We have to cut back on time.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: All right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How do -- how can Israel win the war against this terrorist group using surgical strikes and directions from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I visited Israel. I met with families, the hostages. I saw videos of children being killed in front of their parents. Parents being killed in front of their children. I saw a beheading with a garden hoe. This is not complicated to me. It's a fight between good and evil. \uc2 Hamas\uc2  is a terrorist organization, and they need to be eliminated, not just for the people of Israel and Jews around the world, but for the Palestinians themselves. But, when it comes to the issue of anti-semitism, you just mentioned a lot of things that have been occurring on \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 's watch. He said nothing. Master man --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You are calling him anti-semitic?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- marching. I'm saying had he countenanced antisemitism --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Give me a break.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- and now he is finally talking a big game ever since October 7. How about the --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: For the sake of fairness of the time, gentlemen --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: He said nothing. Nothing on these issues.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- Governor DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Look at the record.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Governor DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: \uc2 Hamas\uc2  wants nothing short than a second Holocaust. They want to destroy Israel and wipe every single Jew off the map. Israel has every right to defend itself to the hilt. Biden should not be kneecapping them in any way, shape, or form. And by the way, Biden stranded a lot of American citizens over there. We're trying to get home. So, I did an executive order in Florida, and we sent planes over to Israel, right in the aftermath of October 7, and we saved over 700 Americans, mostly Floridians, but not all, because Biden wouldn't do it.\par \par \uc2 Finally, Biden started dumping people in Greece, and then they were sending a bill to the Americans just to get to Greece. If you come to this country illegally, they will pay to fly you all over the place. They'll put you up in hotel at no expense. But yet, our own citizens fleeing a war zone, they're going to send you a bill? \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  failed those people, and we stepped up and got it done.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Let me ask you,\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: But, you didn't step up to call our antisemitism on your streets for years --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We don't have a lot of time. So, I want to turn to the issue, gentleman, of have China. I talked about this often, intellectual property theft, unfair trade practices. China has been hostile to our fighter jets in international airspace, hostile to our Navy in international waterways. We know all about the China spy balloon that happened, eight days right across the United States over military installations. The Communist Chinese, they have nationals buying up thousands of acres of ranch land, farmland and land near military installations, their hostility towards Taiwan. They are, Governor DeSantis, our number one geopolitical foe. I don't see that the Biden administration has been tough with them. What would you do differently?\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Well, first, in Florida, we banned China from buying land in our state, because you're right. You don't want them buying farmland or land near your military bases. So, we acted. We also got the \uc2 Confucius Institutes\uc2  out of our universities. China should not be involved in our universities at all. What you need to do is you need to have hard power in the Indo-Pacific to deter China's ambitions. You need to take the economy. We need to decouple from China. We're dependent on them for so many things.\par \par \uc2 And then finally, we need to get serious about their influence in this country. They shouldn't be able to buy farmland anywhere. I can tell you this. I would not go to China and grovel in front of Xi, like \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  did. He says China is a partner on climate change. China is adding two new coal plants every year. China is laughing at us with what they're doing. So, yes, they're the number one threat we face. And we need to take it seriously. And \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is not doing that.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: This is just a reminder. I think it's a question some people probably ask and I know Nikki Haley's campaign is asking, When are you going to drop out and at least give Nikki Haley a shot to take down \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in this nomination? She laid you out.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Please.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: You are a walking hypocrite --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: You win. You win.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What about China?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- you are a walking hypocrite on the issue of China.\par \par \uc2 DESANTS: I'm not.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: This is a guy that was looking for direct foreign trade from China, was doing trade shows, open up an --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: That is old. That's already been debunked. You talk about liberal fact checkers?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: That's absolutely true. You are aggressive at --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Even the liberal fact checkers did that.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  himself today called you red run --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Please.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: -- for a reason because of your complete hypocrisy, again talking a big game.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. We're almost out of time.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I confronted Xi on the issue of fentanyl, Ron. I confronted them out on human rights.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Not on human rights. You didn't.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I absolutely did with the Foreign Minister and the Vice President and other leaders in China. You talk a big game. Meanwhile --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We are over time.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Final question. Governor DeSantis, we owe you about 90 seconds. But, you get the last word as per the coin flip.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: What are you giving me? Five seconds? What do I get?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No. I will do.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: All right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'll be a little more generous in that. Look, it's been a very passionate debate tonight. Actually, it's been fun to be a part of -- I think the American people will decide. Governing philosophies could not be more different. But, let me ask you this, kind of a fun question. You both clearly love your states. You visited each other's state. Governor DeSantis, you can take as much time as you want. You have an extra 90 seconds. What is your favorite thing about the State of California and --\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I will give him five minutes for this. That's a good question.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. We'll stay longer.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: We're not.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Five minutes, Governor.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: When I got orders as a Navy Lieutenant to go to Naval Amphibious Base Coronado, I had not spent any real time in California in my life, Florida native, and I'm very proud of the state. But, I got down there, and that strand is one of the most beautiful places I've ever been. And then, all up and down, just a tremendous coastline. I do believe California has more natural advantages than any state in the country, which is why when you have so many people leaving on net, that's hard to do. Like, people don't want to leave there because it really is such a beautiful area. And I'm proud of the military installations that are there. I'm proud of what the Navy has been able to do in conjunction with the state.\par \par \uc2 It was really important duty. It really helped forge me as an individual and as an American. And so, I always have very, very fond memories of that nice strand down there in Southern California.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I love that. I mean, \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What do you love -- now, what you love -- I don't' know what you love about California.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Reagan used to call it California Coast of Dreams. By the way --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What do you love about Florida?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: What I love about your question is the comedy in the question, meaning, you know what? We all want to be loved. We need to be loved. We all want to be protected, respected and connected. I think there is a unity frame here.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: You said it. Well. I mean, Ron -- I have no doubt \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  loves this country. I love this country. It's not about red versus blue. It's red, white, and blue, the United States of America. And I think we're all better off and we're all better off. And so, I appreciate this conversation. I appreciate you, Ron, being a family man. You got three incredible kids. I appreciate your wife, your sacrifice, and I appreciate your military service. But, I also appreciate we do have fundamental differences about the fate and future of this country. And that's why I'm going to be working so hard to get \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  reelected in 2024.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You couldn't resist. You had to go right back to 2024. All right. Here is the last question. Would you do this again?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I hope we could do another half hour. I got all --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: You know what? We need --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  didn't show up to a debate.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: That's why I wanted to do in five minutes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I have 20 minutes, and I've got a lot of questions.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: I'm happy to --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You want to stay?\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Let's just do an extended hour. I'm happy to do it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay. Then I --\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: This has been fun.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I think it's been fun, and I think it's been more entertaining. I'm sorry to the guests that I've invited. I got to take a break, though, in the meantime. We've got to pay some bills. It's not a cheap set we built for you all. I hope you like it. Courtesy of your favorite channel Fox News, and you do admit you watch often. We will take a break. They have agreed to stay. Well, that's I guess the debate on the fly will continue on the other side and later have live post-debate coverage. We are in Alpharetta, Georgia, the Great Red State Blue State Debate, as we continue.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Welcome back to HANNITY, our red state, blue state debate. By mutual agreement, both candidates had other commitments, and they realized afterwards they couldn't stay longer. But we appreciate them all being here tonight.\par \par \uc2 OK, what did you think about it? Was there a winner, loser, winners, losers? You get to react.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, here joining us, co-host of "THE FIVE" and former Democratic Congressman, Harold Ford Jr. along with the co-host of "OUTNUMBERED," \uc2 Kayleigh McEnany\uc2 , FOX News contributor \uc2 Ari Fleischer\uc2 . Kayleigh, we start with you. That was a very low energy debate. That is my first observation.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEIGH MCENANY, CO-HOST, "OUTNUMBERED": And mine was the opposite. I know you're being facetious. What an edifying, constructive, smart hour with fact-based questions. Sean, one of the best events I have seen in a very long time, so well done on your part.\par \par \uc2 In press, when I was press secretary, Ari knows this, you ask yourself, do you have a facts problem or do you have a messaging problem? And tonight what you saw was a facts problem for \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 . You put up the numbers. They were undeniable. You sourced them.\par \par \uc2 And what the public saw was the sharpest, best messenger in the Democrat party, I maintain that is \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , unable to message the rotting pile of facts before him, both in the state of California and nationally for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . DeSantis had some really strong moments, particularly when he said, look, I talked to a guy who said I love the employment down here, I love the wages down here. I love the state of Florida, how safe it is. By the way, that was your father-in-law, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 . Also pulling out the map of the feces in San Francisco, another strong and powerful moment. So I think the clear winner, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , and a nearly impossible task for \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's get your take, \uc2 Ari Fleischer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ARI FLEISCHER\uc2 , FORMER WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: I think watching this, you realize, Democrats are from Mars and Republicans are from Venus. They speak totally different languages. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 's language was one of economics, gasoline $6, $7 a gallon, the lockdowns in California. It was very practical, very focused on people's daily lives, the rising cost of living.\par \par \uc2 If you listen to \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , his whole message was identity politics, which is the language of the Democrats. I don't like the way you talk about migrants. We have to fight for women. Everything he says is about a group, an ethnic group, a chunk of Americans. It is not about America. And that is the language the Democrats respond to. So you really have two different approaches for what America needs.\par \par \uc2 I will say this. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  is much more articulate, fast on his feet, and sharper than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . And if I'm a Democrat looking at the presidential race, even if I dismiss \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , I have to still worry about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . And that is a difference, and just Biden's age, Sean, as you pointed that out.\par \par \uc2 The final thing I was about DeSantis, I don't think that he closed the gap with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tonight. It was a nice night for him, and he did well, and he had the facts on his side. But when you look at the purpose of him being there, which is to win a presidential race, I just don't think he closed the gap.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Actually, it was separated from that. I could just tell you in the discussion leading up to this that this was really a state versus state, and although clearly, I think Gavin at times wanted to talk more presidential politics. Harold Ford Jr., your take?\par \par \uc2 HAROLD FORD JR., FORMER TENNESSEE REPRESENTATIVE: So first off, congrats, Sean. I thought you did a good job, and you framed this thing the right way, a state versus a state, and both of these candidates who were governors were very passionate, patriotic, they defended their records.\par \par \uc2 I think Kayleigh and Mr. Fleischer are right. I think what Ari said at the end there is probably the most useful and maybe the utility level is highest. Who did best for their parties tonight? I think one of the things, and Kayleigh said at the outset, there's no doubt that \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  will be the most important, the most forceful and articulate advocate on behalf of Democrats in this 2024 election. And Governor DeSantis, I think, displayed one of the things that Republicans are going to have to deal with, how do you talk about the economy? How do you talk about the issues in the face of, I think, whether we like it or not, or agree or not, one of the more powerful issues in this election in 2024 is going to be this issue of reproductive rights for women. It is not going to overtake everything but will certainly be one of the most important issues.\par \par \uc2 And I think where we are six months from today with regard to gas prices and inflation will probably determine more about the outcome of the presidential race than anything else. But as it relates to the state issues, Florida, California, I've got to tell you, I was more impressed with \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  than I thought I would be. I thought that Governor Newsom, who I think is one of the most effective presenters in politics, he was that tonight. But I thought that Governor DeSantis laid out very effectively his record in Florida.\par \par \uc2 Was it able to do what he was able to do on the presidential stage? Probably not. But tonight, I think he probably fared better than I thought a lot of people thought he might have fared against a guy in our party, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who I thought did well tonight. But I thought Governor DeSantis did a pretty good job tonight as well, too, defending his state and his record.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What did you think, Kayleigh, about the answer when I quoted LBJ in terms of Gavin? There's a lot of suspicion, a lot of people around the country, polls are bearing this out now more than ever that people are seeing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as weak and frail and in cognitive decline. That was not something that \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  wanted to admit. But when you bring up the issue of whether or not if his party came to him, whether -- he has been very clear in all three interviews that I have had with him, tonight being a debate, obviously, I'm moderating, but he thinks that it would be the vice president, Vice President Harris, and not him up next. If you say it that often, you have to take somebody at their word, don't you?\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: As a political figure, there are certain things you have to say. This is why every single person probably in all of time who has run for president says, oh, no, it not my time. I'm not thinking of that right now. I'm focusing on by state and my city, et cetera, and then several of them go on to run for president. There are certain things that you must say. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  tonight must have said over and over again it is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and then given that head nod to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But what I look at are what were the words of \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  leading into the midterm elections? Days before the midterm elections, he talked about his fundamental grievances with his party. They are unable to message. It was someone, by his words, that seemed to be clearly posturing in the event of a red wave, either running himself and taking on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , or being the second alternative waiting at the wings. Then the red wave did not happen. It crashed and burned, and all of a sudden \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  kissed the ring and says, yes, it's you, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , you had a very good midterm election.\par \par \uc2 I think he is waiting in the wings. He can't get on the ballot because we have missed several ballot deadlines, but I think he is waiting in the event that something goes wrong at the Democratic Party, at the Democratic National Convention where they actually name the nominee, he is waiting there. That's the only reason that you do a debate like what we saw tonight going toe to toe with someone who is running himself to be the GOP nominee.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Exit, quick grade, that's it. Ari, we will start with you. How would you grade Governor DeSantis tonight? And what grade would you give \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  tonight?\par \par \uc2 FLEISCHER: I would give DeSantis a B plus in the way he handled the facts. I would give him a B minus because he hardly ever looked \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  in the eye. And if you're going to be strong, you need to look at your opponent in the eye. He did it occasionally. You need to do it always.\par \par \uc2 I would give Newsom a D just in terms of his making of the facts, his fabricating, his making things up. In terms of being glib, I would give him an A. I don't think I've ever seen a guy stand in the on deck circle putting pine tar on his bat, studying the pitcher and swinging the bat all the while denying that he is going to step up to the plate. That is what \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  was tonight.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Harold Ford Jr., grades?\par \par \uc2 FORD: I will give them both B pluses. I think they did what they had to do tonight to try to advance where they were. I do think that if you are Governor Haley, if you're thinking about the presidential race tonight, Governor Haley is probably doing fine tonight. And I think in the presidential race, former President Trump is probably feeling much better. And if you are President Biden, you better sign \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  up to be your chief surrogate in this presidential race.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Kayleigh, you get the last word. Grades?\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: DeSantis gets an A. He was the clear runaway winner. However, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , given the bad pile of facts gets a C. He's a sharp messenger. Watch out. That guy is coming. He is a rising star in the party.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Thank you all three. I appreciate it. Thanks for being with us.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, Democratic pollster \uc2 Mark Penn\uc2  and Congressman Chip Roy, they react to tonight's debate. Thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Here with more reaction to tonight's big debate, Texas Congressman and DeSantis campaign surrogate Chip Roy along with former senior adviser to the Clintons, the Harris Poll Chairman, \uc2 Mark Penn\uc2  is with us. Guys, great to have you both. Chip, start with you. Thoughts on tonight?\par \par \uc2 REP. CHIP ROY, (R-TX): Hey, Sean, great to be on. I think what you saw tonight was a clear distinction between freedom and failure. What you saw in Governor DeSantis was a clear message, clear vision for what we have seen occur in Florida versus what we have seen occur in California. Florida with freedom, you're seeing unprecedented success, you're seeing people flock there. And out of California you're seeing the kind of policies that \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  was all too proud to associate with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  extending those California policies to America where now people see E.V.s, cars, piling up on car dealership lots and inflation driving people away from being able to afford their homes, their cars, their ability to put meals on the table. So you saw a clear distinction.\par \par \uc2 But importantly, what you saw is you saw Governor DeSantis make the case for why he won by a million-and-a-half votes in Florida, why he won 62 percent of Hispanic voters, why he won 50 percent of single female voters, why he flipped Miami-Dade, why people are flocking to Florida. And that clear vision when you have an adult conversation, this is what America needs to see.\par \par \uc2 And you know what, it was nice to see someone like Governor DeSantis who grew up in the 80s instead of being in his 80s, someone who can lead this country with energy and vision and served for eight years. And I think you also saw why President Trump doesn't have any interest in debating head to head Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's get your take, \uc2 Mark Penn\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MARK PENN\uc2 , THE HARRIS POLL CHAIRMAN: First, Sean, congratulations on the best debate of 2023 for sure. Look, I thought it was, except for moments of people calling each other a liar and bully, I thought it was an incredibly substantive debate. I thought \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , look, if you are in the DeSantis campaign, putting the campaign talking points I just heard aside, I think you're pretty happy tonight. Your candidate did really well. He held up extremely well. He was articulate. He was a fighter.\par \par \uc2 I thought he did particularly well on the economy, taxes, immigration, and crime. The weakness was social issues. Here's where I thought Newsom was really passionate. Agree with him or not, he was passionate. He stuck to his ground. He articulated his principles. And \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  was stuck with a six-week abortion bill he really didn't want to talk a lot about it.\par \par \uc2 They both had good nights. DeSantis has definitely the best night of his campaign.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Wow, that's a high compliment coming from you. If you were to grade, let's got you, Mark, might as well stay with you, grade both of the debaters, both governors, what would you give them tonight?\par \par \uc2 PENN: I would give DeSantis an A minus. He was articulate, as I said, a fighter. He didn't have a great standout moment, but he really was overall did what he needed to do tonight.\par \par \uc2 I'd probably give Newsom a B, B plus. He had a good night. I don't think he was strong on his state because, after all, the numbers weren't really that good on his state. He was, as I said, passionate about his principles and values, and that counts a lot in the Democratic Party and in the country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Chip, we've got about 15 seconds for you, Chip.\par \par \uc2 ROY: Fifteen seconds. Well, look, Governor DeSantis did a great job. I give him an A. I think he made a clear and compelling case for why freedom works and why it has worked in Florida, why the American people should be attracted to that kind of a vision. And I think, look, Governor Newsom, I can't give him a hall pass for being slick at selling a bad state of California because it is bad because of his leadership. So he gets an F because California is a feeling state.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Thank you both. Mark, appreciate it, and Chip, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, that is all the time we have left this evening. Thank you for being with us. Please set your DVR so you never, ever, ever miss an episode of HANNITY, 9:00 eastern, Monday through Friday.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020231201ejbu0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Special Edition of HANNITY\b0\par\par\uc2 Jason Chaffetz, Jeff Paul, Tammy Bruce, Gregg Jarrett, Jackie  DeAngelis, Leo Terrell \par \uc2 7,850 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 November 2023\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JASON CHAFFETZ, FOX NEWS HOST: Welcome to this special edition of HANNITY. I'm Jason Chaffetz, in for Sean tonight. I hope you all had a very happy Thanksgiving.\par \par \uc2 Well, today, as part of a four-day pause in fighting between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , 24 hostages, including Israelis have been released from Gaza. Remember, these hostages have been held in Gaza since the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks back on October 7th. And after today's release, 240 hostages still reportedly remain captive in Gaza, with an estimated 10 Americans among them.\par \par \uc2 Here now with the latest on the ground in Israel is our own Jeff Paul -- Jeff.\par \par \uc2 JEFF PAUL, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Yeah, good evening, Jason.\par \par \uc2 And we are learning tonight that on top of the 13 people who were released today, we're expecting maybe another 13 could come out tomorrow. But I got to tell you, here on the ground in Israel, the mood is bittersweet, mentioning sort of what you were just saying that there's more than people who are still being held captive in Gaza. But today was a huge and crucial first step.\par \par \uc2 And if this current ceasefire that went into effect at 7:00 a.m. on Friday continues, we could start seeing more and more people coming out. Now, here's what we know about what happened today. According to Israeli intelligence, they say 24 hostages were released by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , 13 of them were Israelis, 11 of them were foreign nationals.\par \par \uc2 Now among the Israelis who were freed, we know that four of them were kids ages ranging from 2 years old to 9 years old. The 9-year-old child actually had his birthday while he was in Gaza being held captive by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Now, three of those people were mothers, six of them elderly women, none of them were among the Americans that were in -- that were being held in there, not at least yet.\par \par \uc2 Now, today, Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  spoke about the hostage release, saying that he is working on to make sure that everyone is eventually sent home.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BENJAMIN NETANYAHU\uc2 , ISRAELI PRIME MINISTER (through translator): I emphasize to you, the families and to you the citizens of Israel, we are committed to the return of all our abductees. This is one of the goals of the war and we are committed to achieving all the goals of the war.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PAUL: Now, we know that Israeli officials have a list of the names of the people who they are expecting to be released tomorrow, but they have said throughout this entire process, nothing is guaranteed until it happens. Local media here on the ground in Israel saying that among the people who are released tomorrow, they think maybe as many as eight kids could be released. We're hoping that ceasefire holds and as long as it does, we're hoping to see more people be released -- Jason.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Jeff, amazing reporting. Thank you. Stay safe out there. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 All right. Joining us now with reaction is Dori Roberts, whose family members were among those released from \uc2 Hamas\uc2  captivity today, and former State Department spokesperson Morgan Ortagus.\par \par \uc2 Thank you both.\par \par \uc2 Dori, it's got to be a bittersweet day. I can't imagine the emotions that are going through what you're feeling. But to have at least three of your relatives come home safe, that's got to be good. But you also had an aunt I believe who was killed in this terror attack.\par \par \uc2 DORI ROBERTS, FAMILY MEMBERS WERE RELEASED FROM \uc2 HAMAS\uc2  CAPTIVITY: Well, thank you so much, Jason, for having me on your show tonight and good to see you again, Morgan. I know we were on this show before and it was very emotional day back then and it's a very emotional day for a whole different reason today. We're very happy to receive our family members back home. They're in the hospital right now, going through medical exams, rejoin with their family. It's been a very, very emotional day to all of us, to seeing our hostages.\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, my aunt, Efrat, was murdered and her body was left by the Gaza border. She was murdered in front of her daughter Doron Katz who is now back in Israel and we are very, very happy to -- for those news today.\par \par \uc2 With that, we have a lot of questions that are still need to be answered. Were they're alone? How they been treated? Were they had any contact with other hostages? We still have about 218 hostages left in the Gaza Strip held by the \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 So we taken this period of time right now to rejoice and reunited with our families and our loved ones. We're very happy for all those families and all those families who received the loved one, but our goal and our mission is still stay focused and keep our actions and our mission ahead is to bring everybody home safe, all of the 218 left in Gaza strip back home to our families, to Israel and to call this as a complete mission to say that everybody are back home with their family, with their loved ones, for the holidays.\par \par \uc2 This is what we're about to do. So we take this time to be happy, but we still have a lot of grief. We lost almost 1,400 lives on October 7th. We now try to rebuild the ones who survived and bring those back to the life they had before October 7th.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: And, Dori, before we go to Morgan, tell me about your aunt. She was murdered in front of family members, on that attack. But tell me about her. What will you remember most about her?\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: My aunt Efrat was very sweet. You can see from the picture that she loved nature. She loved travels. She grew up on the kibbutz.\par \par \uc2 Her entire life and community and family was born and raised on the kibbutz. She was very sweet and kind, very noble, who always found time and attention to give to her kids and her and to us the family. She held us always close and she was a sweet, sweet person that I always remember her gentle touch and her capturing smile her deep eyes and her beautiful hair was always something that I remember from her.\par \par \uc2 And she's now resting peace right next to my mom's grave. That's where we met last time about three and a half months ago when she was there to support me as we lay down my mom. And I will never forget that moment. Right now, she's buried right next to her and we are praying that we'll be able to rejoin and bring our family together once again and hopefully this time to celebrate and not to grief.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Well, fortunately, your cousin and those two young children, ages four and two, are back and safe and they've went through some trauma that I can't even imagine.\par \par \uc2 And, Morgan, I want to talk to you about the look -- you're a mom, but you also worked at the State Department. And so I want to kind of talk about the significance of what this is happening, what this is doing, what this signifies at the diplomatic level because there is no equivalency in kidnapping a 2-year-old and a 4-year-old, and in murdering more than 1,300 people and what's going on today in this -- in this hostage release. It's just -- it's just beyond fathomable on what's happening on the emotional level, but on the diplomatic level, what are you seeing?\par \par \uc2 MORGAN ORTAGUS, FORMER STATE