hen you make that combination?\par \par \uc2 GINGRICH: Well, I think it's very dangerous for the Republicans and very dangerous for the country. What you have today is a nationwide machine on the left, a machine made up of interest groups.\par \par \uc2 I mean, for example, the New York City Democrats are going to be asking for billions to pay for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's illegal immigrants, billions. And they're going to want the money. The city of Chicago, the mayor's is going to want billions. You go across the whole country and what you see is interest group after interest group that's going to want the money.\par \par \uc2 What you have on the Republican side are people who are really worried about the budget. They really want to get to a balance. They want to save Social Security and Medicare -- well, all those things are a direct threat to the interest groups on the left.\par \par \uc2 Now, the difference in a presidential race particularly if \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 's involved is he is such a huge figure, he is not a candidate. He is the champion of millions of Americans, the leader of a movement, very different than anything we've seen in most American history. He can rise above no matter how much money the left has, he has the capacity to reach the American people despite them.\par \par \uc2 And you have to say as of tonight, he's certainly going to be the nominee, and the odds are much better than even maybe three out of five, or four out of five, that he'll be the next president, which as it sinks in, is going to drive the left crazy.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: There's no doubt uh he has a movement like we've never seen which is why they must be deprogrammed in the words of \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Speaker Gingrich, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, the very latest from Israel's war with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Plus, President Biden is either unwilling or unable to deter attack against U.S. soldiers in the Middle East. Forme