wer they look for, some bureaucrat leaks something. In this case, I'm confident that's true.\par \par \uc2 I'm confident that President Biden was presented a full range of options, almost all of which would have been more -- more responsive, more aggressive, more protective of these American soldiers than the ones that they've chosen to take.\par \par \uc2 And so, I think the Pentagon is that signaling, hey, we got to do more if we're going to deter the Iranian regime, we have to at least acknowledge that they were the ones responsible for what happened, the barbaric attacks of October 7th, when in fact the Biden administration has just refused to acknowledge that. We have to do the fundamental blocking and attacking to protect Israelis and Americans and frankly the broader Middle East against these barbaric attacks, by the Iranian regime itself.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: You know, one of those Iranian proxy groups is the Houthis. You know them well, because here's what you did to the Houthis who, by the way, they've taken out a $30 million American Reaper drone. They're now seizing ships that are linked to Israel, that's what they're doing, up to no good.\par \par \uc2 Here's what you did on January 15th, 2021, you designated them a terrorist group, January 15th. Biden, February 4th delist them as a terrorist group. Why would he possibly do that?\par \par \uc2 POMPEO: It's an unexplainable, Kayleigh. They've now committed terror attacks in abundance over the last two and a half years, further demonstrating that what I did in January 2020, excuse me, 2021, was correct. They are terrorists. They're terrorists that much like \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , much like by \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 , much like the militias that are operating inside of Iraq, they are funded, trained directed by the Iranian regime.\par \par \uc2 I can't for the life of me imagine why the Biden administration chose at the very beginning of its time to delist them other than they wanted to go -- the Biden administrat