We have a lot of -- a lot of ground to cover tonight, a lot of breaking news stories from the Biden impeachment inquiry, what I call the \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  bribery and money laundering scandal allegations. The House Oversight Committee, they just subpoenaed \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , James Biden and \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's business partner Rob Walker. They will now be compelled to testify before Congress and this has been a long time coming.\par \par \uc2 The chairman of the House Oversight Committee, \uc2 James Comer\uc2 , will join us. We have all those details coming up straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 First, we have more troubling news from the Middle East tonight. A $30 million U.S. Reaper drone was shot out over the sky, over international airspace by Iranian-backed, you know, the Houthi rebels and terrorists in Yemen. Again, we must start out by asking your commander-in-chief \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Mr. President, what are you going to do about this?\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, we have U.S. soldiers suffering yet another two attacks at bases in the Middle East today by other Iranian proxies. And so far, there have been 42 attacks against our U.S. soldiers carried out by Iranian-linked terrorists in the past month alone.\par \par \uc2 Now, Joe's response was to take out two small empty warehouses, and just hours ago, apparently another, quote, small retaliatory U.S. airstrike against whatever assets they hit in Syria. We'll find out sometime in the next day or two. That's it?\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is -- he's not going to take any substantial action to prevent further attacks against American troops abroad? Is he going to just, you know, keep on bombing empty warehouses? Because think about this, you know, if China -- they have all these hostile actions against American fighter jets in international airspace, no response. China takes hostile actions against our navy and international waters -- well, Joe gives no response.\par \par \uc2 China's spy balloon, what happened? It got to fly eight days over our country, over our military installations. No response.\par \par \uc2 China's hostile actions over Taiwan and their airspace, no response. Russia shoots down our drones, no response. Is it because Joe wants more, what, financial business deals with China and Russia that he won't take action these -- against these hostile regimes, or is he just a pathetically weak U.S. president? We'll let you answer.\par \par \uc2 Now, meanwhile, back at home, antisemitism -- it is exploding. I never thought I'd see this in our lifetime. Any ever think this? Never thought I would see this in our lifetime.\par \par \uc2 Including in the halls of Congress, this as Jewish Americans are now still -- still being held hostage by terrorists in a war zone. And by the way, Joe, why are you not demanding the release of all of these hostages, including Americans that are being held hostage? Where is your president tonight?\par \par \uc2 I'm sure he's sleeping. I'm sure he doesn't know that today is Wednesday. And as anti-American sentiment is on the rise and the threat of terrorism is now spiking, is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  going to do anything to secure our southern border? Is he going to do anything at all?\par \par \uc2 Because we now know the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , there -- you know, there's Alejandro Mayorkas testified today, he has no idea at all how many illegal immigrants are currently in our country, or where they're from, or why they're here. We know, what, thousands from countries like Iran, Syria, other places in the Middle East, Russia, China -- Joe has let in almost 8 million illegal immigrants, and may be 10 million by the end of the year. This is insanity. And it's just another horrible, chaotic day under President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But according to last night's election results, Americans seem pretty unfazed, at least on the surface. We're going to break all of this down. Let's start in the Commonwealth of Virginia where state Democrats were able to hold on to a slim majority in the Senate there, and pick up a slim majority in the House of Delegates.\par \par \uc2 Now some are trying to blame Governor Glenn Youngkin and his expansive get out the vote effort. Here's the reality -- Virginia, whether you want to believe it or not, I had given up on Virginia years ago. It is a blue state. It's not even a purple state.\par \par \uc2 The anomaly in Virginia happened two years ago when Glenn Youngkin won the governorship there, and he deserves a ton of credit for trying as hard as he did to flip both houses. And as the federal government by the way is expanding at a rapid pace, hordes of government workers, the vast majority, 90 plus percent, Democrat, relocating just south the D.C. into northern Virginia, where taxes are low, schools are better and crime is relatively low. And unfortunately, the vast majority of government workers, they're Democrats, so are most of the employees at the NGOs, the law firms and other groups associated with the government.\par \par \uc2 So Virginia was close because of Youngkin's popularity. It's a blue state, in spite of what the media -- what a huge victory, what a -- what -- this is bad for Glenn Youngkin, no, it's not.\par \par \uc2 The fact that Glenn Youngkin won frankly is a miracle. The fact that he won by the large margin he did was another miracle. It just shows what the failure of Democrats can do, can awaken people at least temporarily.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, but once again, we do have to talk about the issue of abortion. It was a major issue yesterday, and I do believe deeply in the sanctity of life. I'm -- I'm pro-life. I'm very open about it.\par \par \uc2 But I also recognize a political truth and reality and that is that the majority of the American people as I have been saying for years, people said yesterday, \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  finally admitted -- no, \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  has been saying it for years that now the consensus in this country, a few years now I've been saying, Americans reject the most restrictive abortion laws. They just do.\par \par \uc2 Now, okay, so people can disagree with me. But now they especially rejected if these restrictions target early pregnancies under 15 weeks. That's the political reality. I'm not giving you my personal view. I'm telling you what, where -- where the consensus of the country is.\par \par \uc2 Even in the state of Ohio, a very red state now, 57 percent of voters there approved a measure adding abortion rights to the state constitution, and Democrats now are using abortion as a political weapon. Not only do they accused Republicans every two and four years of being racist, sexist, misogynist, homophobic, xenophobic, Islamophobic, wanting dirt air, warning dirty water, and wanting to kill grandma and grandpa. Now they're saying that Republicans will end all abortions which is a lie, and the problem has been Republicans have not countered that false narrative in that lie.\par \par \uc2 Now, by the way, this even played a pretty big role in deep red Kentucky where a very popular Democratic governor who totally distanced himself from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  painted his opponent Daniel Cameron as a heartless anti-woman zealot. Republicans need to spend dollar for dollar, every lie the Democrats tell, you must fight back with ads telling people the truth.\par \par \uc2 Over the past two election cycles, Republicans rarely responded to any of these attacks, especially on abortion, they need to start responding. But tonight, it is clear, they must fight back, they need a coherent strategy to counter the abortion narrative, or the abortion lie, or this issue will -- issue will haunt them in 2024 and beyond.\par \par \uc2 Republicans also need to buy into early voting and legal ballot harvesting. They can't show up on election day down by hundreds of thousands of votes, and expect to win. In a perfect world, there would be just one election day, make it a national holiday, paper ballots, voter ID, signature verification, chain of custody controls, updated voter roles, partisan observers watching the vote and watching the vote counting.\par \par \uc2 And if we had all of that, guess what? We would add integrity to our election system and everybody can have confidence in the result of elections. That is not the world that we're living in.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, Republicans that have been reluctant and resistant to voting early and by mail, they need to adapt, they need to organize and they need to beat Democrats at their own game.\par \par \uc2 Here with more, former Arkansas Governor \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 , FOX news contributor Tammy Bruce.\par \par \uc2 Good to see you both.\par \par \uc2 Tammy, let me start with you.\par \par \uc2 TAMMY BRUCE, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yes, sir, everybody.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I wish the country did agree with me on every issue.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I just know the political reality is they do not. Poll after poll, in my view, has shown that, and I think there's got to be a happy medium here. And if Republicans don't get -- if they don't get right on the position and we saw that in 2020, in Pennsylvania, Mastriano had no exceptions for rape, incest, mother's life, he lost by the largest margin to a non-incumbent since the 1940s. I would say because of that one issue.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Many of you may know, I come from the left. Part of my activism was abortion rights activism.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: She used to be the head of NOW, the National --\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: I love that you almost forgot.\par \par \uc2 But I would disagree with you to some degree here. And now, I'm a conservative now. I have in the last year become a Republican. I understand these arguments but I would say that, in fact, it's not even really about abortion. Americans you see on social media, they -- the conservatives are complaining, oh, it's a culture of death. I understand that that is the perspective for the pro-life.\par \par \uc2 But the fact is, this is actually about, I would argue, empathy. It's an -- it's an empathetic dynamic where women do not wake up in the morning and say, oh gosh, I hope this year, I can have an abortion. What I think about is as over 70 percent of the decision regarding have -- for the women who have abortions, 70 to 73 percent is about the economy. They can't afford it. They are working two jobs, and a pregnancy would they would lose their job, they can't afford to raise a child.\par \par \uc2 When the economy is good, abortions go down. I worry about the woman who gets is surprisingly pregnant and she's not expecting it, who wants that child and has to have an abortion because the economy that the system, the swamp sets up, makes it impossible for her to keep that child.\par \par \uc2 So when we think about -- for the pro-life, it's not -- it's just like with the vaccine mandates. Americans don't like being told what to do by the government. They don't want mandates or bans or things like that, and they want a way that where they can make decisions that really reflect their values.\par \par \uc2 Women, if they get pregnant, would want to be able to keep them that child and it's difficult when you can't. So I would argue that for the Republicans and for the pro-life Americans, that this is not about abandoning your values, it's about how do you win to make sure there are fewer abortions. It means an economy that is good. It doesn't mean banning something, because then you're losing that whole real issue about why women are in this position.\par \par \uc2 That's how we win this argument. Right now, when you when you lose in Ohio, and you have a referendum like that, and Democrats get elected, there are more abortions because the economy will be bad, like it is right now. So that's how you win this argument and I think for everyone, it will soften the nature of the issue. It is recognizing that women don't want to be doing this, whether it's a miscarriage or an abortion or any of that, Americans understand this. But women want to be able to do it and do it properly.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me bring in Governor Huckabee.\par \par \uc2 When -- when -- during these election seasons, when Democrats are demagoguing all of these issues, Governor, I believe Republicans don't respond in kind. They have got to answer to any attack, especially if it's a lie. That's number one.\par \par \uc2 Number two, then you have this issue of extremism, those that would support late term abortions or the Governor Northam comment that we have from years ago, or infant -- at some point of viability. Americans don't support that either. I think we're pretty clear on that. That becomes infanticide if the child is viable outside of the womb.\par \par \uc2 So when it comes to parental notification which Democrats don't want, when it comes to issues of late term abortions, I think that is a winning issue for Republicans and mainstream Americans would -- would -- that would resonate with them.\par \par \uc2 MIKE HUCKABEE\uc2  (R), FORMER ARKANSAS GOVERNOR: It certainly would, and I also believe that we have a messaging issue. We don't seem to understand that we need to quit playing defense and start playing offense. It's really hard to score when you don't have the ball, and Republicans keep fumbling and give the other team the ball.\par \par \uc2 We need to focus on one of the things that Tammy said and I would say it a little differently. We need to talk about the fact that we're not against women. We recognize that an abortion has two victims, two victims. Obviously, the unborn child, and the other victim is the woman who's the birth mother who probably got talked into the abortion by a boyfriend, a friend, a mother, a grandmother, maybe a father.\par \par \uc2 And the fact is we're not wanting to punish that woman in any way. We want to reach out and show her compassion and assistance, maybe to keep the baby, maybe to find an adoptive parent, but never to condemn her.\par \par \uc2 And I believe that the other factor that we need to talk about how women are exploited through an abortion. They're not told the long-term physical consequences to their body, or even the long-term consequences to their soul and their psyche.\par \par \uc2 But also, we get bogged down in how many weeks. If we're going to talk about it, let's focus more on something that everybody relates to, more like the heartbeat. If your heart stops, you're dead. If your heart starts, you're alive.\par \par \uc2 Most people can understand that a heck of a lot better than trying to argue nine weeks, six weeks, 22 weeks. We make the mistake of acting like we need to be afraid of the issue. No, we don't.\par \par \uc2 We need to simply say we are for life. We may disagree on exactly how we're going to make that work, but one thing we do agree on is that when you have a pregnancy that's in its eighth month, and you just now decide you don't want it, then no doctor should go in and slice that child into many, many pieces and somehow call that women's reproductive health, because it isn't healthy at all for the baby or the mother.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Governor Huckabee, great to have you. Tammy, always great to see you. Thank you both for being with us.\par \par \uc2 All right. Now, we turn our attention to someone who just won't go away -- \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , once again foisting herself into the spotlight. Today, she joined her humorless friends on that hard-hitting news show called "The View" on ABC, where Hillary actually -- it's a very hard-hitting news show -- where Hillary actually compared Trump to Adolf Hitler. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HILLARY CLINTON\uc2 , FORMER SECRETARY OF STATE: You know, when I was secretary of state, I used to talk about one and done. What I meant by that is that people would get legitimately elected, and then they would try to do away with elections and do away with opposition and do away with a free press. And you could see it in countries where -- well, Hitler was duly elected.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: That's right.\par \par \uc2 CLINTON: Right? And so, all of a sudden, somebody with those tendencies, the dictatorial, authoritarian tendencies would be like, okay, we're going to shut this down, we're going to throw these people in jail, and they didn't usually telegraph that. Trump is telling us what he intends to do. Take him at his word.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, the Democrats doomsday scenarios have only just begun. In fact, Democrats really only have three election day strategies, fearmongering about abortion, fear-mongering about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But last but not least, using the justice system as a political weapon.\par \par \uc2 Right now, we know President Trump is facing the biggest phony witch hunt civil trial in the history of New York. But today, the state forced his daughter Ivanka to testify as a witness and needless to say, the far-left Trump-hating judge was downright giddy.\par \par \uc2 According to "The New York Post", quote, when a state lawyer called the mother of three to the witness stand, while the judge -- the judge in the case, \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 , dryly joked, oh, who's she? Oh, he's a comedian on top of everything else, a showboating judge.\par \par \uc2 Now, throughout the trial, this judge has been abusively biased, constantly ruling against Trump and his family, and virtually every motion, he's sticking to the idiotic, you know, frankly, just insane valuation of Mar-a- Lago at $18 million when it's much closer to a billion, he's guilty of the very thing they're accusing Trump of, and he seemed the judge to take great pleasure in doing so.\par \par \uc2 This is not a fair trial. It's a political hit job. I wouldn't expect this in the USA.\par \par \uc2 Trump, he's not letting this slow him down. Tonight, well, there he is in Florida for a massive rally. Let's take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER PRESIDENT: Our country has never seen the likes of what you witnessed in America last weekend with the menacing mobs of \uc2 Hamas\uc2  supporters chanting their jihad slogans in the streets of our cities. They shouted "Allah Akbar" while calling the barbaric \uc2 Hamas\uc2  terrorist martyrs. They were saying martyrs.\par \par \uc2 In times like these, you can't afford to have a president who wants to be politically correct. We have to do things properly. We cannot have an administration that takes foreign policy advice from \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  or \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 . You can't do that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Here with reaction, South Carolina Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  is with us.\par \par \uc2 Senator, welcome the program. Good to have you.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 LINDSEY GRAHAM\uc2  (R-SC): Thank you, yeah, I wish I was there. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  even today, they're pushing Israel to hit the pause button.\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And I'm trying to understand why they would do that, because when you hit the pause button, they get to rearm. When you hit the pause button they get to resupply whatever they need. When you hit the pause button, they get to restrategize.\par \par \uc2 Shouldn't they be out there winning the war that that they didn't start, that they didn't want, that they now have to finish?\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: I miss Trump. How many of you believe if Trump were president, none of this would be happening?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, let me ask audience, how -- do you -- do you believe this wouldn't happen?\par \par \uc2 (CHEERS)\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Yeah, okay, okay. Here's what I believe, if he were president tomorrow, it would stop tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 But let's talk about \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  -- old, bitter and defeated is no way to go through life. So I support President Trump. It's offensive to me to suggest I'm supporting Adolf Hitler because she disagrees with the way he does business.\par \par \uc2 Here's what President Trump did: he recognized Jerusalem as the capital of Israel. He recognized Golan Heights as part of Israel. He got six Arab nations to recognize Israel as a legitimate one and only Jewish state. That's not Adolf Hitler, that's the strongest supporter of Israel in modern American history.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did more for Israel than any single president. On Biden's watch, more Jews have been killed since the Holocaust. \uc2 Hamas\uc2  saw weakness, they acted and I'll tell you this, if one American is killed by Shiite militia supported by Iran, if one of our soldiers is killed in Iraq and Syria, we should blow the Iranian oil refineries to smithereens.\par \par \uc2 We should destroy their ability to fund terrorism. Let Iran know tonight, you kill an American, we're coming after you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you, Senator, under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , they made this Iranian deal which I thought was nuts giving them billions of dollars. Under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Iran has now been able to sell oil. It's estimated they made between $80 billion and $100 billion, then the $6 billion in payment as a ransom for five hostages.\par \par \uc2 What -- what is it about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and Democrats that think that they can negotiate with the number one state sponsor of terror? I'm -- I'm not understanding it.\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Well, when Obama's president, Putin invades Ukraine, right? When Trump's president, everybody runs and hides in the corner. When Biden's president, Putin invades Ukraine again. When Biden's president, \uc2 Hamas\uc2  kills more Jews than any time since the Holocaust. Afghanistan started this, when he left Afghanistan, a shameful act, that set in motion everything we're talking about.\par \par \uc2 This is the same administration that is having more illegal immigrants cross our border illegally than all presidents combined. They don't know what they're doing on the border. They don't know what they're doing when it comes to bad guys.\par \par \uc2 If you had \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as president, we would secure the border tomorrow. People would listen to him in Mexico and other places because they're afraid of him, If he were president of the United States, this stuff with Iran would end.\par \par \uc2 The only thing that works with bad guys is to be strong. Our border is broken, our policies don't work. It's a matter of time to a bunch of Americans get killed. I will not vote for one dime for any country, including Israel, until we first secure our own border.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Senator Graham, great to have you. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, chairman of the House Oversight Committee, \uc2 James Comer\uc2 , will join us. He just issued subpoenas to Hunter and James Biden, and what is a major development in the Biden impeachment probe as we continue. Thank you all for being with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Hi, welcome back to "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 And tonight, the Biden impeachment inquiry, it is heating up and heating up big time. The walls are now closing in. We have a major development tonight. House Oversight Committee Chairman \uc2 James Comer\uc2  has now officially subpoenaed zero experience \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , Joe's brother James Biden and their business associate Rob Walker for testimony as his inquiry now has gone to the next level.\par \par \uc2 And joining us now, he is the chairman of the House Oversight and Accountability Committee, \uc2 James Comer\uc2  is with us. Sir, how are you?\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 JAMES COMER\uc2  (R-KY): I'm well.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, I asked you a while back, I said, what point do you think it's going to be appropriate to start sending out subpoenas? And you said you wanted to get all your ducks in a row, you wanted to follow all of these suspicious activity reports and all of these shell corporations, follow the money. Do you feel you you've got enough information now that you have some pretty strong questions for these guys?\par \par \uc2 COMER\uc2 : I do. I think we're at the point now where we can connect the dots. We understand what the scheme was. We understand who the people were, who were wiring the money. We believe we know why, but we want to hear from the Bidens, and we're at the point now where the evidence is overwhelming.\par \par \uc2 And now, we can bring the Bidens in and ask them substantive specific questions about things that we have serious concerns about.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How many shell corporations have you been able to discover through your investigation, that the Biden family had?\par \par \uc2 COMER: Over 20, and you know, when you talk about James Biden, I'm not sure exactly what his businesses were.\par \par \uc2 But with respect to Hunter, we're confident that these businesses did not produce a good or service, and we really have no idea what they did, especially considering the fact that they would go months without any revenue and then all of a sudden, a million dollar wire from a foreign national would appear. And then the next day, they would start the laundering process where they would wire money from account to account from shell company to shell company.\par \par \uc2 You know, we see a similar pattern with Jim Biden, but we want to ask Jim Biden exactly, you know, what did you do? What -- what are all these transactions in your so-called business and what involvement did your brother have in these shady business schemes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me -- let me go through the timeline of \uc2 Burisma\uc2 . We know that Hunter admitted on GMA that he had no experience in energy, oil, gas, coal or Ukraine, and he was paid millions of dollars, couldn't explain why, but we have a timeline. It became official Obama administration policy in October of 2015 that that they felt that Ukraine had made enough progress on the issue of corruption, that warranted the loan guarantees, a billion dollars to be -- is the exact amount.\par \par \uc2 We know that five days before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in December of that same year, 2015, went to Ukraine, that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  got on a phone call with his son Hunter and \uc2 Burisma\uc2  executives. We know this is the time when \uc2 Burisma\uc2  executives were begging for D.C. help. Then, we know Joe leveraged that $1 billion of taxpayer money, demanded the firing of the prosecutor investigating \uc2 Burisma\uc2  and his son, and in fact, the son of a B got fired in six hours. And as a result, Hunter continued to get paid.\par \par \uc2 Is that by definition -- does that in your view meet the bribery standards and bribery laws of our country?\par \par \uc2 COMER\uc2 : Absolutely and you, look, that's a quid pro quo. Ironically, that's what the first Trump impeachment was. All he did was ask about the corruption.\par \par \uc2 We have the corruption. You just pointed it out, the timeline is there. We have \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on tape admitting that he fired the prosecutor when he threatened to withhold our tax dollars. So that timeline is a huge concern to our investigation.\par \par \uc2 We also have the timeline with China, with the $40,000 that ended up in \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's pocket that originated from the WhatsApp message where Hunter threatened the Chinese operative to follow through on the commitment they made while \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was vice president.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me -- let me ask you though. That WhatsApp message said, I am sitting here with my father, we're wondering why you didn't keep your commitment, and then saying we are waiting for your call, meaning Joe and Hunter, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had said he never once spoke to Hunter or his brother or anybody for that matter about any foreign business deals. But that app message says that I'm sitting next to my father, why didn't you commit your -- meet your commitment, and between everybody he knows and my ability to keep a grudge, you're going to regret not keeping your word.\par \par \uc2 How many days later was it and how much money was sent into the Biden family coffers? And that, by the way, was an energy company out of China.\par \par \uc2 COMER: Yeah. Five days later, $5 million wired into a Hunter Biden affiliated entity. The next day, he wired $400,000 into the deal that we've heard Tony Bobulinski and others say was the deal where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was going to get percent for the big guy. That $400,000 wire a few days later ended up in a $40,000 check to Joe, exactly 10 percent for the big guy.\par \par \uc2 So, you -- so \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has a China problem and he has a Ukraine problem. Now, we don't know a lot about --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Doesn't he have a Russia problem too because didn't he meet with a Russian oligarch at Cafe Milano?\par \par \uc2 COMER\uc2 : Absolutely, absolutely. He is a Russian problem.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How many Biden -- how many Biden family members got paid and how many were grandchildren and do you know of any work that any Biden ever did for the tens of millions of dollars you've identified?\par \par \uc2 COMER: Well, if you count \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , that's 10 Biden family members. So nine members, excluding Joe, the -- the only two work that may have been involved would have been Hunter and Jim Biden. That's why we're bringing them in first, that there was at least one grandkid, there were several nieces and nephews at a very young age that were getting wires from foreign nationals.\par \par \uc2 So a lot of questions and we're at the point now where you can connect the dots and it's time to bring the Bidens in and that's why we issued the subpoenas today.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. We're looking forward to that.\par \par \uc2 I will say this -- the one thing that \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  has going for him, he does have a great lawyer. He does have Abbe Lowell. Abbe Lowell is a serious attorney in D.C. And we'll see how he plays this. My guess is they're going to try -- my guess is -- my bet is they plead the Fifth..\par \par \uc2 James Comer\uc2  --\par \par \uc2 COMER\uc2 : Abbe Lowell is also representing Menendez, too. I want to make that point.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay, point made.\par \par \uc2 All right. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, Biden's Homeland Security secretary had a disastrous day on Capitol Hill. We're going to show you the low lights and get reaction from Alabama Senator Kate Britt, as we continue.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. So Democrats, they are in disarray. Earlier today, failed DHS Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas appeared on Capitol Hill where he sparred with lawmakers and as per usual denied that there's any crisis at the border. I'm not sure what planet he's from.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: The situation at the border you're saying is not a disaster.\par \par \uc2 ALEJANDRO MAYORKAS, DHS SECRETARY: That is correct.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Despite citing a, quote, imminent need to build more of the border wall in Texas, oh, I thought they said border walls were racist. Anyway, just one month ago, Mayorkas is now singing a very different tune about this. He probably got yelled at after his last appearance. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. KATIE BRITT (R-AL): Do you believe that a border wall is part of the answer, yes or no?\par \par \uc2 MAYORKAS: No.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: He didn't say that a month ago.\par \par \uc2 Now, he had -- well, let's put it this way. His bad day on the Hill didn't stop there. Mayorkas was repeatedly being pressed by Republican senators, including my next guest.\par \par \uc2 Here with more, author of the brand new book "God Calls Us to Do Hard Things", Alabama Senator Katie Britt.\par \par \uc2 I love the title of the book. By the way, good to see you, Senator.\par \par \uc2 BRITT: Thank you so much for having me on, Sean. It's a real pleasure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know what? I mean, I think you're right. I don't think life is easy for anybody. We all face tough times, and challenges and that -- those are the moments that we reach upwards inside and say, God, help us, right?\par \par \uc2 BRITT: Absolutely. I think so many times we see the peaks in people's life, but it is truly the valleys where if you're honest about how you got there, and you allow God to work on you, that he fully prepares you to be able to walk forward and to truly serve his purpose. And so, I think God calls us all to do hard things. He also calls us all to step into the arena.\par \par \uc2 And I think we're seeing right now, more than ever, in this nation, why we need to really cement our values of faith, family and freedom and the next generation, and teach them the things that make this country special so that we as nation can once again do hard things.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We certainly can do better than we're doing now, things were a lot better before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  became president.\par \par \uc2 Let me ask you about the border. When you look at number of gotaways and you look at the number of people that we know have entered this country illegally, it's somewhere around 8 million mark.\par \par \uc2 We know the people are coming from the Middle East. They're coming from Iran. They're coming from Syria. They're coming from Russia. They're coming from China.\par \par \uc2 Do you believe as I believe, and I think I'm 100 percent right, that among these people that Joe has aided and abetted illegally to come into this country, that terrorist cells are among them, and that they are plotting and planning and scheming their next terror attack on this country? I believe with all my heart I am right. I pray to God that I'm wrong.\par \par \uc2 BRITT: I wish you were wrong on that, but unfortunately, I believe you are absolutely correct. Under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , we are less safe on our border, abroad and here at home. It is open season for drug cartels, for human traffickers, and to your point, terrorist.\par \par \uc2 You mentioned the 8 million people who have come here illegally. Today, when Senator John Hoeven asked Secretary Mayorkas the question of how many of them were still in our nation, he had no idea. He couldn't answer the question.\par \par \uc2 When you look at the people who came here, the 1.5 million, 1.67 million known gotaways, meaning people that we saw, but we never touch gloves with, that means they are in this nation. We don't know who they are, where they're going or what their intentions are.\par \par \uc2 When we have complete and total destruction with regards to \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and their barbaric attacks, we know that these people mean death to Israel, death to the Jewish people, we see Iran chanting "death to America" as well, we have to take this serious. We have to secure our border and keep the people in our homeland safe and secure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It should be our top priority. I hope people are listening to you, Senator, because if we don't get this right, this country is going to see an attack probably in the lines of 9/11 or maybe worse, and I pray that that never happens.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 All right. Straight ahead, Squad members are now doing what they do best and that means pulling the discrimination card after the House rightly voted to censure Congresswoman Tlaib. We'll explain. We'll get more reaction.\par \par \uc2 Brooke Goldstein\uc2  joins us as we continue.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. So the House voted last night to censure Squad member Congresswoman Tlaib to over her repeated antisemitic remarks, most notably her endorsement of the chant from "the river to the sea". Now, if you're not familiar with it, I will tell you what it means. It means that is the call for the destruction of the entire state of Israel.\par \par \uc2 Twenty-two Democrats voted to censure Congresswoman Tlaib, but her allies in the Squad, they're not happy about it. Let's take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 AYANNA PRESSLEY\uc2  (D-MA): Mr. Speaker, I rise in opposition to this censure resolution that is blatantly Islamophobic, anti-democratic and an utter waste of time. This resolution is as dishonest as it is unproductive.\par \par \uc2 REP. ILHAN OMAR (D-MN): What is true here is that every single one of them has not acknowledged the fact that Palestinian are dying in the tens of thousands, but we continue to say it is us who are not acknowledging humanity.\par \par \uc2 REP. CORI BUSH (D-MO): This is the place where our Black and Brown staff members repeatedly speak of experiencing racism and sexism, Islamophobia, get pushed off of elevators, xenophobia and more right here in this workplace.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And here with reaction, human rights attorney, founder of the Lawfare Project, \uc2 Brooke Goldstein\uc2  is back with us..\par \par \uc2 Brooke, great to see you.\par \par \uc2 You know, I really -- it really takes my breath away, you know, that this weekend, we saw at our own White House chanting of "Allahu Akbar".\par \par \uc2 It really scares me that in London, they've had massive protests, over hundreds of thousands of people. We've had -- we've heard antisemitic comments in the halls of Congress, Times Square, New York, in college, universities all around this country. In Australia, they actually were chanting "gas the Jews, F the Jews".\par \par \uc2 I never thought I'd see this, Brooke, in my lifetime. What's happening?\par \par \uc2 BROOKE GOLDSTEIN\uc2 , HUMAN RIGHTS ATTORNEY: Me neither, Sean. I'm incredibly concerned about what I see as a major national security threat to this country, and it's certainly not Islamophobia. The very real threat that we are facing in the United States of America is pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  members of Congress, pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  indoctrination on our campuses funded by states like Qatar, and pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  rallies that are turning violent on our streets.\par \par \uc2 Now we can debate the level of anti-Muslim hate or anti-Jewish hate, but what I will not do is legitimize the Islamophobia clarion call by America's number one bigot, and that is \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 , who herself has called for the genocide of the Jewish people, who supports an illegal and racist boycott against Jewish persons and companies, and who spreads blood libels at pro- \uc2 Hamas\uc2  rallies. And I ask you one thing, Sean, because she came out against a bill that was proposed to revoke the visas of Palestinians in the United States, and we can debate the merits of that bill.\par \par \uc2 But if revoking the visas -- if removing the visas of Palestinians from the United States is racist, what then is calling for the removal of the Jewish people from the river to the sea? Is that justifiable racism or is that just the height of hypocrisy?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That is virulent, hatred, antisemitism.\par \par \uc2 There's a gentleman in our audience tonight and maybe we can get a camera on him, he lost a dear friend that was at the concert that day, October 7th. And he gave me this hat before the show and you know this is what Israel is living through.\par \par \uc2 Brooke, always great to see you and our prayers are with the people of Israel as they fight back against terrorism and evil in our time.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, shocking new reports show Bidenomics is failing you the American people. Brian Brenberg, he'll explain as we continue.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. In typical \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  fashion, the president -- he just wandered off stage during his Bidenomics demo day yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Here we go. Joey at his best. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO CLIP PLAYS)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, I'm \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . I mean, he shakes air.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, joining us now -- by the way, no wonder he tried to escape Bidenomics event since Bidenomics are a disaster.\par \par \uc2 Americans now turning to credit cards more than ever before. Look at this, with no ability to pay them off, credit card debt hit a record high of $1.08 trillion just last quarter, and with the total debt for American households now increasing by a whopping $78 billion, well, that averages $145,000 per household. People can't afford this.\par \par \uc2 Now, half the of all Americans say that their financial situation has gotten worse since the 2020 election, only 21 percent say it's improved.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, he's the co-host of "The Big Money Show" on FOX Business, Brian Brenberg.\par \par \uc2 We were just talking to the audience.\par \par \uc2 BRIAN BRENBERG, FOX BUSINESS HOST: Yeah, we had a great conversation. The question I had for them is, do you know somebody who's getting killed by credit card debt right now?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Show the audience. Everyone raised their hand.\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: You know somebody who's getting hit by credit card debt, and we -- they're pointing to people next to them in the audience, that's the point. You know, you saw --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, that is so mean of you to do that.\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: I know, I couldn't believe that, like right on national television. But this is the point, we're living on borrowed time because we're living on borrowed money. Bidenomics stands for borrowing.\par \par \uc2 I know we're talking about yesterday's election. I know we're talking about abortion, the issues that matter. But I'm telling you --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Economy matters.\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: If we run out of steam on that borrowing, people are going to feel it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I read today that we are now annually paying a trillion dollar, over a trillion, just in interest on our debt.\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: You're not getting anything for that. You're not building infrastructure. You're not making America more productive. You're getting nothing but paying off your creditors who are holding that debt and you're paying them $1 trillion a year.\par \par \uc2 We've got a $2 trillion dollar budget deficit right now, folks. That's just the money we're adding through borrowing.\par \par \uc2 What is the point of all this? We can't keep going in this direction. And we're not going to last long?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you this, what other options -- for the 61 percent of Americans living either paycheck to paycheck or borrowing on credit cards or cashing in pensions, I mean, how do they ever get out of that cycle?\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: Well, right now, the biggest thing you can do is be smart. And this is what we're seeing a lot of people do this summer. All the spending we talk about, the consumer spending. You've got a lot of young people, 30 to 39, who say, you know what, I'm not going to have to pay my student debt anymore more and I'm going to go out and I'm going to go to the concert. I'm going to go to the restaurant. I'm going to travel.\par \par \uc2 You can't do that. We are a country that thinks you don't have to honor your commitments when it comes to debt. That is a disaster for us. Number one, you got to fight that (ph).\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Do you know Dave Ramsey?\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Cut up your credit cards.\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: Cut up your credit cards.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: Teach young Americans that debt actually matters and you've got to pay it back. We need a president who can say that and then give us prosperity, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Brian Brenberg, trying to save you money.\par \par \uc2 All right. Unfortunately, that's all the time we have left this evening. As always, thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 Another live audience show -- and by the way, you get free footballs and everything, just go to hannity.com. Your tickets are absolutely free. This is the football you get right there.\par \par \uc2 Set your DVR so you never, ever, ever miss an episode of "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 For news anytime, all the time, every time, go to foxnews.com, hannity.com. In the meantime, and sign up at hannity.com to come to the show tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, let not your heart be troubled. Greg Gutfeld is going to put a smile on your face.\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020231109ejb800001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 MN Supreme Court Rejects Bids To Bar Trump; Democrats Delirious Over Last Night's Elections; Lessons Take Away From Last Night's Elections; New Warning About Foreign Election Interference; Mayorkas Denies Disaster At The Border; DHS Can't Tell Us How Many Terrorists Are In The U.S.; Left Develops Biden Avoidance Syndrome; How The GOP Can Ensure Victory In 2024; USA Today Hires Taylor Swift Reporter; Biden Kill Switches, Coming To A Car Near You; Report Says Search Results Bias Hits 2024 Candidate\b0\par\par\uc2 Laura Ingraham, Ben Domenech, Raymond Arroyo \par \uc2 8,034 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2023\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS HOST: Sad. Tomorrow on Special Report, we talk to Ron Dermer, Israel's Minister of Strategic Affairs, member the war cabinet. Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight. That's it for this Special Report. Fair, balanced, and still unafraid. We crammed a lot in one hour. Laura Ingraham as The Ingraham Angle, next.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Good evening, everyone. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle from Washington tonight. They keep trying to stop Trump, and they keep failing.\par \par \uc2 Late tonight, the Minnesota Supreme Court dismissed a lawsuit that would have kept the former president off the ballot entirely. That was based on a totally bogus claim that he's disqualified from being president under the 14th Amendment. It's just not going to work. So what's next in their bag of dirty tricks to try to stop this guy? Well, we're going to discuss it a little later.\par \par \uc2 But first, what happened and what's next? That's the focus of tonight's Angle. No getting around it. Republicans were once again disappointed last night, big weed and big abortion one in Ohio. The GOP lost its dream of taking control of the Virginia State House and the incumbent Democrat in Kentucky \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , he won. Now naturally, Democrats are leaping to the conclusion that Biden emerges as Superman\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It was a significant victory for Democrats and it couldn't come at a better time for them as there is tremendous anxiety about President Biden's bid for reelection.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Last night is indicative that the coalitions are actually strong.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Boom. Once again, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is underestimated.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, Joe. Now wait, listening to that crowd, do you think that Biden was out there week-after-week vigorously campaigning, Virginia and Ohio, Kentucky? Forget Superman, he's more like kryptonite.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (D), PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: One of the things I convinced president, when I was vice president, I convinced the president to do.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That's the \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  behind him. Now in a \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  poll, Biden's approval in Virginia, is at a lame 43 percent. Meanwhile, in the same survey, Republican governor Glenn Youngkin's approval is at 54 percent.\par \par \uc2 Also, there were some genuinely positive trends for the GOP in Virginia, Republicans won 13 districts that President Biden won in 2020. Republicans won seven districts where the congressional Democratic candidate won in 2022. And look in a state that Biden carried by what 10 points just three years ago, Republicans came within just a few thousand votes of winning majorities in both legislative chambers out of roughly 2.3 million votes cast.\par \par \uc2 So do they wish they did better, of course, but is it a total disaster, far from it. And in Kentucky, let's face this, no one was going to beat Beshear. But at one point polling showed \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2  down double-digits. He came within about what five percentage points. It's not bad, given the power of the Beshear family name.\par \par \uc2 Plus, the good news is that all other major statewide offices in Kentucky went big for Republicans. And then there was Mississippi where Democrats got their hopes up that Elvis Presley's cousin would unseat incumbent conservative \uc2 Tate Reeves\uc2 . But they were all shook up because it didn't happen. Reeves won.\par \par \uc2 Republicans even managed to snag a few victories in New York where Republican Ed Romaine flipped Long Island's Suffolk County Executive seat. We continue to chip away at the Democrat party there. So keep it up.\par \par \uc2 So everyone's asking me today, I mean run into them. What lessons we take from this, what do we do next? Well, first, micro targeting voters matters. Democrats knew that suburbanites in Virginia and Ohio would turn out for the abortion issue, they were right. Almost every Democrat ad that I saw in Virginia over the last what 90 days or so was about abortion. It was nothing about how great the economy is under Biden or the Democrats. So Democrat consultants stuck to that issue, because it worked in the midterms.\par \par \uc2 And with abortion, front and center, the parental rights issue that work for Youngkin back in 2021 kind of got drowned out. This time, Democrats were ready. And by Election Day, the issue was no longer about protecting our kids. It was about keeping Nazis off the school board.\par \par \uc2 Again, it's time to recognize that the suburbs are increasingly Left leaning on the cultural issues. Plus, the Democrats are able to outraise, outspend and better frame these issues than Republicans. And I know now you're hearing this, you're saying OK, so now what? With these dynamics at play, how can conservatives still win? Well, my answer is, of course they can win.\par \par \uc2 Mostly last night's results confirm what we've been saying all along. The GOP must continue to harvest voters from where they are, for the GOP, which is among working class multi-ethnic voters. Right now, we face a coalition of upper-class voters, big business and Far Left cultural warriors. That's not changing anytime soon.\par \par \uc2 Look a few decades ago, certainly back in the 80s, it wasn't this way. Businesses weren't -- they were anti-Soviet, and they were far more pro- American than pro-globalization. The Left was pretty much relegated to college campuses, and a few places like San Francisco, Greenwich Village and so forth.\par \par \uc2 Rich Americans also tended to be more politically pragmatic back then. But that's pretty much changed. But the views of most working-class voters have not changed, which is why it's key that we follow the strategy that Trump began with, economic growth, stuff like lower gas prices, peace through strength, elect Democrats, and you're going to get more inflation, more exploding migrant populations and more war period. That kind of message wins. And we'll prove the overly confident Democrats wrong.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RACHEL MADDOW, MSNBC ANCHOR: Since we've had \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the top of the ticket, they -- Democrats won the presidency. They did fantastically well in 2022. Now in 2023, far exceeding expectations, basically everything they could have won, then won.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Then why are Democrats still so worried?\par \par \uc2 MADDOW: Exactly. Even when Democrats are doing great under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , all they want to do is panic.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Panic. Are the Americans doing great? Panic is exactly what so many American families are feeling now, because of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . And conservatives need to galvanize those people. And these voters aren't just white man living outside the old manufacturing hubs in places like Akron, Ohio, Burlington, Vermont, they're black, and they're brown too. And new immigrants as well who came here for a better life for their children, not what they're experiencing today.\par \par \uc2 So the message might be when we're back in control, you'll be able to keep your gas-powered car and fill it with gas that you can actually afford. When we win, we'll enforce our own border before we spend billions trying to enforce other country's borders, we'll take power away from government bureaucrats and give it back to you, hardworking Americans, who just want a fair shot.\par \par \uc2 Next year's election should be about common-sense. We have it. Democrats have none. So they're celebrating Ohio's ballot initiatives, but those issues didn't stop JD Vance from winning last year, did they? And another reason by the way to believe that Democrats are unjustifiably confident in Biden's 2024 prospects. Look no further than comments made by the matriarch of corruption herself, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HILLARY CLINTON (D) FORMER PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE: \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  was behind at this point in his reelection, my husband was behind at this point in his reelection, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is not only prove that he's done a good job, but look at the alternative. And look at what we would face as a country. And I think the election results yesterday should be very good news for President Biden.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Look at what we face as a country peace, prosperity and a closed border. Yes, Secretary BleachBit is actually trying to convince us that Biden's political skills are on par with Obama's and Clinton's. Yes.\par \par \uc2 The fact is beyond the Republicans being outmaneuvered on the social issues; they were outspent in all of these races as well. So is there a plan? I mean, does anyone have a plan for how to turn that around in 2024? It does not seem like it. And the other point is, as always, the media was egregiously pro-abortion and pro-marijuana and its coverage. Obviously, we know that's not going to change.\par \par \uc2 So again, we must accept these facts and pivot. We have to build on the success that Trump, DeSantis, Greg Abbott in Texas, and a lot of other great governors have found. Their policies appeal to Republicans and independents and open-minded Democrats, including to Hispanics and even more African American men.\par \par \uc2 So is next year going to be an uphill battle? I'm not trying to shy away from that, it is, but Republicans can win. After all, they control about half of the country and their policies make life better for working people. Why else would 76 percent of the country on the Monday poll just released by \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  say we're going in the wrong direction. And that's the Angle.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Ben Domenech, editor-at-large of The Spectator and a Fox News Contributor and \uc2 Phil Kerpen\uc2 , President of the Committee to Unleash Prosperity. Ben, I'm going to talk later in the show about where the GOP goes from here. But what's your take on what happened last night starting in Virginia?\par \par \uc2 BEN DOMENECH, FOX NEWS COMMENTATOR: Well, first off, I have to say, as a Virginian for the three decades of my life, people need to recognize it's a blue state. And it's not the first time that Republican candidates both hardcore social conservatives and people who were Washington insider moderates, Ken Cuccinelli, \uc2 Ed Gillespie\uc2 , they both had to deal with the problem of navigating the abortion issue in that state, they both lost very close elections and that's the kind of issue that's a real challenge in a socially liberal state.\par \par \uc2 In a state that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won by 10 points, Glenn Youngkin came extremely close to achieving Republican ends. And he did so after redistricting that affected a number of these races, situations where you had very close elections where they added 17,000 votes, in particular, to one critical Senate seat from the Democrat side. It's really hard to go up against that. But it's even harder when someone like \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  at the \uc2 RNC\uc2  does not come in and offer any support in Virginia.\par \par \uc2 OK. And that's actually what I would be pointing the finger at, if I was any Republican in Virginia saying, look how close we got, we got this slim margin away from achieving something that could have made this governorship extremely effective for the next few years.\par \par \uc2 But you didn't give any money toward it. You refused the request --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Do they have the money?\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: Well, that's a big question too.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I mean that's --\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: I mean that is a fair question. And -- but the fact that she refused the request that came from the Virginia Republicans for that last minute help in October, that could have been the margin there, a few million dollars here or there could have made the difference in the states (inaudible) --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But again, I don't want to pin the blame on one person here. Because it's not just one person. There are a lot of political consultants that got rich off --\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: Oh, yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: These races, and no matter how wrong they are, they always get hired again, I never understood this about the political consult. I've got to go on that business because I give much better advice.\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: Fail upwards, fail upwards.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Fail upwards. Exactly. But Phil, given the financial disparity here, clearly, Republicans don't have the money that the Democrats have, how to connect that working class message that obviously works in Miami Dade County, it works.\par \par \uc2 PHIL KERPEN, COMMITTEE TO UNLEASH PROSPERITY: Well, look, I think it's interesting that the biggest win of Virginia was actually a race where the Republic had almost no money. It was a Commonwealth Attorney raised in Loudoun County, the Republican I think, spent $70,000 against an incumbent who spent 1.1 million.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Wait, wait and what race was this again?\par \par \uc2 KERPEN: The Commonwealth Attorney Buta Biberaj who spent $1.1 million last --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That was Loudoun County.\par \par \uc2 KERPEN: Loudoun County, she lost because she criminalized parents standing up for their children in the schools and refused to prosecute the actual criminals in the schools. And that did have enough legs to extend through another election cycle, although it wasn't enough to dominate statewide the way that it was --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So Bob Andersen won that seat, Arlington, Arlington, Virginia liberal Fairfax County is so liberal now. It's not in any way moderate. It was in the 80s, mid-80s. When I came here, Fairfax County, Northern Virginia was kind of working class, very moderate Republican. That's totally changed. And Ben, immigration has changed a lot in Virginia, has it not?\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: It really has --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And open borders going to make it worse.\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: It really has. But I also think this is -- this is a failure for Republicans to recognize, you have a new coalition now and you're not going back to the old one. OK. You may have fond memories of the point where you had those upper-class wine moms in the suburbs, coming out and voting for you in midterm elections. But guess who's voting for you now? It's the guy who's building the deck out behind her house. OK. So you have to appeal to him. You have to reach out to him. You have to bring him to the polls.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: To that point, Phil, are Republicans investing in Spanish radio? Because there's an enormous amount of Hispanic radio and television that seems to be fertile ground for common-sense messaging on policies? I'm not hearing anything. Are you hearing any ads in Spanish. I speak Spanish. I haven't heard any ads.\par \par \uc2 KERPEN: Very little. It's very little. And it's a huge missed opportunity. Look, I think that Ben is absolutely right. Republicans are now the party of people who work for a living, OK. The Democrats are the party of the very rich and the party of people who are on government assistance, government dependency, and for Republicans to win, they need to run up the score with everyone who's in the middle economically. And, Laura, I wish they would carry the message exactly like you did in your monologue there, because that's a winning message on the economy. And --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: When I'm president, gas is going to be 2.50 a gallon again, how does that sound?\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: Exactly --\par \par \uc2 KERPEN: Right. What I have such a big -- what I have such a big problem with though is look, I mean, I agree with you. Virginia is a tough state. We did alright. We picked up some seats. The map was tough. But we've got a president who's a total failure --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Total disaster --\par \par \uc2 KERPEN: With a horrible rating, we should be able to win an environment like this. And it's almost political malpractice, that we're not able to --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They ran on abortion in Virginia --\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: It's political malpractice that we let Democrats run away from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . And the responses on abortion are simply not up to the scale that they need to be --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: How did Trump do it. Hillary, you're the radical, you want to rip babies out of the wombs --\par \par \uc2 KERPEN: He went on offense. He went on offense for 20 seconds --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Republicans are scared of the issue --\par \par \uc2 KERPEN: An accomplish more than people who are scared to talk about being away --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: ... let's Democrats to find you on the issue. You can't avoid it anymore --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No --\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: State, local, this is in your territory now. You can't get away with dodging it. You have to come up with an answer and you have to deliver it.\par \par \uc2 KERPEN: The genius of what Trump did is, I think most voters he says Hillary you want to rip babies out and most voters who don't vote on that issue say oh, they're both crazy. I'll vote on the economy. I'll vote on something else. But if you don't -- if you don't give them something to think they're both --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I think they're the radicals --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 KERPEN: I think --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: When does a baby have rights --\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: I have an idea --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: It's a crazy idea, maybe let's start with having an actual organized pro-life movement in the country and then see if there's something that benefits from that.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And Dobbs, what people say was it worth it to have Roe versus Wade overturned? Absolutely, not even a question --\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: Not even a question --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That is like the dumbest question I heard all day. Both of you, great to see you. Thanks so much. All right. Up next, a frightening new report on how bad actors overseas are already getting ready to interfere in the 2024 election. Senator \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2  is here with all the details. But first, where in the world is \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , we'll tell you, very exciting next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PETE BUTTIGIEG, TRANSPORTATION SECRETARY: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 VOLODYMYR ZELENSKYY, UKRAINIAN PRESIDENT: Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 BUTTIGIEG: Thank you for having us over.\par \par \uc2 ZELENSKYY: Thank you. You're welcome. How are you? Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 BUTTIGIEG: Good so far, very good visit.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Of course, Transportation Secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  is just hobnobbing with Zelenskyy in Ukraine. What else would he be doing? I'm surprised he didn't appear in matching Zelenskyy fatigues, he look like his son there, a little kid. Now this year, we've had dozens of trained derailments, including the toxic one out in East Palestine, a spike in aviation near misses, and just bridge collapses, it's no big deal, including \uc2 Phillies\uc2  I-95.\par \par \uc2 But pretty boy Pete is in Kyiv, to talk about rebuilding, even tapping a new infrastructure advisor, not for the U.S., but for Ukraine. What is this? Why is Ukraine asking us for an infrastructure advisor?\par \par \uc2 And more importantly, who's going to be paying this guy's salary? Well, you. Department of Transportation telling the Angle, the funding for the position at the U.S. Embassy, which was a top ask from Ukraine is from a Ukraine aid package, which passed with bipartisan support in both the House and the Senate. Well, if Ukraine asked for it, then how could we say no, really.\par \par \uc2 We'll continue to follow along with Pete's trip. But there's one thing we know for sure. And that's where the Biden Administration's priorities lie.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ANTONY BLINKEN\uc2 , SECRETARY OF STATE: This funding will not only rebuild Ukraine's economy and offset the damage wrought by Russia, but it will also help to reimagine it, investing in new industries, infrastructure and supply chains connected to Europe and to the world.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I can see the buttons and the bumper stickers from 2024 reimagine Ukraine. That shouldn't be Biden's 2024 slogan. That's the only thing they seem to care about.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Two foreign actors, Iran and Russia have taken specific actions to influence public opinion relating to our elections, some voter registration information has been obtained by Iran and separately by Russia. We have already seen Iran sending spoofed emails designed to intimidate voters incite social unrest and damage President Trump.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And now it's about to happen again. Plus, China, new analysis from \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  warning that Russia, Iran and China will likely interfere in the 2024 presidential election. And I think we all know who they're pulling for.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Missouri Senator \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2 . Senator, good to see you tonight in studio, the \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  threat analysis center writes that for those three countries, the stakes are simply too high. The next U.S. president will define the direction of conflict, whether wars might occur, or peace might prevail. I mean, come on, it's pretty obvious who China doesn't want to be the President of the United States. Is it not?\par \par \uc2 SEN. ERIC SCHMITT (R-MO): Yes, and by the way, can I just say something about \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  of the previous segment?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes.\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: I mean, he is in Ukraine, another reason why we should separate this funding, vote on these things individually. The supplemental that has Ukraine funding. I mean, we've got to separate this, but also, he's in Ukraine. He's never been to the Commerce Committee. I'm on the Commerce Committee.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What?\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: We have oversight over the Department of Transportation never once been in front of this committee.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Wait --\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: But he's in Ukraine. So I just find that --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: When I worked at the DOT, we were always up there, not me, but the secretary is always up there testifying.\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: Refuses to answer questions and more interested in world policy than he is --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Maybe you should convene the committee in Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And invite Zelenskyy. And maybe you can get Pete to actually show up --\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: Trick and then to show up. But to your question, I mean, look, this is a serious concern. I think we should be focused on -- there ought to be consequences, by the way, if state actors are engaged in this kind of activity.\par \par \uc2 But I would also say a bit of a warning here, that in the 2020 election, our own government used sort of the Russian hacking leak, pre-bunking of the Hunter Biden laptop story, to affect the election. And we ought to be careful about our own government using this sort of misinformation as a guise --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So, you think that piggyback the misinformation concern, tagging it to those three countries when it actually could be just regular Americans having a conversation. You're worried that that's --\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: Well, I just don't want to see our government engaged in censorship like we've seen under the Biden Administration. And we saw leading up to the 2020 election, there's no doubt in the Missouri versus Biden lawsuit, we've shown this, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was engaged in this but to the --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But China wants Biden -- China's -- they're brokering the big surrender from the United States right now. They say it's a deal. It's a U.S. surrender to China on all these trade issues. They're going to drop these tariffs. That's trillions of dollars over a decade. That's probably a couple trillion dollars for China. alone for trillions of dollars they'll do pretty much anything, will they not?\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: Yes, and this administration is projected nothing but weakness on the world stage and China sees that and that's another reason again, our focus instead of the worrying about this, the sanctity of other country's borders and not our own, we need to be laser like focused on China. And so, we need to retaliate, by the way, when there are cyber warfare, they've hacked into State Department emails, China has, we need to retaliate. But this again, this administration doesn't really want to play --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Retaliate -- they're sucking up to China left and right. I mean, they -- we had a parade of ignoramuses go over to Beijing from the Biden cabinet, one after the other. I mean, this was like, the dating game, the old dating game, I was expecting the big flower decal, it was ridiculous.\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: Well, \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  bowing, being our top high-ranking officials being snubbed by that? I mean, this is a really sign of disrespect --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's humiliation, it's American humility --\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: That's exactly right --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: In its total conciliation. Senator, a few weeks ago, the U.S. Attorney for the Central District of California raised concerns about this happening in local and state elections in his state. He told the Judiciary Committee that we're the gateway to Asia, and we have China trying to influence our elections, trying to target some of our individuals. And this was said, by the way, and he was talking about pro-China. I mean, sorry, anti-China, politicians. And this was this -- this testimony was given while \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  was where, in Beijing. I mean, how beautiful is that?\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: Yes, I mean, look, China's out for world domination. We should put nothing past them. We should take them seriously on all levels. All levels.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, senator, great to see you. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: For coming in tonight. All right. Well, now it's time for a political palate cleanser. Now, look at the two characters I ran into on my way out of the dog park yesterday.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So my dogs are going crazy, because we just ran into the fox and the buck who are friends out in the woods. Look at this. Dogs are crazy. The deer doesn't even care. And I wonder if the fox will follow him.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I know my dog was going -- the dogs were going insane. But the buck kept looking back to see if the fox would come into the woods. They were obviously friends. Anything's possible, senator.\par \par \uc2 All right. If you thought the Homeland Security Secretary could locate the terrorists who have crossed our southern border, think again, we play you the sound and you won't believe it, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Do you believe that a border wall is part of the answer? Yes or no.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: No.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Situation at the border, you're saying, is not a disaster?\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: That is correct.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Those are just a few of the questions that DHS Secretary Mayorkas was able to answer today about the border crisis that, of course, was created with purpose by his boss. What's more striking is what he wouldn't tell us.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: There's 280-something people on the terrorist watch list. Are they out of the country or in the country?\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Senator, they may very well be out of the country.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: But you don't know.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: You came to this hearing today without those numbers.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: That is correct, senator. I'm not aware of a member of \uc2 Hamas\uc2  crossing the border. I don't know that -- I will follow up with you. I can get you that information.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, waiting for that information to flow at any moment. Joining me now, Tennessee Senator \uc2 Bill Hagerty\uc2 , on the Senate Appropriations Committee, who was at that hearing earlier today. Senator, in any professional setting, with the job that he's done, he would have been fired long ago.\par \par \uc2 SEN. BILL HAGERTY (R-TN): Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But this is his job, is to confuse and obfuscate and allow millions of people into the country.\par \par \uc2 HAGERTY: It's Orwellian to hear him speak. And I think this is what has the American public so frustrated, Laura. Beyond frustrated, they're angry about what's happening at our southern border. And this is the architect of that strategy.\par \par \uc2 Today, he could not tell me anything that was truthful at all. He denied the fact that they are asking -- now, the authority to re-purpose all of ICE's budget. They want to basically defund ICE.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I want to play that exchange about defunding ICE. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Senator, I have -- I have never proposed the defunding of ICE. I would vigorously --\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Mr. Secretary, that's the exact -- please read this language that I hand to you here. Are you denying this would allow you the ability to preprogram even one dollar?\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Let me -- let me be clear, senator, because it's -- I would want to read this carefully and in the context.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What document was he reading?\par \par \uc2 HAGERTY: This is his own request. His own budgetary request that he put forward to us that basically asked the latitude to reprogram the entirety of the ICE budget and use it for basically turning ICE into a travel agency to welcome people here, send them by airplane to New York City, and put them into hotels. That's what he wants to do, reprogram up to the entirety of the ICE budget to do just that.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now these cities are getting increasingly frustrated --\par \par \uc2 HAGERTY: Indeed.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: -- specifically New York. And it was just reported that New York has more shoplifting than any city in the past four years. Of course, a bigger problem. So, everything is adding to the problems New York already has.\par \par \uc2 But, as this is happening, we see the administration deflecting and going to, well, the Republicans aren't