erference in your life reporter. For instance, it was barely reported, a big part of Biden's infrastructure bill were kill switches, which will be mandatory in all vehicles in 2026.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, they claim it's a safety feature. It's a safety feature that's automatically going to disable vehicles when the driver is impaired or disagrees with government policies. Did I add that? Sorry.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah. Laura, who determines when the driver is impaired? And who else has access to this kill switch? Congressman Thomas Massey tried to defund that amendment and killed this last night. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: It's so incredible that I have to offer this amendment. It almost sounds like the domain of science fiction. If the federal government would put a kill switch in vehicles that would be the judge, the jury and the executioner on such a fundamental right as the right to travel freely.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Laura, believe it or not, the House rejected that amendment by a vote of 229 to 201 with the help of 19 Republicans. So now these kill switches are going to be in all of our vehicles in 2026.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. This is just another reason to have a 1975 Buick or something. You don't want any of these cars. I mean, why would they be against people traveling, Raymond? Pray, tell, so they couldn't gather together? So, you can't just pick up, like we're going to Florida tonight or we're going to go -- no. They don't want you to have that freedom.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: And you know people are going to be able -- in a foreign government like China, will be able to hack into your car and just shut it down on their whim. This is a terrible idea. And they're talking about lasers and breath, they read your breath as a driver, to see if you're impaired or not. This is way too intrusive. I don't want to surveilled when I'm driving my car. Thanks a lot.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM