vidual.\par \par \uc2 We want to talk to some of the folks who bought \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's art. We think that's important for us to get into. So those subpoenas will be coming. Some of those will start I believe as early as Wednesday, Thursday of this week.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Do you have any doubt that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was active in these business deals? Do you have any doubt that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  lied about what he knew? Do you have any doubt that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  himself benefited financially? Do you have any doubt that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took specific actions when he was vice president that benefited his family members which would be the very definition of the bribery statute in this country?\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Well, there's no doubt that he told us things that were not accurate. He said he was never at dinners, never talked to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's business partners, never talked to the people \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and his team were doing business with. We know that is false. We had that from Devon Archer in a in a deposition, so we know that is false.\par \par \uc2 And we know that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  specifically weighed in relative to \uc2 Burisma\uc2  and the executives who were under pressure after he gets a call from his son, and just a few days later goes to Kyiv and starts the process of firing the prosecutor. So we know that all happened relative to \uc2 Burisma\uc2  and Ukraine. So that sure looks like they told us things that again were not truthful.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Jim Jordan, thank you. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Coming up next, we're going to take you to Capitol Hill. Lawmakers on both sides of the aisle, they are preparing to formally rebuke radical Congresswoman Tlaib after she seemingly called for Israel to be wiped off the map.\par \par \uc2 Also, tonight, more disturbing examples of antisemitism all across the globe. The former prime minister of Israel, Bennett, will be with us tonight.\par \par \uc2 And we continue to watch results around the country on this election night as we continue.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK) HANNITY: We have breaking news tonight out of Capitol Hill. A vote to censure radical antisemitic Congresswoman Tlaib could happen at any moment after she touted a slogan calling for Israel to be annihilated. This is a well known phrase, a well-known antisemitic phrase, from the river to the sea.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now with the very latest, our very own Chad Pergram is with us.\par \par \uc2 Chad, here we go again. It doesn't get any more clear in terms of the antisemitism in that statement.\par \par \uc2 CHAD PERGRAM, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Well, this has been a big divide that they've had in the Democratic Party here with \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 . Many of the Democrats who I talked to today, they indicated that they did not like her language. And there was some uh who voted against -- against bringing this to the floor earlier today.\par \par \uc2 Jared Moskowitz\uc2 , a Jewish member, a Democrat from Florida, and he said that he voted to table or kill this resolution earlier today, but he would vote to censure.\par \par \uc2 I should note that in about past half hour or so here, they made the decision to go ahead and put this on the floor and censure her tonight. She will become House member in history to be censured. It just takes a majority vote. The last one who was censured was Adam Schiff, the Democrat from California. This was back in June.\par \par \uc2 And you know, there was another effort by \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  to try to censure \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  tonight, but they've pulled that from the floor.\par \par \uc2 And also, some Democrats have thought that this tit for tat, there was a resolution to try to censure \uc2 Brian Mast\uc2 , the Republican congressman from Florida. This was something that was put together by the Democrats earlier today. Sarah Jacobs, a Democrat from California, and they -- we believe are going to withdraw that as well because Democrats don't want to get into this tit for tat.\par \par \uc2 But sometime, probably after 10:00, is when the House of Representatives will vote to censure to Tlaib, and there is something different about this resolution. Usually when they censure a member, you have to appear in the well of the House and you stand there and the speaker of the House wraps the gavel and says you have been censured.\par \par \uc2 If you look closely at the text of this resolution, that's not in there. That's not the way they censored Charlie Rangel back in 2010. It's not what happened with Adam Schiff, where it was kind of a party in the well of the House where many of his defenders came, the Democrats came to the well and all rallied around him and you couldn't even hear what the speaker was saying.\par \par \uc2 So this is going to look a little bit different. Once you have been censured, once that vote is closed, she is censured and that is entered in the journal of proceedings of the House of Representatives, and that's it. She will have been censured -- Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Chad, thank you for that hitchhiker's guide to all things censure, especially with Congresswoman Tlaib.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, for weeks, now thousands have taken to the streets, echoing Tlaib's hateful, virulent antisemitic rhetoric, and sadly, these rabid anti-Israel riots are getting worse and so are the chance from the protesters. Take a look at what they were screaming outside of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's White House this weekend.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO CLIP PLAYS)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Allahu Akbar, sound familiar? Yeah, those were words echoed by some of the pilots on 9/11/01, as they killed 2,977 Americans.\par \par \uc2 Here now with reaction, the former prime minister of Israel, \uc2 Naftali Bennett\uc2 , is with us.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Prime Minister, good to see you.\par \par \uc2 NAFTALI BENNETT\uc2 , FORMER ISRAELI PRIME MINISTER: Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: For the life of me, I do not understand the United States of America -- Israel stood strong with America post-9/11. You guys never wavered ever, and here, this is the worst terror attack in Israeli history and we have an American president and administration pressuring Israel to put a pause on defending your homeland, defending your country? Has that been happening?\par \par \uc2 BENNETT: Well, I want to explain, Sean, the meaning of a pause in the -- in the war. Right now, we've embarked on inevitable war to eliminate \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . There's no way that we can accept a terror state that did what it did on our border. The moment we pause in the middle of the war, it gives time for our enemies to replenish themselves, to rearm, to freshen up, and in effect it lengthens the war. Every day of pause is another two weeks of war, which means many more dead people on both sides.\par \par \uc2 It would be tantamount to say January of 1945, that the allies would tell Germany, you know what? We're going to pause the war for a few days, take your time, we don't want to hurt civilians and the war would have continued into the 1946, 1947. The best way to save lives is to accelerate the war, beat \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and this whole nightmare will be over.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you, Mr. Prime Minister, and this is important to me, doesn't the net result have to be the elimination of not only \uc2 Hamas\uc2  but \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  and Lebanon. Doesn't the net results have to be that neither Lebanon nor Gaza can no longer be launching areas for the hundreds of thousands of rockets. I've been there when they've been fired, I've been in the terror tunnels, doesn't this have to end with those areas no longer being a launching pad to attack Israel with those rockets? Doesn't that have to come to an end?\par \par \uc2 Doesn't it also -- don't you have to destroy all of this network of terror tunnels? I've been in them -- don't that -- doesn't that have to be part of the equation too? And at some point, doesn't somebody need to deal with the head of the snake and that being Iran that is orchestrating all of this with their proxy wars?\par \par \uc2 BENNETT: I think you're absolutely right. We have an octopus of terror. The head is Iran and the arms are \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 , \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , Islamic Jihad and the terror cells around the world. And those who are fueling it are sitting in Tehran and they feel immune. What we need to do is ultimately hit Tehran as prime minister.\par \par \uc2 When I was prime minister of Israel, according to foreign sources, when they messed around with Israel, there were commanders of Al Quds terror units that were assassinated in the heart of Tehran. There was a drone base in Iran that was bombed and that's what we need to do because fighting just the arms -- fighting just the arms of the octopus doesn't really make sense and you're right about that (ph).\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Mr. Prime Minister, I only have about 30 seconds left. We have seen, you know, "from the river to the sea," we've heard that. I never thought I hear the words "gas the Jews, F the Jews' and all this virulent antisemitic rhetoric in the United States, on college campuses, in the halls of Congress and worldwide.\par \par \uc2 I've never been one to use Nazi analogies, but this sounds eerily like the 1930s to me and all that I've learned in history. I had no idea that this level of hatred existed. What is your reaction to it in the 30 seconds we have?\par \par \uc2 BENNETT: Sean, me neither. I never imagined that on the ground of the United States of America, we'd hear people chant effectively "kill the Jews", because that's what "from the river to the sea" means, because that's where the state of Israel is. But there is a response, there's one way to do away with all this anti-Semitism in America and our war with the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and that's total victory on \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Defeat them, hit them, kill