at.\par \par \uc2 So we have to stick to the 80 percent issues and if we do that we can take that issue off the -- off the page.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We'll give you the last word on all this, your take tonight, Stephen.\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN MILLER\uc2 , FORMER SENIOR ADVISOR TO PRESIDENT TRUMP: Yes, well, let's just stay on this point. Republicans need to learn how to talk about abortion in a way that is going to appeal to suburban voters, single mothers, married mothers, women across the political spectrum. President Trump's emphasis on having the ex -- the exceptions for rape, incest, life of mother worked, his emphasis on the barbarism of late term abortions worked.\par \par \uc2 Look at how Trump trounced in Ohio compared to the results tonight. Republicans need to understand as President Trump did how to talk about abortion in a way that wins elections. And then we have to combine that with ballot harvesting, on the ground operations, door-to-door canvassing to be able to succeed in 2024.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. We appreciate you both. \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , thank you. And Reince Priebus, thank you.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, we'll check in with our Bret Baier for the latest election results all across the country. That's next. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. We are tracking election results all around the country in the Mississippi governor's race, along with what's going on with Virginia, the legislature, and much more. Bret Baier is back at the big board.\par \par \uc2 Busy night tonight, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Hey, Sean. Yeah, just got some results in the referendum. Ohio, we've been talking about now legalizing marijuana in Ohio, 56 to 54, legalizing marijuana in Ohio. You talked about abortion, that is about the same, 56-44, putting those individual rights into the state constitution. That may have other ramifications.\par \par \uc2 Virginia, we're looking closely at the state sena