t our troops, the leadership.\par \par \uc2 This is a horrific assault on Israel that needs to be managed by them and smartly, and I have full confidence, they're going to do just that. And we should support them 100 percent. And at the same time, we need to be very careful not to get give the Biden Defense Department carte blanche to make a horrible situation, even worse because if anyone can make it worse, they can and draw us into another nearly two-decade war in the Middle East. And that's the Angle.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now, Newt Gingrich, former Speaker of the House and Fox News Contributor. Newt, what's your reaction to what we're seeing on the ground tonight in Israel, it looks like the very beginning perhaps, of the Israeli response to this horrific assault, targeting even women, children and the elderly?\par \par \uc2 NEWT GINGRICH, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, my hope is that this is the beginning of an all-out effort to destroy \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , to go into Gaza, to methodically track down every element of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , and literally destroy it. The same way, we destroyed Nazi Germany.\par \par \uc2 The fact is, these are evil people. I mean, how can you watch what they've done in the last three or four days, and not realize you're dealing with pure evil? And they're very open about it. I just did a newsletter about the fact you have quote, after quote from \uc2 Hamas\uc2  leaders, not a single Jew will remain. What do you think that means? These are people committed fully as much as the Nazis to genocide. And I think that, my hope is that the Israelis will decide that they are now not going to just bomb them, not just going to cause some damage, but that they are going to methodically destroy the capacity of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , wipe out not just its leadership, but arrest every single member who's been active militarily in any way, and create an alternative government in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Anything short of that in five, 10, 15 years from now, we're going to be right back at the same horrible situation. So I think this is a very, very important turning point. And I think Biden can make a real contribution this evening, there is $6 billion, sitting in a bank in gutter that has not been released to Iran. Biden should prove he really favors being active by simply freezing that money, taking it away from the Iranians. He could, for example, be turned over to the Israelis to be used to rebuild all the things that \uc2 Hamas\uc2  has destroyed in the last four days, that would be an intelligent, active step to strengthen Israel, and to weaken Iran.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Newt, doesn't it also show us how important as I mentioned in the Angle, how important it is for America to have a president who is sentient and reassuring and knowledgeable enough to be able to go on camera, address a situation with a specificity that's necessary, reassure the nation, and then clearly pledge unwavering support for Israel. And yet, our president is nowhere to be seen, three minutes on Saturday. And we're supposed to all trust that they know just the right path forward.\par \par \uc2 GINGRICH: Well, I mean, first of all, no serious person thinks that this administration has a clue about what it's doing. There are reports you know, that some of the American weapons from Afghanistan are now being used by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , which would just be a further example of the collapse of the American system, under the Biden leadership. Remember, it's not just about being sentient, and having cognition, Obama was a very clever person, he was just totally wrong about Iran.\par \par \uc2 You can believe the wrong things and be very articulate. You can also be totally inarticulate, which Biden is. But the reason I'm bringing up the $6 billion, is it's a straightforward test. And the Congress should, if necessary, pass a law. And I think they get an overwhelming vote in both House and Senate, that says, this money will be taken back, and it will be turned over to the Israelis to help them rebuild precisely the damage, which remember, the Iranians planned all this, the Iranians funded this, the Iranians provided the weapons and the training, and the Iranians gave them permission to do it.\par \par \uc2 So to make the Iranians pay for rebuilding Israel would have, I think, a certain justification, and would be a real -- a practical, real signal that this stuff is going to cost Iran more and more and more, the more --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The problem is -- sorry to interrupt. But the problem is the administration does not actually admit that Iran is behind this. In fact, John Kirby went out of his way on with Martha earlier to say, well, we don't have that information. We don't really -- we can't really connect those dots.\par \par \uc2 GINGRICH: Of course, they do.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So I don't think there's going to be any recognition on the part of this administration on that. Real quick. Sum it up.\par \par \uc2 GINGRICH: Well, I just don't -- I'm just (inaudible) with Victor Davis Hanson earlier about people in the West Bank always lying. This administration always lies. Why would you think anybody in the Biden Administration would ever tell the truth about anything? They can't survive if they tell the truth. But this is a straightforward test and I hope that Schumer gets back from China. I hope the Republicans get their act together in House and I hope they pass a law and overwhelm the president's veto. Take the six billion dollars and give it to Israel to help them rebuild what Iran helped destroy.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right. Newt, thank you so much. Now former director of National Intel, John Ratcliffe, is here on how this planned attack was missed. Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: This is an attack that I don't think anyone saw coming in the immediate.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Was it an intelligence failure, Mr. Secretary? Do you acknowledge it was an intelligence failure?\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: We will have plenty of time to -- the Israelis will have plenty of time to look into that. All of us will have time to look into that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We didn't see it coming. Joining me now, John Radcliffe, former U.S. director of National Intel under President Trump. John, what's your read of what happened here? President Trump spoke in Wolfeboro, and laid out the reasons why \uc2 Hamas\uc2  did what he did -- what it did. It was very compelling. And we're going to play it actually right now.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT: If we reduce the Iranian economy, and I withdrew from the disastrous Iran nuclear deal, impose the toughest ever sanctions on the regime. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  undid it. He undid it all and gave billions and billions of dollars to the world's top sponsor of terror, tossing Israel to the bloodthirsty terrorists in Jihadist.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, I guess nothing seems as simple as it sounds, but that's pretty convincing to me. Your reaction.\par \par \uc2 JOHN RATCLIFFE, FORMER TRUMP NATIONAL INTEL DIRECTOR: Yeah. No, it is pretty simple. This wasn't intelligence failure, and it was, in part, because the Biden administration changed the priorities. President Trump correctly outlined under the national intelligence priority frameworks, we focused on the eradication of the ISIS caliphate, which we achieved. And we focused on Islamic terrorist regime, Iran, minimizing their influence. We were very successful.\par \par \uc2 The first thing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did when he came into office was to scramble all of that, and to state clearly that the intelligence community would focus on our top national security threat, climate change. Since that time, he's added focusing on domestic violent extremists, which they have defined to include parents and Catholics, and even now, Trump supporters.\par \par \uc2 So, you know, the idea -- you know, the intelligence enterprise is very good at focusing on what the administration wants. And in this case, we had him focusing on the weather instead of on \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , and I don't think anyone should be surprised at this kind of an outcome, unfortunately.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Blinken is continuing to spend, John, the administration six-billion-dollar Iran deal, raw deal. Here he was on CNN.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: No U.S. taxpayer dollars were involved. These were Iranian resources around and accumulated from the sale of its oil that were stuck (INAUDIBLE). They were moved from one account to another, in another country to facilitate that use.\par \par \uc2 As of now, not a single dollar has been spent from that account. And it's deeply unfortunate that some are playing politics when so many lives have been lost.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Playing politics. They never play politics on any issue, John. But Newt said, if, you know, we release some of these transcripts of the phone calls that Blinken's had, and if they're as bad as it seems, like, as they've been, he should step aside.\par \par \uc2 RATCLIFFE: Well, Laura, that is so disingenuous what \uc2 Anthony Blinken\uc2  said. But let's even assume that that's true. What's his explanation for, at the very moment that he was negotiating to give that $6 billion in exchange to Iran, in exchange for U.S. hostages, that Iran was at that very same moment working with \uc2 Hamas\uc2  on a plan to take more hostages, including possibly U.S. hostages, in addition to killing, you know, hundreds of Israelis and an American.\par \par \uc2 So, you know, and it's not even 6 billion over the course of two years, we've documented how the Biden administration's policies have enriched Iran to the tune of $60 billion by the easing of restrictions, not enforcing sanctions, allowing Iranian oil sales, all of that.\par \par \uc2 And the last point on this is, to say that there's no link. Look, the best intelligence is direct intelligence. And when \uc2 Hamas\uc2  leaders go on camera, and thank the IRGC for their participation, that's the equivalent of a signed confession.\par \par \uc2 And it's so disingenuous for \uc2 Anthony Blinken\uc2  to try and spin this as somehow Iran's not involved when so clearly, they were.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah. But the State Department and the Pentagon want black checks from Congress because they're so trustworthy. Wall Street Journal's piece on this was fantastic, how Iran planned over several weeks these attacks with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . John, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Now, after these just -- you know, horrific. The words don't even describe it. Events of the weekend. Do the members who took out Kevin McCarthy have any regrets? Any second thoughts? Congressman Nancy Mace responds next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Do you envision any scenario in which you could be a candidate for speaker, especially with the deadlock in Israel?\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Look, this is about a moment in time. That's a decision by the conference. I'll allow the conference to make whatever decision. Whether I'm speaker or not, I'm a member of this body. I know what history has had, and I can lead in any position it is.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: McCarthy not ruling out a return as speaker as Israel's crisis unfolds. The Republican conference just met on Capitol Hill ahead of tomorrow's speaker's forum. Joining me now is one of those Republicans who voted to remove McCarthy, Nancy Mace, South Carolina congresswoman. Congresswoman, thanks for being here. Are you concerned about not having a speaker in place, especially when we saw the horror of what unfolded over the weekend in Israel?\par \par \uc2 CONG. NANCY MACE (R-SC): Well, for starters,