p until nine months.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Right. So, what -- again, what's your position there and how specifically have Republicans been hostile to women? Because to make that kind of comment, you have to have something to back it up.\par \par \uc2 MACE: Oh, for sure. I mean, I have pro-life groups that I have done legislation with as recently as the first of this year that will not work with me now because I am pro-birth control. Why can we not talk about birth control and access to birth control in this country?\par \par \uc2 As I -- as that clip just said --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Is that raise of birth control not readily available in the United States? Is that really? I mean, that sounds like a Democrat talking point.\par \par \uc2 MACE: No. Well, I just -- you just played the clip where I said that there are 14 counties in my state of South Carolina that don't have a single OBGYN doctor. So how are they supposed to get access to birth control? Now, my conservative governor, \uc2 Henry McMaster\uc2 , Last year when Roe was overturned, he got access to the pill for women from the pharmacy, so you didn't need to do that.\par \par \uc2 And so, there are a lot of things that we can do to show women that we care. It's not just always related to abortion either.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I think the point is, the most -- the number one thing that's most important to women is the economy. I mean, and I think playing into all these other issues, not that they're not important, to me that just gives the Democrats a huge opening against Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Because, again, the fanatics are those who want to deny when human life begins, in my view. If you believe in science, life begins at conception.\par \par \uc2 MACE: Well, somebody go ask \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  what her end date is. She can't tell you because it's up to nine months. Or \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . They won't tell you --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I just think that's a better approach for you. I'm telling you, do whatever you want. But we'll save our cannabis discussion for another day. Can we agree on that?\par \par \uc2 MACE: We can agree to disagree on that one.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right. And I was laughing that -- thank God I didn't have my red blazer on because you and I really would have looked ridiculous. Thank you for coming in.\par \par \uc2 MACE: You look good in army green.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Great to see you. Thanks so much. All right, after these barbaric attacks in Israel, some in the media rush in to defend \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Raymond Arroyo has that report next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Fox News contributor, Raymond Arroyo, is with us. Ray, have you been monitoring the media reaction to this terrorist attack in Israel now?\par \par \uc2 RAYMOND ARROYO, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: I have been, Laura. And it's startling. It's actually quite dangerous, because it's the way that the media is characterizing this surprise attack by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  on civilians in Israel. Listen closely.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Boy, would they wish that those same Israelis who were out there protesting the so-called judicial reforms would be protesting Israel's inhumane treatment of the Palestinians who live under Israeli occupation.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: You've got 2.2 million people crowded into 141 square miles, so they automatically become the victims of Israeli airstrikes. And it's basically like living, Alex, in an open-air prison.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: The prime minister of Israel, the most right-wing in its history, the most far-right extremist Jewish nationalists, Jewish supremacist government that has existed in Israel.\par \par \uc2 The rhetoric that has come out from Israeli politicians towards the Palestinians in the West Bank over the past several months has been vile, has been disgusting.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah, I wonder if it's been as vile as slaughtering civilian women and children. I mean, look, there's no justification, Laura, for the kind of barbarity and slaughter of innocent people, civilians. They're at home, they're outside at concerts, and these guys are parachuting in and shooting teenagers in the back. Raping children, rounding them up, and women. These are not the acts of a legitimate government. I'm sorry. And this is an outrage that they're trying to frame it that way.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And the Journal just did this unbelievable piece, investigation of what Iran has been doing over the last several weeks to help plan this with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . And Kirby's asked about this, like, well, we don't really have anything to say. We don't have anything to say about that. How does the Wall Street Journal know about this?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah, but everybody else is clueless. Laura, CNN wasn't much better. Christiane Amanpour, she was pouring it on thick with a battalion of pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  spokesmen, starting with this guy, who's talking about \uc2 Hamas\uc2  butchering civilians.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: What other choice did they have?\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Do you condemn what \uc2 Hamas\uc2  did inside Israel to Israeli civilians? There are dead and there are hostages.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: First and foremost, the Western media most really abandoned this framework that has gotten us to where we are today.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: OK, but the fact that Israel is an occupying power, the fact that Israel has violated international law and Palestinian rights.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: It's really unbelievable, Laura. It's like -- it's where they're dealing and talking about Canada and the United States. The people in Gaza elected \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . It's the \uc2 Muslim Brotherhood\uc2 . It's an offshoot of the \uc2 Muslim Brotherhood\uc2 . It's a terrorist organization. That is their government. Of course, this was going to happen. And now Iran is pulling their strings, and the blood and the bloodshed follows.\par \par \uc2 But to justify this, in any way, if they want to protest the land and contested land, fine. Find a diplomatic solution. Killing children and women is not the way.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They're making justification for this. Raymond, I was in Sderot in Ashkelon in 2006. I think it was 2006, 2007, from my radio show back then. And it was always, it was so precarious being in Sderot where the Qassam rockets would, you know, kind of, you know, they were kind of, they weren't the most sophisticated rockets, but they were coming across, and they did damage. They killed people.\par \par \uc2 And the proximity of being next to Gaza, that close with the \uc2 IDF\uc2  when we were there, it was chilling. And you felt it, you felt the tension.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: We have a little breaking news. Special Counsel Robert Herr has spent the last two days interviewing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  related to those classified documents he had in Delaware, and in his office in DC. That's breaking news.\par \par \uc2 How much you want to bet Biden doesn't remember a whole lot and his most frequented word is probably, anyway, I got to go.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, why didn't they just say that? I mean, we were railing against Biden not appearing on campus -- on camera.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Right.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Why didn't he just say that? Raymond, thank you.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: That was the lid. The lid was because he was being interviewed by the special counsel.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Again, they can't -- they can't be honest. That's it for us tonight. Don't forget, set your DVR. We always want you to stay connected with us. Also, on social media. Thanks for watching. It's America, now and forever.\par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020231010eja900001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 The Left Sees Any Opposition As Criminal; \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  Welcomes Oppositional Protester To His Event; \u