y first wish is related to that last story. People wonder, how did the first dogs, Commander and Major, become so aggressive? Well, we found some video that might answer that question. Look at how Biden treats Commander as he exits Marine One here. Watch this. They'll put the video in.\par \par \uc2 Look at this. He kicks the poor animal. No wonder Commander went full Cujo on the White House staff. The dog's trying to get to the big guy, who apparently has a habit of kicking him. \uc2 Judicial Watch\uc2  reported that not only does he kick and punched the dogs, but he may be abusing them in all kinds of ways. I wish President Biden would stop abusing his pets.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: Oh, no, no, no, Raymond, it's the mean Secret Service agents with the guns. That's what the White House staff told us. Crazy. He only has 25 percent of Democrats wanting him to run. You might have lost half of them with the kick of a dog.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah, I agree.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: All right. What's your second wish?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Oh, second wish. My second wish is that the airlines would stop encouraging their flight attendants to cross-dress in the air. \uc2 British Airways\uc2  released these photos of a male flight attendant in a dress. And Virgin Airlines also updated their uniform policy. Basically, in-flight attendants on these airlines can wear whatever they desire.\par \par \uc2 But it can be confusing for the customer, Kayleigh. I mean, at this point, I'm afraid to look up the new Hooters uniform policy. You'll never know what you're going to find.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: Yeah. I mean, look, I will say this, our flight attendants, they are great, Raymond, and they get a lot of crap from passengers. So, I'll take it. I'll take it. Just be nice to our flight attendants.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: OK.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: All right, Raymond --\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I agree. But you know, the thing you can't be offended if they call your man and you're not, which I saw the other day if you're in the costume, OK.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: OK. Third wish. If you are the mayor of Burbank responsible for protecting citizens, I wish when asked about your support for the police, you wouldn't say this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Complete transformative change in our society to move to a police-less state. You do something bad, you got to get punished. That works when you're five. As an abolitionist, my policies resonate with the average American.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: Yeah --\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Is another bite there where he where he actually says, I'd support total police-less cities. I mean, that's what he supports this guy.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: So, all I'm thinking about right now -- first of all, this Mayor Burbank, he's absolutely nut. He said some really weird things outside of policing. I'm just thinking of Abigail -- she's that moderate Democrat, barely won her seat. She picked up the phone and tell democrats, stop saying defund the police. She's probably throwing something at the wall right now, like, get out of here.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Well, three weeks ago -- only a few weeks ago here in Burbank, there was an armed robbery at a \uc2 Rite Aid\uc2  where, you know, people were pistol-whipped. We need police in every locality. This is crazy. And I guess he's worried, you know, corporal punishment he's against, too. He was the guy that had the drag queens spanking him a few weeks ago. Everybody saw that video.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: Oh, my gosh. That's right. That's right. That's what I was thinking of. Raymond --\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Maybe that's corporal punishment he supports.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: Oh, maybe so. Raymond, you are traveling on your book tour this weekend, The Magnificent Mischiefs of Tad Lincoln is out. You gave my daughter, Blake, an advance copy. So sweet. Where are you headed?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Well, I'm