\uc2 , FOX NEWS ANCHOR: Hi. Welcome to Hannity, the second Republican debate is now in the books. And we are live from the spin room at the Ronald Reagan Presidential Library in beautiful Simi Valley, California. Coming up in just moments, Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  Nikki Haley, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , Senator Tim Scott will join us right here on set.\par \par \uc2 By the way, someone you might not expect to see it a Republican debate California Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  will join us. I got to ask him I came to the state, first thing I see is $7 a gallon for gasoline. We got a question or two to ask him. But they do have In and Out Burger anyway. At first sparks were flying at tonight's debate as all seven candidates easily demonstrated the ability to run circles around \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . We can start with that point.\par \par \uc2 We're going to get Laura Ingraham's take in just a minute. But first here with reaction in the spin room, Fox News contributor Kellyanne Conway and Fox Business host \uc2 Larry Kudlow\uc2 . Good to see you both. All right headlines you run away with.\par \par \uc2 KELLYANNE CONWAY, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: anybody on that stage to do a better job than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . I think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a little bit of a winner tonight, because when his name was invoked, they kept saying he should be here to defend his record. He should be here to debate. He should be here to face to people. Why would you want in there when he's going to eat into your time? And I think eating to some of their sound bites.\par \par \uc2 I thought it was a little flat today. I thought everybody had a good moment. But moment shown will not overtake a front runner leading by 40 points, moments won't tell the American people what you would do differently.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's got to be a big moment. We're in the Reagan Library so we could say this. Remember, there was a lot of questions about Reagan going into the second debate with Mondale and he turns to him and he goes, I will not allow my opponent's youth and inexperience become an issue in this campaign.\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: There was nothing like that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Even Mondale started laughing. It was game over at that point.\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: There's nothing like that tonight. But look, I think everybody did well enough to make it to the next debate in Miami, which probably is their goal. The question is, what are you doing in during the five weeks in between the debates, these are important nights, but you got to get out there and mix it up with the people. And I actually thought that the moderators are very well prepared. I -- you get extra credit if you actually answered some of the questions they came to play with.\par \par \uc2 They had certain things they wanted to say. And they got it out they took on China, which is great. There was a little bit of more of an economic plan on how to turn around Bidenomics and inflation. Young people can't afford a house yet. People are in debt, 40 year high mortgage interest rates, 40 year high of inflation. People are suffering every day. I think there was enough connective tissue from these candidates tonight, that they can make a case. I know a little bit more about your struggles and maybe \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . But I don't I think the polls aren't going to move much.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes, Larry?\par \par \uc2 LARRY KUDLOW\uc2 , FOX BUSINESS HOST: Yes, there were a lot of little moments, no big moments. It's hard to get a big moment. Remember, Reagan said to Car (ph) there he goes again.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It will, there it goes again.\par \par \uc2 KUDLOW: I mean for 40 years that people have been using that line. So it's hard to get a big moment. I agree with Kellyanne. I wanted somebody to say, as per Reagan, I kind of worked for Reagan long time ago, I'd come in to the Reagan Library. We played all these Reagan clips on my show this night. I wanted someone to say as per Reagan, that government is the problem, not the solution.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes. I actually played that clip of Reagan when he said it. The word was nine words I believe in English.\par \par \uc2 KUDLOW: I'm here from the government. I'm here to help you. That's right. I also wanted someone to say that we need to get 4 or 5 percent economic growth, not 1 percent. So we should be slashing taxes across the board. We should be lowering marginal tax rate, the way John F. Kennedy did, the way \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  did, the way \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did.\par \par \uc2 I want to just someone to say that tough stuff to get the economy moving. There are a lot of good points on the economy. They acted more like Republicans this week than they did the last debate. Did they make the sale on the economy? I'm not entirely sure that they punched away out off to some extent. I still don't think Bidenomics was buried today on that stage. I just don't think so. I don't think there were direct hits and I was disappointed.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Would you both agree with me. I felt there were a couple of people and I'm not going to sit here and be insulting and name names. It just really didn't have any business being on that stage. We all know they don't have a chance. And for them, this is their moment. And maybe the criteria needs to be a little tighter going into any future debate.\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: Well, there's going to come a time Sean and Larry, where you have to justify being on the debate stage of you're still mired in single digits if you truly want to get rid of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . People talk about unity. They say the Democrats have unity. No. The Democrats have unanimity, every single Democrat was exactly the same way inflation reduction and not for the tax cut and jobs act, against Amy Coney Barrett. They all voted for \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , 15 ballots, all 213 of them.\par \par \uc2 The point is, we can have unity, to try to get together to defeat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . It's early in the process. But as time goes on, and you just make in the debate stage, and yet you're mired in single digits in the early states, and nationwide, you have to ask yourself, how much can I sacrifice on behalf of the team to get rid of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 We'll see what \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  has to say he'll probably bring a message tonight that's a little bit better than MAGA, MEGA, MAGA Republicans, deplorable irredeemable. But I think if you're a Democrat, you have to be very worried that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are not even being asked what they have to say about this field. People are going to be --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Right. Let me ask you this --\par \par \uc2 KUDLOW: Can I Sean, can I just a make a point.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: This is an exit question and then we have the governor coming on in a minute. Here's my exit question. Did anyone distinguish themselves as a clear person, you know, with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's having such a dominant lead in the polls as the one person that could give him any run for his money?\par \par \uc2 KUDLOW: I don't think there was a breakout-breakout if that's what you're asking. No, I don't think so.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, Kellyanne?\par \par \uc2 KELLYANNE: No. Not enough to overcome him in the polls enough to survive. So I think their best argument is a war of attrition slow and steady, wins the race. But no, nobody there made the case as to what they would do differently or better than he did. They want to build a wall. They want to secure the border. They sounded a lot like him.\par \par \uc2 And look, I give them credit for taking on the big issues. But I don't think that there was enough clarity. And Sean, I said to Larry, early in the day, I want to come out tonight feeling away that I didn't feel it for the first debate, which is each person has a two or three 