you and Laura -- how come Laura doesn't, you know, poke at you every night?\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: I know my football, I left it. I left it in the other room. Darn it. I was going to throw it at the screen, but they're mad at me here if I break another camera. Sean number one, I miss you. But you look great. You're doing a fantastic job. But let me tell you dovetailing into your previous conversation with Kellyanne and Larry. I think after watching this tonight, the debate I want to see before your debate that you're going to host between, of course DeSantis and Newsom is DeSantis and Nikki Haley, because for me, at least tonight, those two emerged as the strongest advocates for their brand of conservatism.\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley is a lot closer to the GOP establishment, the donor base on issues of regarding Ukraine, and you know, the immigration system is broken, all that kind of lingo. And then you have DeSantis, who's much more on the populist strain of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and probably the person if Trump ends up being the nominee, the likely person to pick up the torch after Trump. So a debate between those two maybe without a moderator and listened to I think would be fascinating for the American people because all those big issues would actually be --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You say you want to have Gov. DeSantis debate Nikki Haley on your show, I got it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I am a little bit. No. But you see what I'm saying?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm just kidding.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But you what I'm saying about this.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes. I do. No, I understand.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That's it. That's the struggle inside the party. The populace part of the party is much bigger. It's at 84 percent of the party versus what, 26 percent of the party, or 16 percent of the party, depending on what polls you look at. So I think that would be interesting. But I agree. I don't think anyone had like a Socko moment. I know the Vivek is coming up. He's a very smart guy.\par \par \uc2 But he seemed to be on the defensive a lot. They were all coming at him tonight. And Burgum, you know, he seems very smart. But he has to he has to move on down the road. \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  and Pence seem like they're mostly motivated by their anger toward Trump and running. And so I think both of them, you know, God bless them, I like both of them. But that's not going anywhere. So Haley and DeSantis to me are the --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's not a platform I think people want to hear.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No, I think this DeSantis and Nikki Haley, that's the debate. We want to see if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's not going to be at the stage at least.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, I'm going to ask the governor right now, considering you push that. Anyway, Laura, we do miss you. But we're happy. You're doing great at 7:00. Thanks so much for staying up and being with us. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 All right on the set now, after another strong debate performance, Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . How are you Governor? Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 GOV. RON DESANTIS (R), PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: I'll tell you what, I've been in California. We're getting Sunday night and we were in Coronado.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It happens in the room.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: One time, I'm going to say yes, people are buzzing about this debate with you're going to do so I think it's going to be incredible, we're do. But tonight, look, there was a lot of bickering on the stage. And you know, my thing is, is like, look, we owe it to the American people to give our vision about how we're going to reverse this country's decline. And I think I was able to do that I think some of the crosstalk, if I was at home watching that, I would turn the channel when I saw that. So we were able to, I think, rise above that and deliver our message.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Listen, in my view, there were a couple of people on that stage, in my view that probably shouldn't have been there. I mean, and I think at that point, it lends itself mortal conversation. It is interesting. I think this debate is with you, and the governor is going to be very interesting. So I'm looking forward to moderating that. And I think with 90 minutes that just plenty of breathing room. So that will lend itself to more conversation.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: And you know what, maybe we can say, since the former president didn't come here, maybe he'd be willing to do one with you and I. I think he owes it to our voters to come and make the case. I mean --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm now challenging, so this is going to be Hannity one on one debate.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Let's do it. Let's do it, right?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'll do anything. I'll ask him.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: But here's the thing, though. You owe it to the voters to come and make the case. No one's entitled anything. You know, you can say, oh, there's some poll months before, no, you got to make the case. You got to owe to the voters. So I'm going to show up everywhere. I think that that's what we were able to do. And, you know, there were some, I think, some important issues that were discussed tonight. There's also others that I know you and I've talked about that weren't discussed.\par \par \uc2 But at the end of the day, I think the thing that was clear for this, there's a lot of talk, a lot of people had good things to say, I'm the guy that's done it. In Florida we did everything I promised, we delivered. And we're sick of the talk with Republicans, they always promise all this, like what are the two biggest issues arguably right now?\par \par \uc2 The debt and the border. You and I have been talking about this for as long as we've known each other. Isn't it time we get a leader to come in and bring this stuff into a conclusion and a landing. And I think if we're able to, you know, to do that with the nomination and win the election, we're going to be able to get all this stuff done.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Nobody brought up to the point regarding the border. And I thought you had a very strong position of what you would do to close the border. And, you know, no nonsense, get this thing closed. It's now become to me more than anything else, the national security issue.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We are catching people that are on the terror watch list. But we're not vetting anybody. We have no idea what their backlogs.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: People are coming from China, Russia, Iran, all of our enemy countries, they're coming across the border. I hope I'm wrong. But if I had to bet my life savings, I would bet that there will be a terrorist attack that happens in the future of this country that's going to be --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I guarantee it. I mean I wish we were wrong.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: And here's the thing, these guys in D.C., they don't care. There's no urgency. I mean, some of our guys in the House care. But like, the elites in D.C., they don't care. Biden doesn't care. He's missing an action on this as the carnage mounts. And I agree. I mean, I think that this is above all a national security issue.\par \par \uc2 Now there's also nuts and bolts issues. I mean, the amount of illegals that are pouring in, medical care is being taxed, schools, it's overwhelming communities far away from the border. You see it in New York City.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know what so fascinating, in New York City so they're paying on average $40,000 per illegal immigrant. OK. They expect --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: And they're kicking out the veterans to make room for illegals.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: The veterans never had the four-star hotels. They're building all these facilities. They expect to spend $12 billion in the next 18 months. And, you know, they're claiming this came from Governor Abbott. No.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: No.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: -- I think I've been very good, exactly.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's 13 percent.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: But here's the problem with this government we have and I think why people are rightfully so frustrated. They can't tell us how many illegals are coming across the border. They can't tell us how many tanks we left in Afghanistan. They can't tell you all the money in Ukrainian went. They can't even tell you how cocaine got in the White House. And yet, they want to go after if you do $601 transaction --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Wait a minute. Let's be fair to the investigators. They spent 10 long days investigating where that cocaine came from, and came to the conclusion they'll never get a conclusion. How is that but in the Menendez case, they actually found the fingerprints of the people that handed the envelopes so they claim to Senator Menendez pretty interesting comparison.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Why I can't believe, you know, he had all the gold bars there. I guess that's a real testament to Bidenflation.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Listen, I love that he Googled.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: You know, you're bribing people you need to --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How much is a kilo of gold worth, right, you can't make this up. Generally speaking, you know, I guess the theme of the night as I watched and listened to you tonight was, OK, these are the tough stances I took in Florida. These are the -- that's my proven track record. And that's what I want to bring to the White House. That's your --\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: I think it's leadership. And I think it's deliverables because we can have great sloganeering, we can have great debates. But if we're not ultimately going to get this done, then none of it matters. And one of the things I've been thinking about lately, because preparing here, I looked at Reagan's farewell address. So in 2033 in January, what would I say to the American people after serving two terms, and that's really the vision of, you're going to be able to get ahead again, in this country.\par \par \uc2 We're an economy that works for people. We're going to have our sovereignty restored and borders enforced. We're going to make sure that we have education, not indoctrination, we will be the world's leading superpower, we will fend off the threat from China successfully. We're not going to have crime overrunning every city in America anymore. And we're going to restore the constitution so that we have a limited government that works beside us and on our behalf, not a weaponized government that comes after us.\par \par \uc2 If we can do that, then we will have restored the shining city on the hill that Reagan talks about, and we'll be able to turn over America to our kids and grandkids better than we found it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Governor, thanks for coming by. Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Thank you. Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Thank you. Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, another candidate with a strong performance tonight, GOP outsider, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 . Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: One is we do have to seal that southern border. Building the wall is not enough. They're building cartel financed tunnels underneath that wall. Semi trucks can drive through them. We have to use our own military to seal the Swiss cheese at the southern border. But we also have to be honest, there's a demand side problem in this country too, a mental health epidemic.\par \par \uc2 I met family in Iowa, two parents Kathy and Derek. They lost their son Sebastian, 17 years old. He bought Percocet on \uc2 Snapchat\uc2 , and then he died. Why did he die? Because it was laced with fentanyl. That is closer to bioterrorism not a drug overdose. That is poisoning. So it is our job to make sure that never happens. But it's also our job to make sure that 17 year olds don't turn to Percocet via \uc2 Snapchat\uc2 . We have to bring back mental health care in this country.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Joining us now \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 . Sir, how are you?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Good to see you, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You just told me your favorite part of the debate was after the debate when your son came on stage.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: It was the last five minutes of it. When he came on, I saw him sitting quietly in the front row. He's three years old. And that's about as a well behaved as I've seen him in a long time I'm proud of him.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: He's at the Reagan Library wouldn't expect the less. One of the more contentious moments was you and Nikki Haley. Nikki saying every time I hear you, I feel dumber. We can't trust you Vivek, so you came under some fire tonight. What's you're reaction to that. Why?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: So and the feeling dumber, that's actually the first time I've actually ever heard that. So I'll take that as a first. But Sean, my view tonight was there were a lot of personal insults coming my way. That's OK. These are still good people. I respect the policy disagreements that we had. But I'm not running against any of them. I'm running for this country.\par \par \uc2 And I think part of what you saw is I am the new guy. And I do have to earn the trust of the voters at home. And I understand that and I respect that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- because stuck out, that moment struck me.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You were sending a message maybe I come off as a little, I don't know.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: No, at all, you know.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, at all. OK.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: You know, I understand that --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, I'm a talk show host, every talk shows you'll ever meet comes off as a, no, at all. So I can identify --\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: But the thing, Sean, is --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Why do you want to it? What is it that you 