op -- our law and order saved them, security, our school systems. It's all fixable. What?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Yes. The flipside of that is it's good news is it's fixable. Drill, frac, burn coal and brace nuclear, stop paying people more money to stay at home than to go to work. Abandon the climate cult that shackles the United States, while leaving China untouched. Declare economic independence from our enemy, Communist China, who we cannot depend for the shoes on our feet, to the phones in our pockets --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And the drugs and the medicines we take.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: To the pharmaceutical supply chain, which I of course understand and know, well, the same country that's poisoning the illegal supply chain.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Trump put a tariff on them, Trump made them pay.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Why do we got to go further than that? I think the answer is --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What's further?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Well, I think what is further is total decoupling. We to --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you this.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: -- land in this country, we will not turn companies into lobbying pawns. We're going to hold them accountable for unleashing hell on the world for the COVID-19 pandemic. We can't forget about that one, Sean, is that that was catastrophe inflicted on us. And if we don't hold them accountable for that we can expect worse in the future. That one says in the Reagan Library tonight --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Reagan said this about the Soviet Union.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How cool is that with his jet hanging on -- it's over your head.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: It was awesome. Yes. My young son --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm bet you're hoping that those doesn't fall?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: No. Look, it was it was a beautiful sight.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It is a nice sight.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: It was inspiring to me. What did he say? His foreign policy strategy against the Soviet Union was we win, they lose. Well --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Here's my next question.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: -- is the threat. I say to Communist China, we win, they lose. That's how I'm going to lead.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK. There was a guy that wasn't on that stage today.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And he's got a massive lead against all of you on that stage.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK. That's obstacle number one.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Well, look, I the way I look at it is I was a little different than everybody else on the stage. The reason \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's in the lead, let's be honest, is that he was an excellent president. But I'm in America first conservative, not a Trump first conservative. And I think we have to reunite this country and reach the next generation to take our America first agenda to the next level. So I will honor \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his legacy more than anybody else.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Do you think, do you find these -- do you believe that these indictments are, first of all, they all should -- they're all politically motivated.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: I think they're sham.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I think they are too.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: And I will pardon him on day one. I said that at the last debate. I stand by it. And one of the things I noticed tonight, is that I think they're --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: If he asked you to be vice president, what would you say?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: I would ask him to be my most important mentor and advisor in the first year when I'm in office.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Because that's what allows --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: If you don't make it for some reason?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: So Sean --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You don't want to answer that question?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: No, this isn't about me. And it's not about Trump.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm just asking.\pa