ons after that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Mr. Vice President, good to see you. Thank you, sir.\par \par \uc2 PENCE: Thank you Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 PENCE: Good to be with you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, coming up, Senator Tim Scott and is the governor of the great state of California \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  on set right here with us as we continue.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, welcome back to Hannity. We are live. We're in beautiful Simi Valley, California at the Reagan Library. Joining us now South Carolina Senator Tim Scott. Senator, how are you? Good to see you. Thank you for joining us. You had a lot of interesting moments that I thought really interesting. I actually wrote them down. I love when you called up Vivek and saying, excuse me, you said were bought and paid for.\par \par \uc2 SEN. TIM SCOTT (R), PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You said at another point what I thought was a from the heart passionate monologue almost, you know, America is not a racist nation. And you talked about your background. And then the other thing, and it's maybe not as popular with conservatives right now, you made a strong powerful defense about the need to degrade Russia's military. Take any one of those three.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yes. So, think about the fact that we live in the greatest country on Earth. But we don't celebrate it. We have people who say that America is in decline, actually, we are in the middle of a \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  retreat. We've seen this movie before.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, isn't it \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  decline isn't a way of parsing words?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Maybe. I don't think so. The difference between the decline, I have lived in devastated neighborhoods that felt like a decline. The 20 percent of Americans who are living in the most devastated areas of our country need to understand that this is just a retreat. You can turn it around with the next leader of this country. By doing so you restore hope and you create opportunities. And frankly, you stop the devastation in these big liberal cities that are marching towards socialism in the same fashion as a great society.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Do you think that it's so divided, is that why we have Governor Newsom on a lot of people live in California? Do you see the gas prices here?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Oh, $6.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, 7.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Absolutely terrible.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And crazy. OK. And so you have a migration out of New York, California, New Jersey, Illinois, they go into your state, they're going to North Carolina, they're going to Tennessee, they're going to Texas and Florida.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yes. Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And how -- why are they doing that?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Because the red states have proven that America is still the land of opportunity. We prove that free markets and capitalism works effectively. But we need in these big blue cities, think about Chicago as a classic example, $30,000 per student for education. And yet, the vast majority of minority kids are below grade level. In Detroit --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Do you see the 13 high schools in Baltimore?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Zero.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Zero.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Zero.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Zero proficiency.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: You talk about the greatest, absolute disgusting form of discrimination, it's brought to us by the teachers unions who are standing in the door house of schools today, saying the poor kids, you're trapped in, you're never getting out. And what does that lead to? Leads to hopelessness, it leads to high unemployment, and that leads to crime. We've lost control of the cities because the Liberals with their super majority have done nothing.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You said and you talked about your background. You did a good job in your book about this but you talked about America not being a 