u're here. Grab a seat. Get comfortable. I feel like Arsenio Hall.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for being here.\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE MEMBERS: USA! USA! USA!\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. I got to get the show started. Thank you all for coming.\par \par \uc2 We do have a good show tonight, great lineup. \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  on set with us right here in studio. Senator Tim Scott right here in studio. And in just moments, we're going to hear from House Judiciary Committee Chairman Jim Jordan. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 Now, today, Jordan and other Republicans confronted big time the Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  who frankly needs to be impeached, during what was an explosive hearing on Capitol Hill. More than half of the country no longer trust Garland and for good reason. Biden's so-called justice system has become weaponized and politicized like the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , beyond belief, unequal prosecution, unequal sentencing, unequal application of our laws. We don't have equal justice under the law.\par \par \uc2 And a sitting president who, of course, has been shielded, protected from any and all legal scrutiny -- well, his chief political rival, \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 , has been targeted with dozens of stack charges in one of the most aggressive prosecutions in American history. This has never happened to a former president one time. It's happened four times, perfectly timed interestingly enough, even though these issues go back years for the 2024 election season.\par \par \uc2 But this is all news to \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 . The attorney general believes he's done a heroic job. He thinks he's great, leading a fair, righteous Department of Justice.\par \par \uc2 But for some reason, well, Garland just wasn't willing to able or able to answer questions in any direct or forthcoming manner as I kind of predicted. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Have you had personal contact with anyone at \uc2 FBI\uc2  headquarters about the Hunter Biden investigation?\par \par \uc2 MERRICK GARLAND\uc2 , ATTORNEY GENERAL: I don't know -- I don't recollect the answer to that question but the \uc2 FBI\uc2  works for the Justice Department. It's --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I'm sorry, I'm sorry. You don't recollect, you don't recollect whether you've talked with anybody at \uc2 FBI\uc2  headquarters about an investigation of the president's son?\par \par \uc2 GARLAND: I don't believe that I did.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I don't believe, I don't remember, I don't recall. Willful ignorance was the theme of the day for \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 . Question after question after question, no clarity whatsoever. Garland didn't seem to know much about anything to be honest, like -- likely by design I would think.\par \par \uc2 Garland, he's not a fool. On day one, he knew that the old Biden family business was a huge problem. But luckily for Garland and, of course, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the solution was already in progress, thanks to federal prosecutor David Weiss. Weiss's seemingly never-ending investigation now over five years long into \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  allowed Garland to distance himself and ignore all the questions about the allegations against Joe and Hunter.\par \par \uc2 When he became special counsel, I told you this would happen. At the same time, Garland put a big show about his integrity, his independence, bragging that he and Weiss had the undisputed power to bring charges anywhere, any jurisdiction, knowing full well that Weiss was not using that authority at all and told the \uc2 IRS\uc2  whistleblowers they didn't have the authority, and contradicted himself to both Jim Jordan and \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After getting turned away by Biden appointed prosecutors in another district, well, Weiss was reportedly just simply content, plan A was to charge Hunter with nothing. And you know, close the investigation, it was over.\par \par \uc2 Now, all of a sudden, we had those \uc2 IRS\uc2  whistleblowers show up and sound the alarm. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. JIM JORDAN (R-OH): You said he had complete authority but he'd already been turned down. He wanted to bring an action in the District of Columbia and the U.S. attorney there said, no, you can't. And then you go tell the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  under oath that he has complete authority.\par \par \uc2 GARLAND: I'm going to say again that no one had the authority to turn him down. They could refuse to partner with him. They could not --\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: You can use whatever your language, refused to partner is turning down.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. From the looks of all this, either Garland was lying under oath or Weiss did all the dirty work, while the attorney general was pretending to bury his head in the sand. Now, of course, the Weiss case is now a disaster in every single way, multiple serious allegations of misconduct from government whistleblowers, and an \uc2 FBI\uc2  whistleblower, followed by a highly unusual sweetheart deal that was rejected by the judge. Remember, that was plan B because they didn't plan on originally charging \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Okay, whistleblowers show up. Let's act like we'll give him a slap on the wrist. We'll insert in the plea agreement in the gun charge provision, the diversion program, oh, full immunity for Hunter. No jail time, and after five years of investigating Weiss, he allowed the statute of limitations to run out of some of the most serious tax charges, that -- during the \uc2 Burisma\uc2  years. What a coincidence.\par \par \uc2 Well, despite all of this, you know who Garland appointed as special counsel to clean up David Weiss's mess. He appointed David Weiss, of course.\par \par \uc2 It's almost as if the goal is to protect the big guy \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  instead of actually prosecuting serious crimes. Look at this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Mr. Garland, did you consider -- I just want to go back to this question. Did you consider anyone else when David Weiss requested special counsel designation on August 8th?\par \par \uc2 GARLAND: No, Mr. Weiss asked to be made special counsel and I made -- I did not consider an alternative. I'm going to --\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: To be clear, he was the only one under consideration. It was either no special counsel or if there was a special counsel, it was going to be the guy who presided over the investigation for the previous five years. They made an intentional decision to say we're going to let the statute of limitations lapse, and I want to know who decided that and why they did it.\par \par \uc2 GARLAND: Mr. Weiss was a supervisor of the investigation at that time and at all times. He made the appropriate decisions and you'll be able to ask him that question and he will --\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: You know why they did it. Everyone knows why they did it. May not say it, but everyone knows why they did it. They did it -- those tax years that's that -- that dealt with the pre -- that involved the president. It's one thing to have a gun charge in Delaware, that doesn't involve the president of United States. But \uc2 Burisma\uc2 , oh my, that goes right to the White House. We can't have that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Why would Garland ever consider anyone else? Weiss already debased himself in court, sacrificed -- you're right -- sacrificed his reputation to protect \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Right on cue, though, a couple of gun charges, plan C now against Hunter showed up, not against Joe, the low-hanging fruit. Now that the plea deal, of course, imploded, thanks to that Delaware judge, that actually read the plea agreement, asked the prosecution, have you ever seen a deal like this before? And they gave the answer, no, they never saw one. Then why are you offering it to them?\par \par \uc2 And a federal judge demanded action. By the way, no FARA violations, the tax charges, statute of limitations go away, nothing that would implicate Hunter's father, the big guy Joe, who Hunter gave half his income to pops and paid all of pops' home repairs and we have the emails proving that.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, who has lied -- \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has lied and changed the story repeatedly and was up to his eyeballs engaging with Hunter's business partners both here at home and abroad. The DOJ, they'll go to great lengths to serve \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and other Democrats for that matter. If you are part of the BLM riots, tried to burn down a federal courthouse in 2020, 574 riots, if you doxed a conservative Supreme Court justice's home, you surrounded them with angry mobs, Biden's DOJ was more than happy to let you off the hook.\par \par \uc2 But if you were accused of obstructing a sidewalk outside of an abortion clinic, legally, get ready for a SWAT team to come knock on your door, guns drawn, full tactical gear, followed by several serious felonies, a lengthy prison sentence.\par \par \uc2 You all know it's true. We don't have equal justice. Biden's weaponized DOJ has no -- so much contempt for, you know, what, half the country. That they're criminalizing conservatives while protection -- protecting the likes of the Clintons, the Bidens, and anyone that's a Democrat.\par \par \uc2 Today, Garland couldn't even give a direct answer to this simple question about traditional Catholics or allegedly targeted spied on by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the DOJ because of their deep, abiding faith, religious views. Look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. JEFF VAN DREW (R-NJ): Attorney General, through the chair, I ask you, do you agree that traditional Catholics are violent extremists?\par \par \uc2 GARLAND: I have no idea what your -- what the traditional means here.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 VAN DREW