id Weiss tells Senator Graham I have not sought special counsel authority. Then on August 11th, the attorney general -- general announces that David Weiss will be a special counsel. What happened in those 32 days? What took place?\par \par \uc2 The whistleblowers came forward with their testimony and the plea deal that they were trying to sweep everything under the rug, the plea deal is declined by a judge who did her job. And that's why we got a special counsel. They were going to get away with all this, but for those two brave whistleblowers and that judge in Delaware who did her job.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you, you had a line of questioning with the attorney general about the statute of limitations and why the statute of limitations lapped (ph), and why it was important in the years 2014 and `15. These were the \uc2 Burisma\uc2  tax years.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Exactly, exactly.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And then you gave four facts that I think are critical, regarding this.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Can you break that down for this audience?\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Well, the facts are real simple. Fact number one, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  gets put on the board of \uc2 Burisma\uc2 . He gets paid millions of dollars for those taxes 2014, 2015.\par \par \uc2 Fact number two, he wasn't qualified to be on the board. In fact, he said it, not me. He said he got the position largely because of his last name. Devon Archer in his deposition said the brand was \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the Biden name.\par \par \uc2 Fact number three, the \uc2 Burisma\uc2  executives asked \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , can you help us. We're under pressure from the prosecutor. Can you help us? There's a call made to D.C.\par \par \uc2 Fact number four, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  goes to Ukraine, starts the process and actually successful in leveraging our tax dollars to fire the very prosecutor who was putting the pressure on \uc2 Burisma\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Those facts are not in dispute. They are as solid as can be. And here's what's interesting, that fourth fact is exactly what the confidential human source told the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  recorded in the 1023 form, the same 1023 form \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  didn't want to let Congress see. Those said that it's all spelled out in there.\par \par \uc2 So you got corroborating evidence. That's the pattern and then they let the statute of limitations lapse, expire. There's probably no one any person in your audience, that raucous studio audience you have right now, if they owe hundreds of thousands of dollars -- if they owe hundreds of thousands of dollars, I bet the DOJ doesn't let the statute of limitations lapse for them.\par \par \uc2 But they did for the president's son because \uc2 Burisma\uc2  goes to the White House. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is involved. Not on the gun charge, they can do that. That doesn't involve \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . But on \uc2 Burisma\uc2 , it goes to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask the fundamental question here. As Garland was pleading ignorance all day long, does the attorney general not have to sign up? We had -- the first plan was no charges. The second plan was okay, we'll do the slap on the wrist deal. We'll put in the plea agreement, an immunity deal, and in the gun diversion portion of this.\par \par \uc2 Thankfully, that judge caught that.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Then plan C was, oh, I guess, we're going to have to indict him on the gun charge but at least that still protects Joe. If Hunter has to be sacrificed, he gets sacrificed, because he was pleading, oh, no, no, independence for Weiss.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: When the attorney general have to sign off on whatever decisions are made here?\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Well, you would think particularly when supposedly David Weiss goes and this is testimony we've got. David Weiss goes to the U.S. attorney in the District of Columbia and he declines to allow me to prosecute there. You would think the attorney general would weigh in then.\par \par \uc2 But it looks like he didn't. Now, he's weighing in with the special counsel. The other thing I think is happening here in this third plan, I think the special counsel allows them to extend this out even further, so we'll see what that all means.\par \par \uc2 David Weiss is scheduled to be in front of our committee on October 11th. They committed to have him come in front of our committee. I hope they will honor their commitment.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Chairman Jordan, great job today. Thank you for being with us. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 All right. Ahead, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's arraignment for gun crimes, the president's son requested more special treatment from the legal system, asking to appear in court remotely through a webcam. The federal judge deny that request, thankfully, and Hunter will now appear in person like everyone else.\par \par \uc2 Here now with reaction, FOX News contributors Kellyanne Conway, \uc2 Ari Fleischer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Okay, I'm glad about that part, that Hunter has to do that.\par \par \uc2 Kellyanne, let me start with you and I'd really like to know, you know, when you look at this in total and you look at the aggressive prosecution of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ho you work for, for all those years and you look at the absolute, the opposite treatment, no prosecutor would prosecute, subpoenaed emails, deleted 33,000, no problem, a dirty dossier, four locations, top secret classified information for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , no raids, no charges, nothing.\par \par \uc2 What is it -- what is -- what should the average American, especially a conservative think about law and order and justice in this country?\par \par \uc2 KELLYANNE CONWAY, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: That there is special treatment. I thought the Delaware Judge Christopher Burke did today, Sean, was masterful. Finally, for the first time in years, if