pposed to speak again, but my dad used to have an expression when I was growing up. My father had an expression. My father was -- did not have a college degree, but he was a well-read man. He worked very hard his whole life.\par \par \uc2 He said, Joe, a job is about a lot more than a paycheck. It's about your dignity. It's about self-respect.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Does that include Hunter's job? I'm just asking.\par \par \uc2 And despite Biden's constant struggles and his mumbling and bumbling and very low poll numbers, his team is now telling worried Democrats to relax because apparently, they believe that by focusing on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and abortion they're going to be able to win easily next year. Excuse me.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, joining us now live in studio, 2024 presidential candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 VIVEK RAMASWAMY\uc2  (R), PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Good to see you, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How are you? Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I've noticed as time has gotten on, you've come under more fire. What do you think that is?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Well, look, I think that it's politics. Yeah, at the start of this race, I was at 0.0 percent in the polls, nobody cared about me in the race. Now, we're verging on second and third in most national polls, and you're going to run for U.S. president, if you can't handle the heat, you stay out of the kitchen.\par \par \uc2 So I can handle the heat and it -- my view, Sean, is we talked to all media, left-wing media, right-wing media, no wing media. If I'm not willing to sit across the table from the people who disagree with me, then I'm not willing to sit ready to sit across the table with Xi Jinping.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Why did you want to sit next to the jackasses of fake news CNN or MSDNC? Don't you feel like you're wasting your time? By the way, not many people are watching fake news CNN.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: You know, the fact of the matter is there are times when I feel that way, but I'm not running to lead a political party, Sean. I'm really running to lead a nation.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- you want to be watched.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Well, you know what? I think that my view is we have to talk to the people who disagree with us because every time we do it, we show up and we win. You'll remember with Don Lemon that last interview that he did with me was one of his last ones before he got kicked off the air. So we're doing services through this campaign.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So, you got Don Lemon fired?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: That's what "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " said. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, I don't think it's very complicated to be a conservative. I think we believe in limited government, lower taxes, more for individual freedom.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Amen.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, look at the things we want. We want secure borders. We want law and order, safety and security.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We want energy independence. We want constitutionalists on the bench. We believe in peace through strength, and then leave us the hell alone.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: That's about right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's not that hard.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: And you know what, Sean? Here's the real thing in the country? That's not even a Republican versus Democrat idea. Those are basic American ideals.\par \par \uc2 I think 80 percent of this country agrees on the ideals that you just listed. The American dream, the idea that you get ahead in this country not on the color of your skin but on the content of your character -- I think 80 percent of people in this country agree on that and half the 20 are people younger than me who never learned those ideals in the first place.\par \par \uc2 We're going to bring them along, too. And if we do, Sean, I think we can win the 2024 election in a landslide, with a multi-ethnic working-class coalition, leave no state left behind, no city left behind. I think that's the opportunity with this failing president from the economy to the poorest border.\par \par \uc2 This is our opportunity. If we have the courage to actually stand up for our own vision, that's how we win.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You're saying something deep and profound. The Republican Party has to be the party of working men and women.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I believe that.\par \par \uc2 It also has to be the party that brings minorities on board --\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- that have been lied to and frankly disappointed regularly by the Democratic Party. They have been failed. The schools are failing.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: No doubt about it. I'll tell you an inspiring story.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They're not keeping them safe and secure.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Sean, so I've gone to places like the South Side of Chicago or Kensington in the inner city of Philadelphia --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Amazing you didn't get shot.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: -- in this campaign. Well, I mean, I've been to third world countries growing up. You go to the third world, you want to where you go, go to Kensington in Philadelphia today.\par \par \uc2 But here's what I saw on the South Side of Chicago, 90 percent Black room, supposedly mostly Democrat. That is a room that fully agreed with me on militarizing the southern border, on ending that border crisis that is impacting their community every bit as much as Republican communities across this country.\par \par \uc2 And so, America first includes all Americans. That's what I say.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I agree. Americans should not be suffering in Biden's economy. His idiotic energy plans, we shouldn't have open borders. You know, we need law and order.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: That's right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: These are the basics -- these are all those all preventable problems that he caused.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: That's right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Why do you think he chose that path?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Well, look, I want to say something about Biden and why I don't talk about him that much on the campaign trail. I don't even think he's really the one running the country, Sean. I think he is a puppet for the managerial class in the administrative state.\par \par \uc2 And you mark my words, when I'm the nominee, they're not going to let him run against me. It's going to be the next puppet that they trot out. So we have to recognize that this is a broken system. We have to stand up to that managerial class, shut down those three letter agencies. It's not Biden that's alone the problem. It's the three-letter agencies in the deep state. We have to get in there to shut it down,\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: There are good people in those agencies, but the upper echelon tend to control everything.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: The managerial class. And so, yes, there's 25 percent of people in those agencies who are doing important work, but I think that we have to downsize the government significantly, 75 percent head count reduction. That's what I'm bringing to Washington, D.C.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Here we go. \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 When we come back, \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  forces special new accommodation from the Senate so he can you know feel right at home on the Senate floor and putting in shorts. Well, Fetterman's colleague, South Carolina senator, 2024 presidential candidate, Tim Scott, is next, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Anyway, so we have this issue with the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and it is getting pretty interesting. And one Democrat -- one Republican nominee for president has decided to take it on and that would be Senator Tim Scott from the great state of South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Let's give a warm "Hannity" audience welcome Senator Scott.\par \par \uc2 How are you?\par \par \uc2 SEN. TIM SCOTT (R-SC), PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: How are you?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Great to see you.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: You, too, thanks.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You're doing okay?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 , all right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, we love having you. Great to see you again.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Thank you. You as well, absolutely.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We had a great time in South Carolina with you.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Thank you for coming down. We always love to see you in South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I love South Carolina better than here.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: You bring them -- we all love South Carolina better than New York. Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: It's good to be home.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I don't think I often disagree with you. We've been friends a long time.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: That's true.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And I heard your comments about Reagan and the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and you strike, you get fired.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Here's where I might differ from you --\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Okay.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- a little bit and tell me where I might be wrong.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm looking at the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , and they -- by the way, their four-day workweek, 32 hours, take that proposal, no way, that's -- okay, I work like 90 hours a week. Sorry, I don't -- nobody gets a 40 workweek.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yes, yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay, I don't know anybody that doesn't work, you know, 16 hours, 14 hours a day.\par \par \uc2 But here's the thing, they're getting -- they are totally losing their jobs because of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  --\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- and this push towards electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: EV, absolutely.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Four point five billion dollar profit loss on the EV line of Ford this year -\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That they are killing these workers. That should be -- what recourse do they have?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Without any question? Anytime you have a president who drives us to inflationary levels of 16 percent, this is like the sequel to the \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2  years. It is devastating and it's devastating working class Americans. They've lost thousands of dollars of spending power and without any question, whether you're a non-union or a union worker, you're being devastated by the Bidenomics, devastated.\par \par \uc2 One of the things I focused on, Sean, that's really important is the fact that, in the first -- y'all remember -- remember that $1.9 trillion COVID package deal passed in 2021? There was $86 billion to bail out the unions. That's terrible.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's nuts.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: They keep offering deals.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Because the unions are forcing the Democrats, you know, they use - -\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: They own `em.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They own `em.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: They own `em. And when that happens, the taxpayers -- there's no such thing as a federal dollar. They're your dollars.\par \par \uc2 They're all your dollars, putting $86 billion of your money into shoring up union pensions because they keep over-promising and under-delivering, it's just wrong. We need a president who says, we are not going to subsidize unions, period.\par \par \uc2 You make the deal. You live by the deal. If it goes belly up, it's not on the back of the taxpayers.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How do you like this idea? I mean, usually, CEOs and there's been a lot of talk about disparity CEO pay, okay. But most of their pay, most time, not all times, is based on performance.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What if they had the same type of performance where everybody has skin in the game.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Everybody, the company does well, these guys get massive pay increases, bonuses, as well as the CEOs. Would that -- that would keep it - - that would have everyone pulling in the same direction.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: It would make the world a better place.\par \par \uc2 Here's one of the things that happens, there's a company called \uc2 Nucor Steel\uc2  in South Carolina, where many of the workers there make six-figure incomes because they get production bonuses. We should encourage and incent compensation to match the production of a company. When you make the company more money, you should share in the profits of that company. That's all common sense in America.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Let me move to the controversial issue of abortion and lately, you have distinguished yourself with some of your fellow candidates and I read it with great interest because I think that the issue politically of abortion, not the moral side of this --\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- although -- I can -- they're probably intertwined. But the political side of it is I think probably the country politically is at the Dobb's decision, 15 weeks, 12 weeks.\par \par \uc2 And you said, there should be a ban after 15 weeks at the states that have -- will now make the decision shouldn't be able to go longer than that.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Absolutely. Well, number one, if you think about the fact that at weeks that baby can suck his or her thumb, feel pain. Three out of four Americans say 15 weeks is the exact right place to be as it relates to stopping radical states like New York, California, and Illinois on having abortion on demand up until the day of birth. That's just wrong.\par \par \uc2 So -- exactly. We as a nation we're better than that we have to learn to stand up for our rights and make sure every single child in every single state has the same right. And that means 15 weeks to be a national limit, and I want my entire presidential -- all the presidential candidates whether it's Ron, Nikki, the former president, they should all join me in support of 15-week limits.\par \par \uc2 We can't trust California with anything. Think about this -- think about this, Sean -- in California, today, they will take away a parent's rights to their kids if they don't agree with the gender decisions. That's wrong. We should stand up against that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Senator Tim Scott, great to see, my friend. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: God bless, brother.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, coming up, this might be \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's dumbest idea ever, the American Climate Corps. Brian Brenberg will join us next, and talk about it.\par \par \uc2 And we'll see you soon. Thanks, Senator.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Forget Bidenomics. Biden inflation now continues its rein of terror over the economy that's killing every American. A new poll shows 92 percent of the American people have had to cut down on spending, especially on things like new clothes, eating out, because they could barely afford the essentials.\par \par \uc2 Sixty-one percent living paycheck to paycheck. Meanwhile, Biden's border crisis is now stretching the budgets of local governments around the nation right here in New York, $40,000 this year for every illegal immigrant. They are a sanctuary city.\par \par \uc2 All right. All the way out to Denver which just announced it spent $25 million on housing illegal immigrants. Are they housing our veterans that are homeless?\par \par \uc2 And what is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  doing about these issues?\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE MEMBERS: Nothing.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 He has launched something called the American Climate Corps. Young kids going to be paid -- young adults, $15 an hour, put to work implementing energy-efficient technologies and advancing environmental justice. Gee, that's great news.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, here with reaction, he is the host of "The Big Money" show, co- host, Brian Brenberg, who, by the way, is going to be co-hosting an education --\par \par \uc2 BRIAN BRENBERG, FBN HOST: Don't miss this.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- with Vivek, who was with us, and former Education Secretary \uc2 Betsy DeVos\uc2 . That's at 1:00 p.m. tomorrow, FOX Business, don't miss it. Tickets are free, by the way, go to -- what is it?\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: Eventbright.com. Look for "Big Money". Senator Tim Scott is going to be there, too.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, that's great.\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: It's going to be great. Everybody's going to be there.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: He is basically piggybacking on my show.\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: It's like, let's take "Hannity" and do it at 1:00 p.m. tomorrow on FOX Business.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That will work. I like it.\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: Look, I got to -- I got to say this. This American Climate Corps, first of all it has to be unconstitutional. How can the president do this when Congress hasn't passed it?\par \par \uc2 But the other part of it is this, you talk about inflation, you talk about interest rates. You've got more spending coming from this president. You've got more spending coming on migrants.\par \par \uc2 That's why your inflation is going up. That's why you can't afford a house. That's why you can't find one on the market right now. All of this is related.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Let me go to the latest numbers.\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: He wants to separate it and you can't do that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So, the Feds passed on raising interest rates, even the last two months, inflation has gone on.\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: Yep.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK. Now, we have gas back to $4 a gallon, $100 a barrel for oil which means that in two months, gas prices are going to be $4.50 a gallon and maybe higher.\par \par \uc2 So, inflation has to go up. That means interest rates will have to go up yet again.\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: I mean, bad news is that it has already been ticking up again because oil has been going up again. And you're right. As that raises, then the Feds says, well, let's see, is the administration going to cut spending? Are they going to do anything to fight inflation?\par \par \uc2 They're not going to do anything. They just want to keep the money flowing. And so, the Feds in this spot where they raise interest rates. You are paying 9.5 percent for a new car that cost $50,000.\par \par \uc2 Can Middle America afford that? They can't because the president, for all he talks about with unions, all he talks about Middle America, middle out, bottom up, he does not care a whit about the average working American in this country. And I don't -- you don't take my word for it. Just look at the policy.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, add to that, the insanity they want you to change your gas stove. They want you to get rid of your air conditioner.\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: Right, right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They want all of these other appliances taken away from you. OK. Who's going to pay for all of that?\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: They want the bureaucrats to go shopping for you, and then they put it on your bill. If you can't afford it, they start handing out government cash and they put it on the taxpayers tab. But do you get it? Bidenomics, it's all borrowed.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: $33 trillion new debt.\par \par \uc2 BRENBERG: Yep, and it is going up. Until you get a new policy, until you get a new administration, you're not going to fix that problem, folks. It is a generational issue for your kids and grandkids. We've got to get a handle on it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: The Republicans in the House need to hold the line. They got to force a spending issue.\par \par \uc2 Brian Brenberg, we'll see you tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 All right. Coming up, Howard Stern says he's woke and he's proud of it. Reaction, Clay Travis straight ahead as we continue.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Howard Stern got famous by being offensive, okay. He was proud of it. But, now, Howard has been reborn as a woke social justice warrior.\par \par \uc2 Howard, what happened?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN AUDIO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HOWARD STERN, HOST, THE HOWARD STERN SHOW: I kind of take that as a compliment that I'm woke. I'll tell you how I feel about it. To me, the opposite of woke is being asleep. And if woke means I can't get behind Trump, which is what I think it means, or that I support people who want to be transgender or I'm for the vaccine, dude, call me woke as you (EXPLETIVE DELETED) want. I'm not for stupidity. I am woke (EXPLETIVE DELETED) and I love it.\par \par \uc2 (END AUDIO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Wow. Here now with reaction Outkick founder Clay Travis is with us.\par \par \uc2 You know, I admire him as a broadcaster and one of the things that was quintessential Howard in this was he took criticism and gave an honest answer. That defines his career, I give him credit for that.\par \par \uc2 I don't know what happened. The guy that I felt I listened to would have loved an iconoclastic, straight forward, hard-hitting guy like Trump. He would not be hiding in his closet afraid of COVID. You know, that's not the guy that I thought I knew.\par \par \uc2 CLAY TRAVIS, OUTKICK FOUNDER: It's well said, Sean. And, look, he is a radio legend and I both --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, talented.\par \par \uc2 TRAVIS: -- do radio daily and we understand what that requires.\par \par \uc2 But the Howard Stern today would, as you said, hate, absolutely hate the Howard Stern of 25 years ago and vice-versa. I think he is an emblematic example, Sean, of what happens when people got broken by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and COVID, the combination of the two of them.\par \par \uc2 This guy didn't leave his house for two and a half years. He just left his house to get his COVID booster shot. By the way, how many people in your audience are going to get their COVID booster shot at any point? How many people are going to get your six-month -- like the CDC said, the COVID shot.\par \par \uc2 You know, part of Howard Stern's popularity, Sean, was his rebellion against the status quo. Now he has become a zealous advocate of the status quo and of authority. He's become the opposite of what he used to be.\par \par \uc2 You saw when he went after the Congressman Boebert, too, for the dress that she wore. He said it was too much. This is a guy that used to have lesbians having sex on the radio live on the air, and now, he's -- now he's grabbing his pearls and fainting on the couch because an attractive woman wears a sexy dress?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You raise a good point. He is the guy that said lesbians equal ratings. He did say that.\par \par \uc2 TRAVIS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Look, it's fine. Everybody has a chance to evolve. He wants to get as many shots as he wants. I believe in freedom.\par \par \uc2 I don't think anybody is against personal choices of adults, but we don't want our kids indoctrinated by teachers at younger and younger ages, into transgenderism, and gender identity. I just prefer reading, writing, math, science, computers. You know, stick to the basics.\par \par \uc2 TRAVIS: Yeah, and here is what I would say, Sean. When he defined woke, to me woke means identity politics over everything. You don't care about anything other than who you vote for, what your race is and what your gender is. That's how woke ideology has taken over in America.\par \par \uc2 I don't think Howard understands it. I think he's lost. I think he stopped being a rebel. And, frankly, I think his show is boring which is the ultimate indictment of everything.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's going to be -- I think he's proud of it. He's being honest. That I can applaud and appreciate. I do. That has defined him his whole career.\par \par \uc2 But I kind of like the other guy a lot better that was irreverent, over the top, politically incorrect.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But, you know, we have not been -- he gets paid more money, almost probably second to God when it comes to, you know, entertainment.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, Clay, great to see you, my friend. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 All right. Unfortunately, that's all the time we have left.\par \par \uc2 Quick reminder, live studio audience show. We're having a great time?\par \par \uc2 (CHEERS)\par \par \uc2 Come and join us. Tickets are free, Hannity.com. We have in-studio guests, Tomi Lahren, Jimmy Failla, and special guests.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, let not your heart be troubled. Why? Greg Gutfeld is standing by and he will put a smile on your face. Thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020230921ej9k00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Five Americans Freed In Prisoner Swap With Iran; Lawmakers Scramble To Finalize Funding Deal; Hunter Biden Suing IRS Over Tax Disclosures; Negotiators Resume Talks As Automakers Strike Continues; Trump Criticizes DeSantis Heartbeat Abortion Bill; Candidates Debate 15-Week Limit; Haley: Focus On Late Term Abortions; Global Impact Beyond Fossil Fuels; Schumer Drops Senator Attire Guidelines; Senate Passes New Dress Code Allowing Senator \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  to Dress Less Formally; Video Emerges Of Teen Driver Hitting And Killing Bike Rider; Owner And Tenant Of Daycare Facility Arrested For Exposing Children To Fentanyl Leading To One-Year-Old's Death; Biden Administration Criticizes For Releasing $6 Billion In Frozen Funds To Iranian Republican In Exchange For Five American Prisoners; Former President Trump Criticizes Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  For Signing State Abortion Bill\b0\par\par\uc2 John Roberts, Peter Doocy, Chad Pergram, Grady Trimble, David  Spunt, Rich Edson, Bret Baier, Mark Meredith, Alexis McAdams, CB Cotton,  Brit Hume, Juan Williams, Ben Domenech \par \uc2 7,880 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 September 2023\par \uc2 Fox News: Special Report with Brett Baier\par \uc2 FNSPBB\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: I'm lactose intolerant, Judge. Just looking at this gives me diarrhea.\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL LEGAL ANALYST: Yes, but you know what, the truth is that there's more than cheese in that.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Will it be explosives?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: It will be explosive.\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: All right, good luck out there with the traffic. That's it for us. Have a great night everybody.\par \par \uc2 JOHN ROBERTS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Good evening and welcome back to Washington. I'm John Roberts. Bret Baier will join us from Saudi Arabia a little bit later on.\par \par \uc2 But breaking tonight, five Americans are on their way home this evening after being released from custody in Iran. It is part of a prisoner swap with that country, one that includes the release of $6 billion of frozen Iranian assets that has led to fierce criticism of the deal.\par \par \uc2 White House correspondent Peter Doocy starts us off tonight from 1600 Pennsylvania. Good evening, Peter.\par \par \uc2 PETER DOOCY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: John, good evening. When these freed hostages land overnight in the D.C. area, they will be immediately offered help from the Defense Department at adjusting to life on the outside. And so far, we haven't heard anybody say anything but positive things that Americans are heading home. But there are a lot of complaints about the deal to get them here.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 MIKE POMPEO\uc2 , FORMER SECRETARY OF STATE: This is a ransom payment of about $6 billion, about a billion bucks per prisoner.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voice over): President Biden says, today, five innocent Americans who were imprisoned in Iran are finally coming home after many months of difficult and principled American diplomacy.\par \par \uc2 American Siamak Namazi held since 2015 says, I am dying to find out what gadgets now exist. When I was taken hostage, the iPhone 6s had just come out. You cannot imagine what an eight-year itch feels like.\par \par \uc2 The returning Americans have already spoken to President Biden and Secretary of State Blinken.\par \par \uc2 ANTONY BLINKEN\uc2 , U.S. SECRETARY OF STATE: I can tell you that it was for them, for me, an emotional conversation.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voice over): To get the five Americans home, President Biden worked to unfreeze $6 billion in Iranian funds that are only supposed to be used to buy food or medicine.\par \par \uc2 BLINKEN: We have the means and mechanisms to make sure that that happens.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voice over): That leads to new concerns about an easy workaround in Tehran.\par \par \uc2 REP. MIKE WALTZ (R-FL): That frees up 6 billion of Iranian money for terrorism, for supporting Russia and everything else. I worry that this is really greasing the skids to back into a new nuclear deal.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voice over): The five Iranians freed from U.S. jails were charged with offenses ranging from failing to register as a foreign agent to buying parts that could be used in missiles, the deal making between D.C. and Tehran appears to be limited to hostages. For now, no plans to try to reenter the Iran nuclear deal.\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY, PRESS SECRETARY, PENTAGON: It would be great if we could diplomatically get to a place where we were back in 2015. And I'm not saying that diplomacy is completely off the table. It's just not the focus right now.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (on camera): President Biden is already in New York City for the \uc2 United Nations General Assembly\uc2  but has no public events on his schedule today, including at the \uc2 United Nations General Assembly\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He did just arrived at his first meetings of the day, though, it's a pair of fundraisers, including one that is being billed as Broadway for Biden, John.\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: But we will be watching that big speech tomorrow before the General Assembly. Peter Doocy for us at the White House tonight. Peter, thank you.\par \par \uc2 We are now just a week and a half away from a potential partial shutdown of the federal government if Republicans and Democrats cannot agree to legislation to keep offices open and services running.\par \par \uc2 GOP members who control the House are said to be getting jittery at the prospect of being blamed for another negotiating failure. Our Senior Congressional Correspondent Chad Pergram is on Capitol Hill tonight. Chad, a lot going on there.\par \par \uc2 CHAD PERGRAM, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONGRESSIONAL CORRESPONDENT: John, good evening. Lawmakers are no closer to avoiding a shutdown. GOP South Dakota Representative \uc2 Dusty Johnson\uc2  and other centrist Republicans crafted a bill to fund the government for a month and enhance border security. But the plan lacks the votes.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 REP. DUSTY JOHNSON (R-SD): Nothing happens easily around here. The reality is that we can't shut down government and we must secure the border.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): The plan met a frosty reception from Democrats.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 CHUCK SCHUMER\uc2  (D-NY): Last night's proposal in the House can be boiled down to two words, slapdash, reckless. slapdash because it's not a serious proposal for avoiding a shutdown.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): The house has only approved one spending bill this year. House Speaker Kevin McCarthy tried to get his members to pass spending bills since July. That failure means the House loses leverage to the Senate.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM: Is that part of the idea to demonstrate to them that they're going to get jammed by the Senate if they don't move something over here and strengthen your position?\par \par \uc2 REP. KEVIN MCCARTHY (R-CA): The best way this system works is we pass our individual bills. Unfortunately, I have some members denying those come up. We're going to keep working through that.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): McCarthy said a government shutdown impedes impeachment. GOP Indiana Representative Victoria Spartz is retiring but she called McCarthy, "weak". McCarthy rebuked Spartz.\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY: You know, one thing I've learned in life, anybody who criticize you has never worked harder than you. I mean, if Victoria is concerned about fighting stronger, I wish she would run again and not quit.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (on camera): A cocktail of Democrats and GOP members could renew old funding on a temporary basis to avert a shutdown. But that could draw the ire of the right. McCarthy says he's not worried that opponents could try to remove him as speaker, John.\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: A lot of rhetoric being thrown there on Capitol Hill. Chad Pergram for us tonight. Chad, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is suing the \uc2 IRS\uc2  over the release of his tax records. The president's son is facing the prospect of being charged for tax crimes and other violations relating to his business affairs. Correspondent David Spunt is at the Justice Department tonight and has the latest from there for us. Good evening, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SPUNT, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: Hi, John. Good evening. \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is going on the offense just days after he was indicted on three felony counts for owning a gun back in 2018.\par \par \uc2 This suit specifically 