hat's a problem that we face as a nation. We need to dig into some of the most important, consequential issues facing the American people and not have a food fight on the stage.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY(on camera): You know, one of the things that stood out to me is a point that I often make, that on average, the average American household is paying nearly $10,000 more for the same items that they were paying when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  left office on January 20th of 2021.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: You're a hundred percent right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So, my point is, and then you have 61 percent of Americans living paycheck to paycheck. Then, you have $54,000 average American debt. How do you climb out from under that or bear necessities? People throwing it on their credit card. That is real suffering. And a lot of it's self-induced because of Biden's energy and economic policy?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Absolutely. Number one, we have to know that energy security is national security, but it's also one of the parts of my 10 million new jobs made in America plan where we could have three million new jobs in the energy sector. America would be the leading country on earth if we had a president who believed in our national energy resources.\par \par \uc2 If we had that, we would rise to the top because we have more energy when you add oil, gas, and coal. Listen, Africa, India are going to continue to see the carbon footprint explode because they have tons and tons of people living in poverty. Why not use our resources to meet their needs and create high paying --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Gas is going back up to $4.00 a gallon.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: 11-month high.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK. 11-month high and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in his years as president, it never went above $3.00 a gallon, never reached $3.00 a gallon.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: In December of 2020, in South Carolina, the gas price was $1.99.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Those are called the good old days, right?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: The good old days. We can get them back, though.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You're right.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: We have to have a president believes in our own energy resources.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK, so you talked about firing Director Wray.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You talked about \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  and getting rid of him, you said we'll get rid of no \uc2 IRS\uc2  agents, we'll hire them for the border.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK, now do you believe that our Department of Justice and our \uc2 FBI\uc2  have been politicized and weaponized, what are the main reasons you would fire them?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: 100 percent they have been weaponized. We know now that Lady Justice no longer can find the blindfold. When you watch what this Department of Justice has done against political opponents, you would consider that unethical and immoral. When you think about what it's done to parents just showing up and saying, I want my child educated, not indoctrinated; you would call this Department of Justice immoral.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Right.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: When you see a SWAT team show up at a pro-life activist's home with guns drawn? You'd call that immoral, irresponsible, and unacceptable. What we know as Americans, we must trust our Department of Justice. It is un- American and unacceptable to see what \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , and \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  has done to the DOJ, and most importantly to the American people's confidence in the Department of Justice.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, I won't admit publicly that when we had a throwing contest at the town hall that you threw further than me. That's not, that's just not going to come out of my mouth.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Absolutely not.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We'll keep it a secret. Senator, always good to see you, my friend.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Thank you. Appreciate it. All right, now, of course, Senator Scott wasn't the only candidate from the great state of South Carolina on the stage tonight. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 NIKKI HALEY (R), PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: But we've got to get these kids reading. If a child can't read by third grade, they're four times less likely to graduate high school. So, we need to make sure we bring in reading remediation all over this country. We need transparency in the classroom because parents should never have to wonder what's being said or taught to their children in the classroom. Parents need to be deciding which schools their kids go to because they know best and let's put vocational classes back into the high schools.\par \par \uc2 Let's teach our kids to build things again. When we do that and we allow that innovation, that's when it will get back. And yes, I will always say I'm going to fight for girls all day long because strong girls become strong women. Strong women become strong leaders. And biological boys don't belong in the locker rooms of any of our girls.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How are you? All right, joining us now, former South Carolina Governor Nikki Haley is with us. Governor, great to see you. How are you? Did you have fun out there tonight?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: I did have fun. It was great.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: One thing that stood out in my mind is what a difference between the policies of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and everybody on that stage, one thing you had in common. There were a couple of things that you did in this debate that really interested me. Is, is -- you kind of went against some of the party's main positions on the issue of abortion. Well, first of all, you said women, you want something done, so you really don't trust men to do the job. Is that true? I'm kidding.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: No.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's a joke. That was a famous \uc2 Margaret Thatcher\uc2  quote. That was well said. But 