they have --\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes, yes. Go to Vegas.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Vegas has a better -- a better Eiffel Tower.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Right.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: And (INAUDIBLE).\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Right by the slots.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes, you can get the --\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: The one slot.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: There the songs, anything.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: OK, everyone to Vegas. "ONE MORE THING" is up next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: It's time now for "ONE MORE THING" and Jessica goes first.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: All right, I absolutely love this story. So, two adopted siblings just found out by DNA testing that they were actually siblings by blood. 19-year-old Victoria was just a baby when Angela and Dennis adopted her into their family. They already had one biological son and had adopted another named Frank a year and a half before. They lived under the same roof for 20 years and then they went on \uc2 ancestry.com\uc2  to figure out where they came from. Their parents completely unaware of the fact that they were actually siblings.\par \par \uc2 You think it's fake?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No, I'm just hoping that nothing happened before that.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Oh, you're so perverted.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No, that's the first thing that I thought. Like, how old are they?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: That's horrible.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No, I'm just --\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I'm happy for them.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I don't understand --\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: We all should be.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: -- but I'm happy for them.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Like -- whatever. OK, I go next. So, one dedicated basketball fan took his love for the game to the next level this past weekend. At the annual best of all Hall of Fame induction ceremony --\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh, dear.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: -- he got a tattoo of the logo for the 2023 ceremony. But he wasn't done there. He then proceeded to 