er is dropping today. You can preorder it now. It's an amazing story of mercy and forgiveness. And shows a father's love and how a father and a son created a national holiday tradition we continue to do.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Raymond.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: It's pre-ordered now.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Thank you. Exciting. Thank you, Raymond. All right. Why is \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  hiding, what is she hiding about the real security failures ahead of January 6? Congressman Barry Loudermilk, he got his hands on some new information and is going to share it with us in moments.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: The January 6th insurrection shook our republic to the core. For many in the Congress and across our country, the physical, psychological, and emotional scars are still raw.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So raw that Democrats may want to keep key information about security failures before January 6th secret. The congressman charged with investigating the J6 committee's work says they did not adequately preserve documents, data, or even communications with the Biden White House.\par \par \uc2 So, what are they hiding? Joining me now is that congressman, Barry Loudermilk of Georgia. Congressman, what's the biggest piece of information, the type of information you know they have not turned over to you, or that they lost?\par \par \uc2 CONG. BARRY LOUDERMILK (R-GA): Well, Laura, there's several pieces of information that we have finally identified that we don't have. One is the videotapes of all the depositions and of the interviews that they did. We know they did videotapes, that's standard practice, and they used some of those videotapes in their Hollywood production hearings.\par \par \uc2 And so, that, in itself, requires preservation. But there's also documents that we have found, references to documents, that they return to the White House and the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , but they redacted what those documents were.\par \par \uc2 And so, even though they were supposed to preserve all the information that they used during the entirety of the select committee, they purposely sent those away. We're asking for them.\par \par \uc2 But there's also nothing about the security failures at the Capitol on January 6th. And that's one of the key elements of our investigation is where was the security failure, what happened? And how can we fix it? In the future it looked, security should not be political. But we cannot find any documentation regarding the blue team, which was tasked with investigating the security failure.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I mean, I think you should ask the question also. I mean, this was a, you know, what? Three or four dozen people who actually got violent, right? Everyone else was kind of just milling around, walking around. But there was a core group of people who, you know, caused real trouble.\par \par \uc2 But what if it were someone else? I mean, what if these were actual terrorists? What if this was, you know, a band of people who had crossed the border and were really wanting to cause real trouble? Maybe true insurrectionists, not just rioters who were mad about the election.\par \par \uc2 LOUDERMILK: Right. And I don't know that we are prepared in that scenario at this point, because we haven't adequately addressed the intelligence failure. We know that there was actionable intelligence. We know the executive branch, the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , CIA, and others knew of the intelligence that there was going to be this group of folks to make an attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 However, the intelligence never made it to the chief of police, even though it made it to the intelligence division. So, we're trying to figure out, was it suppressed intentionally? Was it incompetence? Either way, there's a cover-up. But this blue team was supposed to be working on it.\par \par \uc2 The interesting thing is, I'm trying to figure out, are the documents missing or did they never create any? Because if you're going to investigate the \uc2 Capitol Police\uc2  and the security failure, you also have to investigate the politicians and the offices that have oversight, which would be the Speaker's Office and the Committee on House Administration.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Bingo.\par \par \uc2 LOUDERMILK: But here's the thing --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Congressman, we want --\par \par \uc2 LOUDERMILK: -- the chair --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We want Pelosi's information, Congressman. We're going to keep track of this. Sorry we had to cut this a little short, but there are a lot of questions out there that we still have, that's for sure. That's it for us tonight. Jesse Watters takes it from here.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020230810ej8900001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 FBI\uc2  Fatally Shoots Man Who Allegedly Threatened \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ; House GOP Releases Records On Hunter Biden Business Deals; \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  Denies Talking Business With Son; GOP Push To Withhold Homeland Security Money; U.S. Blamed For Increased Tensions With Taiwan; Hawaii Under State Of Emergency; Hurricane Dora Winds Fanning Flames; Christie Takes Aim At Party Rivals; Republican Presidential Candidate \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  Interviewed On Campaigning In New Hampshire, U.S. Support For Ukraine Against Russia, And His Criticisms Of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ; U.S. And Other Nations Working