t of people would make more sense. Sounded like she said population, but she meant pollution.\par \par \uc2 OK, let's get to your Winners and Losers, Marie. We'll start with you.\par \par \uc2 HARF: So winner, President Biden's fundraising operation. A record breaking for a Democrat at this point in the race, $72 million, over more than twice as much as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  raised. For all of those commentators and even some Democrats who were worried about enthusiasm for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , this showed there is a ton of enthusiasm, including among small dollar donors.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: I've got to have you, quick --\par \par \uc2 HARF: My loser is Senator Tommy Tuberville. I mentioned it earlier. He is holding military promotions for political reasons.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Lightning round. Phil?\par \par \uc2 WEGMANN: My loser is Ukrainian President Zelenskyy who earned a rare rebuke for grumbling that \uc2 NATO\uc2  wasn't moving fast enough. My winner is the Indy film house behind the surprising blockbuster "Sound of Freedom." It's got good reviews and it's raised a ton of money. Plus, conservatives finally feel they have got a hit of their own.\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: My winner is Senator Tommy Tuberville. He's had to fight not only Biden and the Democrats but some of his own party to defend the sanctity of human life and keep the military from being woke. Loser, \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  who had that awful testimony this week.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: OK, panel, thank you very much. You got it in under the wire.\par \par \uc2 It's Friday. Time for "Notable Quotables."\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Ukraine will not weaken.\par \par \uc2 VOLODYMYR ZELENSKYY, UKRAINIAN PRESIDENT: You spend this money for our lives.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: They treat people differently based upon their political beliefs.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: If you were to look into your crystal ball, sitting where you are sitting right now, where does it all go?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: We want to determine whether or not \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is compromised, and in the end, I would predict that there will be criminal referrals.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Are you protecting the Bidens?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Absolutely not.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: They don't know who it is. Clearly the Secret Service is failing at their job.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: House Republicans weren't blown away, pun intended.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: A.I. is kind of a fancy thing. First of all, it's two letters. It means artificial intelligence.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: \uc2 NATO\uc2  takes, all of us take Article Five literally. Going into \uc2 NATO\uc2  territory means all are going to work together.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: There's a lot of tensions in the relationship.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It's so frustrating to us for this to happen to the "Barbie" movie.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We are being victimized by a very greedy entity.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Getting overheated like that, you start to get tired, irritable, angry, you are not thinking clearly.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: We never had mud like this. And our cellar is turned upside down.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: We're not even sure where he is and what relationship he has. If I were he, I would be careful what I ate.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: OK, Monday on SPECIAL REPORT, our "Common Ground" segment features West Virginia Democratic Senator Joe Manchin and former Utah Republican Governor \uc2 Jon Huntsman\uc2 . They are going to talk about their work with the group No Labels.\par \par \uc2 Please join me for FOX NEWS SUNDAY. My guests will be National Security Spokesman John Kirby from the White House and Arkansas Senator Tom Cotton, himself a veteran. We are going to talk about these battles over defense spends. It's