oice over): House Speaker Kevin McCarthy took up the mantle of social conservative.\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY: We're watching the deterring of our -- of our military training. I think it harms us with our adversaries.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): There's a plan to prevent the Pentagon from paying for hormone treatment or gender altering surgeries.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: This amendment will likely lead to service members leaving the military.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): There's also a proposal to end diversity programs in the armed services.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The American people I talked to back home don't want a weak military. They don't want to work military. They don't want rainbow propaganda on bases.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): Inclusion of such white hot issues could make it hard to pass the bill. Democrats say it's a distraction.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: These amendments are disgusting. It's another example of the Republican Party not interested in governing for all the American people.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): The most controversial issue, an amendment to overturn the Pentagon policy which allows service members to travel out of state for abortions. But even some Republicans believe that restriction goes too far.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Well, this really feels like meddling with women who are traveling out of state, women who are willing take a bullet for their country app. I hope we don't drop the ball.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (on camera): Now, the House just approved amendments, ending the Helsinki Pentagon's abortion policy and barring the use of the military's health program for transgender treatment.\par \par \uc2 Also, Senator Tommy Tuberville talked today with defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  about his blockade on military promotions over abortion. And President Biden says it's, "Irresponsible and jeopardizing U.S. security". Gillian.\par \p