ass through this Congress. The 20-week bill that we worked on, the Pain-Capable bill, never saw the light of day.\par \par \uc2 As a matter of fact, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and the Democrats won`t even allow any pro-life legislation. Thirty weeks could not pass this Congress today. That means we have work to do to create the culture.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Do you worry then, Senator, that six weeks is too much? Do you worry that six weeks is too much, and that that might hurt Republicans` chances?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Well, on the federal level, here`s what we know.\par \par \uc2 We want states to do the very best they can to create that culture I just discussed earlier. I`m 100 percent pro-life.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Right.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: I have got a 100 percent pro-life voting record.\par \par \uc2 For us to get it done on the federal level, we`re going to have to convince people. And, today, we haven`t convinced enough Americans even for a 15- week limit. So, every other conversation outside of getting the number from 39 or 40 weeks down to 15 is inconsequential if we can`t win it in the Senate or the House right now.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: So, when you look at where this whole abortion thing stands, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the former vice president, has said on this Iowa move to make it six weeks: "I`m pro-life. I don`t apologize for it."\par \par \uc2 He says: "I just have heard so many stories over the years of courageous women and families who were told that their unborn child would not go to term or would not survive, and they had a healthy pregnancy and a healthy delivery."\par \par \uc2 He is going so far as to say, as you`re probably familiar, that women should carry even difficult pregnancies to term. What do you think of that?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Well, I think the answer to your question is a question of viability.\par \par \uc2 And for those who -- that are not viable, that`s the question that I think Mike was answering. He and I have very different opinions on that topic. I think the one thing I would consistently say is that, if we can consistently protect the culture of life, focus our attention as a nation and as a party on making sure that we have a limit that stops the radical left from pushing abortion on demand for any reason whatsoever...\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: ... we find ourselves where three out of four Americans actually agree with us.\par \par \uc2 We need to take that as momentum to be successful.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: So, I`m sorry, Senator. I just -- I apologize.\par \par \uc2 I just want to be super clear on this.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: As I see it so far, Senator, the vice president, the former vice president, is the only major candidate who supports a federal ban on abortion at six weeks.\par \par \uc2 That is what Iowa Governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  is recommending. Are you saying that that`s too extreme for you?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Well, what I said, and I will continue to say, is that the 15-week limit is where we start the conversation. Until we win the hearts and minds of the American people, we cannot get that through Congress.\par \par \uc2 I`m looking from the perspective, as president of the United States, I would sign the most conservative pro-life legislation we can get through Congress. And, today, that`s not even a 30-week. So having the hypotheticals that we`re talking about is something that I know we can`t get done, because, today, we can`t get the 20-week done, we can`t get the 15-week done.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Got it.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: And so I`m going to continue to work as president of the United States to create the culture where at least the 15-week limit is something we are able to accomplish.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: I mentioned the governor, \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And she`s in a dust-up not of her own making, but \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and. Her she says she has to be impartial in this race. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was offended by that, kind of picked a fight with her that she`s ungrateful because he had supported her and helped make her governor.\par \par \uc2 I just want your thoughts on that.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Well, Governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  is one of the most remarkable individuals in the country, and she is one of the strongest governors her state and any state has ever seen.\par \par \uc2 This is the woman who passed pro-school choice legislation for the first time in the history of her state. She has provided a $7,500 scholarship for kids within 300 percent of poverty. What that means, Neil, as the guy who`s championed the cause of pro -- being school choice, pro-school choice, what that means is that we now have the poorest kids in her state having the same opportunities as the richest kids in her state.\par \par \uc2 She`s also worked on starting -- jump-starting one of the strongest economies during the most difficult times in the state. I am thankful that, today, she`s agnostic about which candidate should be president of the United States. I look forward to winning her support.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: It`s very early in the race, and we -- you have been reminding me of that in past interviews, Senator.\par \par \uc2 But one poll that I found interesting on you is that you`re rapidly rising to be everyone`s favorite number two. In fact, you have doubled in that sentiment in polls that have been taken around the country.\par \par \uc2 Are you interested or would you be interested, should you fail to get the nomination, to be the runner-up, to be the guy running with the person who wins?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yes, well, Neil, the one thing -- I never correct you on TV because you`re so good at what you do, but I don`t think everybody wants me to be the number two.\par \par \uc2 There are some who want me to be the number one. And so I`m going to continue to run this race for one objective. It`s to be the president of the United States. I did not enter this race to come in second place. Second place is the first loser.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: From my perspective, the only way to run for president is to do it 100 percent of the time.\par \par \uc2 And all we`re focused on is making sure that the next generation of stories of the American dream make mine pale in comparison. We are the city on the hill, Neil, and we must remain the beacon in the midst of the storm.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Would you support any one of your colleagues if you don`t get that nomination for president, all the way up to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Here`s what I can tell you. I will be the nominee for the great opportunity party. And I will stop there.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Got it.\par \par \uc2 Is it really true as well -- I looked in your background -- that you really love the movie "Rocky III"? Tell me that is not true.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Well, listen, I`m going to bust you up, sucker.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: That`s what Mr. T said to Rocky.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: So, here`s what we know.\par \par \uc2 And, of course, the response to that, of course, was Neil: "Go for it."\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Got it.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: And so I would just say, let`s go. I love "Rocky III."\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, there we go. I pity the fool who thinks otherwise.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: But, Senator, thank you.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: I pity the fool!\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Oh, that`s pretty good. That`s very good.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: God bless you.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, Senator Tim Scott, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, Inc.  Copyright CQ-2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All materials herein are  protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced,  distributed, transmitted, displayed, pub